1
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,320
Today is the day of the semifinal game.

2
00:00:15,590 --> 00:00:17,760
Except for Ji Hoo and me,

3
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:20,990
no one got eliminated
and made it back into the competition.

4
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:24,560
We were the only two people
who experienced the Revival Match.

5
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,360
Our determination is on another level.

6
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:28,670
I'm ready to draw
my Crescent Moon Blade...

7
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:31,500
and wield it against these people
like Guan Yu.

8
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,740
Today's weather is amazing.

9
00:00:40,910 --> 00:00:42,580
Before I knew it,

10
00:00:42,580 --> 00:00:44,820
I made it to the semifinal match.

11
00:00:45,050 --> 00:00:46,620
There are eight of us now.

12
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:49,750
A large group of players made it
to the semifinal match.

13
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,560
I wanted my team to take the lead...

14
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:53,960
and earn the right to advance
to the final match.

15
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:57,130
I've been aiming for that in my head.

16
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:05,470
I made it this far thanks to my team.

17
00:01:05,470 --> 00:01:09,310
I made it back into the game
by showing everyone what I was made of...

18
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:11,210
during the do-or-die Deathmatch.

19
00:01:11,210 --> 00:01:13,810
I wanted to play the semifinal match
on my own.

20
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:16,210
That's what I had in mind before the game.

21
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:19,320
So this is the semifinal match.
Will we be playing...

22
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:20,490
individually?

23
00:01:20,490 --> 00:01:21,590
Probably.

24
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:23,590
No more headaches then.

25
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:25,020
Headaches?

26
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:27,090
We'll be at a disadvantage
if it's a team match.

27
00:01:27,160 --> 00:01:30,060
- Why?
- Seong Beom and Jin Ho will team up.

28
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,000
It'd be nice if they split up.

29
00:01:32,260 --> 00:01:33,360
- Seong Beom and Jin Ho?
- Yes.

30
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:34,970
That's a dangerous duo.

31
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,970
Seong Beom and Jin Ho.

32
00:01:38,970 --> 00:01:41,040
If I can,
I'd love to see them get eliminated.

33
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,240
The players I see
as big threats would be...

34
00:01:43,240 --> 00:01:46,280
Naturally, they're Jin Ho and Seong Beom.

35
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:49,480
I also have my eyes on Seung Yong.

36
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,990
The weather is great today.

37
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:00,530
Even if I have to...

38
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,960
be attacked by the majority again
like yesterday,

39
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:05,500
I'll fight to the very end.

40
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,400
Seung Yong helped me a lot yesterday.

41
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:11,470
So I want to do my best,
so both of us can survive today.

42
00:02:11,470 --> 00:02:13,840
"I need to be on my toes starting today."

43
00:02:14,310 --> 00:02:17,210
"This is the moment
I've been playing for."

44
00:02:17,210 --> 00:02:18,240
That crossed my mind.

45
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:20,550
Please gather in the main hall.

46
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:21,710
My gosh.

47
00:02:22,580 --> 00:02:24,920
- Race? Is it a race or what?
- My gosh.

48
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,050
- What race?
- L and R?

49
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:27,050
- What's this?
- Gosh.

50
00:02:27,050 --> 00:02:28,050
(Surprised)

51
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:30,590
They stand for left and right.

52
00:02:31,520 --> 00:02:32,960
- I see cars. This is a race.
- How interesting.

53
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,090
- What?
- This looks fun.

54
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,630
The car race looks fun.

55
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,560
I wonder what kind of game
we're going to play.

56
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:43,230
It looks like
it's going to be a race or something.

57
00:02:43,370 --> 00:02:45,840
There are eight of us.
And say that it's a race.

58
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:49,540
In the end, it's going to be a game
of passing, chasing, and blocking.

59
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,540
That's what I'm expecting.

60
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:54,850
That made me think that
I might need to form an alliance.

61
00:02:55,050 --> 00:02:57,550
I didn't know what it was,
but it looked like a race.

62
00:02:57,550 --> 00:02:59,520
It seemed I was the only one
without a driver's license.

63
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:00,820
I thought that might be a disadvantage.

64
00:03:01,190 --> 00:03:04,490
I was hoping it would be a game
where we had to play individually...

65
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:08,030
or a game where the Minority Alliance
would have a shot...

66
00:03:08,030 --> 00:03:09,660
at beating the Majority Alliance.

67
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,600
Hello.

68
00:03:13,930 --> 00:03:16,600
I'd like to welcome the eight of you...

69
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,300
to the semifinal match of Bloody Game X.

70
00:03:20,170 --> 00:03:23,780
I will now explain the rules
of the semifinal match.

71
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:27,510
The semifinal match is the last hurdle
before the final match.

72
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,750
It will be an eight-player
individual competition.

73
00:03:30,180 --> 00:03:33,020
As for the number of players
advancing to the final match,

74
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,020
it's a total of four players.

75
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:38,890
For the final match of Bloody Game X,

76
00:03:38,890 --> 00:03:41,560
there will be three tournament rounds.

77
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:44,330
Round One of the final match...

78
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:46,760
will be between 1st and 4th place
of the semifinal match.

79
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:49,430
Round Two of the final match...

80
00:03:49,430 --> 00:03:53,500
will be between 2nd and 3rd place
of the semifinal match.

81
00:03:54,410 --> 00:03:57,540
The top two players
of the semifinal match...

82
00:03:57,540 --> 00:04:01,050
will earn the right to choose the game
for their final match respectively.

83
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:03,750
The winners of each round...

84
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:05,720
will advance to Round Three.

85
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:09,750
Then the final winner of Bloody Game X
will be decided.

86
00:04:11,390 --> 00:04:15,230
The game for the semifinal match
will be revealed now.

87
00:04:15,730 --> 00:04:17,630
The game for the semifinal match
is called...

88
00:04:17,630 --> 00:04:19,030
(Prediction Race)

89
00:04:19,030 --> 00:04:21,630
Prediction Race.

90
00:04:22,830 --> 00:04:26,070
Prediction Race will be
an eight-player individual competition.

91
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:28,410
In this game,
players must move their race car...

92
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:30,980
through placing bets and arranging cards.

93
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:34,110
Each player is given a race car...

94
00:04:34,110 --> 00:04:35,550
of a distinct color...

95
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:38,950
and a gear board
featuring left and right slots.

96
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:41,690
Before the game, players will make...

97
00:04:41,690 --> 00:04:45,260
a secret prediction of their final ranking
in the race.

98
00:04:45,690 --> 00:04:46,960
Once predictions are locked in,

99
00:04:46,960 --> 00:04:52,500
all players will receive 5 betting cards
from 1 to 5.

100
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,300
When a player uses up all five cards
in their hand,

101
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,800
they will immediately receive
a new set of five cards.

102
00:04:58,670 --> 00:04:59,870
During a round,
actions are taken in order.

103
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:02,010
Betting, playing movement cards,

104
00:05:02,240 --> 00:05:04,810
and moving race cars.

105
00:05:05,410 --> 00:05:07,350
This is the betting phase.

106
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:10,480
Movement cards come in a set of 12.

107
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:14,090
Three random movement cards...

108
00:05:14,490 --> 00:05:17,720
will be revealed in Areas A, B, C, and D.

109
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:20,190
Players must make a secret bet...

110
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:23,030
in the Voting Room
with one of their betting cards...

111
00:05:23,030 --> 00:05:24,700
on 1 of the 4 areas.

112
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:29,270
The player with the highest bid
in each area...

113
00:05:29,270 --> 00:05:30,500
will claim...

114
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:32,940
three movement cards from that area.

115
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:37,280
In the event of a tie for the highest bid,

116
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:40,510
the player with the second-highest bid
will claim the cards.

117
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:41,710
(Won)

118
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:44,550
The next stage is
playing the movement cards.

119
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:48,190
The successful bidders will go in order...

120
00:05:48,190 --> 00:05:50,150
to place the movement cards
either on their gear board...

121
00:05:50,150 --> 00:05:53,020
or other players' gear board.

122
00:05:53,620 --> 00:05:56,660
The players also have an option
to discard the cards...

123
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,200
if they wish.

124
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:01,870
Once the successful bidders
finish playing their movement cards,

125
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:04,300
the race cars will be moved.

126
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:08,070
Once both slots of the gear board
are filled,

127
00:06:08,370 --> 00:06:11,180
the race car will be moved
based on these following rules.

128
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:14,550
One. If the numbers on both sides
of the gear board match,

129
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:16,680
the race car moves straight
by that number of spaces.

130
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,750
Two. If the numbers don't match,

131
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:21,720
the race car moves straight
by the lower number,

132
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,750
followed by a diagonal move equal
to the difference of the two numbers...

133
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:25,390
toward the direction of the bigger number.

134
00:06:26,060 --> 00:06:29,630
Three. If there are a reverse card
and a number card on the gear board,

135
00:06:29,830 --> 00:06:31,860
the race car moves backward
by the number shown on the card.

136
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,000
If both slots contain reverse cards...

137
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,070
or if a reverse card is paired with zero,

138
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:39,940
the race car cannot move,
and the cards will be discarded.

139
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:42,770
The race cars move in order,

140
00:06:42,770 --> 00:06:45,380
beginning with the first player
for that round.

141
00:06:45,880 --> 00:06:48,250
If only one slot of the gear board
is filled,

142
00:06:48,450 --> 00:06:51,020
the player can keep the card
for the next round.

143
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:53,180
Here are the variables...

144
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:55,190
when moving the race cars.

145
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:59,660
One. When a race car bumps into the wall,
it overturns.

146
00:06:59,860 --> 00:07:02,960
The player can neither move the race car
nor put down cards on the gear board...

147
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:04,200
in the next round.

148
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,530
Two. If a race car collides
with another race car,

149
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:08,800
it goes on top of the car.

150
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,540
The car underneath cannot move.

151
00:07:12,270 --> 00:07:14,970
Three. If there's another race car
in front of a player's race car...

152
00:07:14,970 --> 00:07:16,140
at the starting line,

153
00:07:16,370 --> 00:07:18,840
the booster activated by the slipstream
allows the race car...

154
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:21,250
to start two spaces farther ahead.

155
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:24,520
The game can last up to 20 rounds.

156
00:07:24,780 --> 00:07:27,850
If a race car crosses the finish line,

157
00:07:27,950 --> 00:07:30,920
the game ends at the end of that round.

158
00:07:32,060 --> 00:07:35,490
As for the final rankings,
players with correct predictions...

159
00:07:35,490 --> 00:07:38,230
win top positions,
ordered by their race results.

160
00:07:38,230 --> 00:07:41,500
Next,
players with incorrect predictions...

161
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:44,000
are determined by their race results.

162
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,470
(Players with incorrect predictions)

163
00:07:45,470 --> 00:07:48,210
There's a hidden rule
in the semifinal match.

164
00:07:48,770 --> 00:07:50,980
It will be revealed to all players
before Round Six...

165
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,210
begins.

166
00:07:52,940 --> 00:07:56,050
Prediction Race will begin shortly.

167
00:07:56,850 --> 00:07:59,050
All players must submit...

168
00:07:59,050 --> 00:08:01,750
their predicted ranking
in the Voting Room.

169
00:08:02,550 --> 00:08:05,390
Winning first place
isn't the goal of this game.

170
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:08,530
Finishing the race in the predicted rank
is the most important.

171
00:08:08,530 --> 00:08:11,700
But if I reveal my predicted rank,

172
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,460
other players might try to get in my way.

173
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:15,800
I can never let them
find out my prediction.

174
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:17,400
I have to hide my intention.

175
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:20,270
Then I must finish in the position
I want at the end...

176
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:21,740
to win the game.

177
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:25,210
The key point of this game is that
I must conceal my prediction...

178
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:27,910
while trying to figure out
other players' predictions.

179
00:08:27,910 --> 00:08:31,250
I think the Majority Alliance
would have an upper hand in this game.

180
00:08:31,250 --> 00:08:34,220
So I'll have to take that approach
no matter what.

181
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:36,420
There's an advantageous approach
to win the game.

182
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,490
So why wouldn't I take it?

183
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:41,190
Actually, I like turn-based games.

184
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:43,560
A psychological element comes
into play in this game.

185
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:45,700
We don't know each other's predictions.

186
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,670
Will they go hard from the start?
Or will they take their time at first?

187
00:08:48,670 --> 00:08:50,800
This kind of decision could mislead them.

188
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:53,470
Well, since it's the type of game I like,

189
00:08:53,470 --> 00:08:56,140
I want to do well
and earn a chance to advance...

190
00:08:56,140 --> 00:08:57,240
to the final match.

191
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,540
You will have ten minutes...

192
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,910
to strategize before the game begins.

193
00:09:03,110 --> 00:09:04,720
Do we need an alliance for this game?

194
00:09:05,380 --> 00:09:08,020
Well, the thing is,

195
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:10,120
if my car ends up getting overturned,

196
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,760
I can't help anyone at that point.

197
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:13,320
By the nature of the game,

198
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:16,260
it's impossible to win
if you play this game on your own.

199
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:18,760
I thought forming an alliance was a must.

200
00:09:18,830 --> 00:09:21,200
Let's say we play as a team.
Then it's better if our turns are...

201
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,730
back-to-back.

202
00:09:22,730 --> 00:09:24,000
If our turns aren't consecutive,

203
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,970
other people might play their cards
and get in our way.

204
00:09:26,170 --> 00:09:27,340
How much money do you have?

205
00:09:27,610 --> 00:09:30,740
I have... I see.
I might have the most amount.

206
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:32,040
Right. You do...

207
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:33,880
- because...
- Seong Beom.

208
00:09:35,350 --> 00:09:37,150
Why don't we play individually this time?

209
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:39,120
- Oh, that's...
- You don't want to?

210
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:40,520
- I'm not sure.
- You're not sure?

211
00:09:41,390 --> 00:09:44,120
The silver lining was that
only four of us could advance.

212
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:47,730
Forming a five-player alliance
would be pointless.

213
00:09:47,790 --> 00:09:50,460
If the Majority Alliance
wins all the cards...

214
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:52,500
and dictates the flow of play,

215
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,400
there isn't much
the Minority Alliance can do.

216
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,270
This time around,
I'll keep my head in the game...

217
00:09:56,270 --> 00:09:57,940
and do my best to stop them...

218
00:09:58,240 --> 00:09:59,340
from forming the Majority Alliance.

219
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:01,710
What do you think about
strongly advocating independent play?

220
00:10:01,970 --> 00:10:06,180
But I don't know if they'll listen to me
and play individually.

221
00:10:06,380 --> 00:10:09,350
I doubt playing as a group
will be a catch-all solution.

222
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:11,950
But this game is
all about gathering information.

223
00:10:13,180 --> 00:10:14,250
That's true.

224
00:10:14,750 --> 00:10:16,290
What do you think? Should we team up?

225
00:10:16,290 --> 00:10:20,320
Would it be better if we were
to make predictions as a group?

226
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:22,660
In my opinion, it might be better
to share our predictions...

227
00:10:22,660 --> 00:10:24,760
and help each other with the cards...

228
00:10:24,760 --> 00:10:26,260
when we place bets.

229
00:10:26,260 --> 00:10:27,260
- Yes.
- What did you say?

230
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:29,200
Right.
So you mean we should play together.

231
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:31,440
And let's not forget that
you have the most funds right now.

232
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,670
- So you can decide the order.
- Yes.

233
00:10:33,940 --> 00:10:37,240
Since I had the largest amount
of personal funds,

234
00:10:37,810 --> 00:10:40,410
I was able to determine
the order of players.

235
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:43,150
With that in my favor, working
with other players from time to time...

236
00:10:43,150 --> 00:10:44,750
will be very important.

237
00:10:45,350 --> 00:10:47,420
It looks like
those guys don't want to team up.

238
00:10:47,850 --> 00:10:49,150
- What? They want to play individually?
- Yes.

239
00:10:50,420 --> 00:10:51,590
We can at least talk to them.

240
00:10:52,960 --> 00:10:55,160
Well, we'd like to talk to everyone.

241
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:58,100
Are you planning to form an alliance
for this game?

242
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,030
Or are you planning to play individually?

243
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:02,800
It depends on the situation.
We could be giving help or receiving it.

244
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:04,070
You could share your predictions,

245
00:11:04,070 --> 00:11:06,170
so you could help or receive help
from each other.

246
00:11:06,370 --> 00:11:08,340
To be honest,
that's the best-case scenario for me.

247
00:11:08,340 --> 00:11:10,710
Making predictions
without discussing them...

248
00:11:10,710 --> 00:11:12,440
would be best, right?

249
00:11:13,110 --> 00:11:15,010
- Because that will be a fair game?
- He has a point.

250
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:17,620
- Sung Joo, let's go out for a smoke.
- Sure.

251
00:11:17,750 --> 00:11:19,920
I'd pick playing without an alliance...

252
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:21,550
if I have to vote.

253
00:11:22,350 --> 00:11:24,120
Of course, I don't want to get eliminated.

254
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,490
I don't want
to ride anyone's coattails anymore.

255
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:28,160
I really don't want to do that.

256
00:11:28,430 --> 00:11:30,630
People are complex creatures.

257
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:34,130
I had to keep relying on these nobodies.

258
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:36,100
When I had to do that,
I got a reality check.

259
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:39,140
I came here, determined to survive
even if I had to be a cockroach.

260
00:11:40,070 --> 00:11:43,640
Since that's not who I am,
I'd hit the breaking point.

261
00:11:43,640 --> 00:11:44,740
The mental breaking point.

262
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:47,210
Honestly,
looking at the current situation...

263
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:49,080
and the remaining players,

264
00:11:49,510 --> 00:11:52,380
if I were to team up with Jin Ho
and Seong Beom, I wouldn't get eliminated.

265
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:56,020
But I really don't want to cave
into their alliance and join them.

266
00:11:57,120 --> 00:11:58,220
I don't want any ambiguity.

267
00:11:58,220 --> 00:12:00,760
- If we're going to play individually,
- We should do it properly?

268
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:03,560
we should gather everyone
and be in agreement before we begin.

269
00:12:03,990 --> 00:12:06,800
Or if you want to play as a team,
we should tell everyone about that.

270
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:08,170
So other players can keep that in mind.

271
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:09,600
If you say you'll play individually,

272
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,840
but it turns out
the two of you were playing together,

273
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:14,040
- that's annoying and pathetic.
- Right.

274
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:18,040
Let's say we don't form an alliance.

275
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,340
But it looks like I might end up...

276
00:12:19,340 --> 00:12:20,950
- working with players I don't want.
- Right.

277
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:24,480
Here's the only way
we can play as an alliance.

278
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:25,750
The four of us...

279
00:12:25,750 --> 00:12:29,150
can discuss strategies
and share our predictions. That's one way.

280
00:12:29,150 --> 00:12:30,960
- It might not work with four people.
- Two people?

281
00:12:30,960 --> 00:12:32,260
- Everything?
- Yes.

282
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:34,190
But here's something to think about.

283
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:37,360
Looking back, we won Money Challenges...

284
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,800
and helped our teammates survive.

285
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,230
Is there a reason
why we shouldn't work as a team for this?

286
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:43,170
- You have a point too.
- Yes.

287
00:12:44,470 --> 00:12:45,870
They're pushing for individual play...

288
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:47,300
in an important game like this...

289
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:49,870
because they know an alliance
would put them at a disadvantage.

290
00:12:50,410 --> 00:12:51,780
I'm not so happy to hear that.

291
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:55,310
He's just so annoying.

292
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,750
As for Seong Beom,
he always thinks he's the star.

293
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:01,090
If I wanted to team up with anyone,
it would be Jin Ho.

294
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,650
I don't have any interest
in teaming up with Seong Beom.

295
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:06,220
Let's talk about this quickly.

296
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,030
I think it's okay to team up
after placing bets.

297
00:13:08,030 --> 00:13:09,930
But we shouldn't team up before that.

298
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:11,530
I think that's fair.

299
00:13:11,530 --> 00:13:13,100
But why is that fair?

300
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:18,300
At the end of the day,
this survival game is played by people.

301
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:20,070
I made my moves strategically,

302
00:13:20,070 --> 00:13:21,740
always considering
who to keep by my side...

303
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:23,940
and who to face as my opponents
the whole time.

304
00:13:24,410 --> 00:13:26,640
I really did my best
during Money Challenges.

305
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:28,050
So my teammates didn't get eliminated.

306
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:31,020
If you say that doesn't matter now
and we should play individually,

307
00:13:31,320 --> 00:13:33,250
you're only arguing that
because that gives you an advantage.

308
00:13:33,250 --> 00:13:34,490
That's not being fair.

309
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:37,390
He had a valid point.

310
00:13:37,790 --> 00:13:39,920
But he didn't have to be so rude
when he spoke.

311
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:43,530
Despite that,
I still appealed to their emotional side.

312
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:47,060
I think I was successful in setting
the tone that a Majority Alliance...

313
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:49,900
would be bad for the game.

314
00:13:50,630 --> 00:13:53,140
His speech was artificial too.

315
00:13:53,340 --> 00:13:56,110
You can let things go, Seong Beom.
We all know that you're the man.

316
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:57,880
Both of you have a point.

317
00:13:57,880 --> 00:14:00,340
I think playing individually
for the entire game won't be possible.

318
00:14:00,610 --> 00:14:03,350
If anyone wants to form an alliance,
they should announce it to everyone.

319
00:14:03,710 --> 00:14:05,620
Secondly, even if there are alliances,

320
00:14:05,620 --> 00:14:07,550
it won't be
the majority versus the minority.

321
00:14:07,690 --> 00:14:09,620
There can be a cap
on the number of players like 2 or 3.

322
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:12,060
Once we set a cap on that,
their options will be limited.

323
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:15,430
Forming an alliance might not make
a huge difference.

324
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:18,330
We brought it up
because playing individually...

325
00:14:18,330 --> 00:14:20,460
would be more comfortable for people
without an alliance.

326
00:14:20,530 --> 00:14:23,100
In the end, we all need
some form of alliance to play this game.

327
00:14:23,270 --> 00:14:25,440
Once that became the nature of our game,
we have no choice...

328
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,070
but to lean toward forming alliances.

329
00:14:27,070 --> 00:14:29,040
And that's why people do form alliances.

330
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:31,010
Not to repeat what happened yesterday,

331
00:14:31,010 --> 00:14:33,410
I'm proposing that
we come up with a minimal set of rules.

332
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,680
That's completely doable,
and that's what I'm suggesting.

333
00:14:35,910 --> 00:14:38,650
I think two people would be enough.

334
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:40,550
I'd prefer to play individually.

335
00:14:40,950 --> 00:14:42,620
I know we won yesterday.

336
00:14:42,620 --> 00:14:44,220
But I got the feeling that...

337
00:14:44,220 --> 00:14:45,820
the alliance was much bigger
than the game needed.

338
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:47,630
- But...
- I want it to be a small alliance.

339
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:49,860
during Blind Auction,

340
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,160
Teams P1, R, and C made an alliance.

341
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,930
I'm not saying that what we did was fair.

342
00:14:53,930 --> 00:14:55,470
- How did you feel then?
- What?

343
00:14:55,470 --> 00:14:56,830
- How did you feel after that game?
- Even though we won,

344
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:57,840
- it was like yesterday.
- It didn't feel good?

345
00:14:57,840 --> 00:14:59,670
- Right. It was the same.
- Once we play, we should go all the way.

346
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:00,970
They always have excuses.

347
00:15:01,070 --> 00:15:04,110
They wanted to play individually
because they were at a disadvantage.

348
00:15:04,110 --> 00:15:05,580
But they left that out.

349
00:15:06,010 --> 00:15:08,380
"You guys are so awful
for playing as the majority."

350
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,410
"You're such cowards."

351
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:10,810
Saying things like that...

352
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,320
makes them bigger cowards.

353
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:15,120
He made it sound like
not making an alliance...

354
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:17,790
would leave me at a loss.

355
00:15:18,320 --> 00:15:21,660
Of course,
if we only considered winning and losing,

356
00:15:21,990 --> 00:15:23,890
his argument sounded reasonable.

357
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:26,060
But I'm sick of this dynamic.

358
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:27,630
I don't envy them.

359
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,570
There's going to be a bloodbath.

360
00:15:32,340 --> 00:15:34,310
This is Bloody Game now.

361
00:15:35,510 --> 00:15:38,980
For this game, having a lot of people
on your team won't necessarily...

362
00:15:38,980 --> 00:15:40,280
give you an advantage.

363
00:15:40,510 --> 00:15:42,550
At max,
it will be a three-player alliance.

364
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:45,150
If so, it's best to play with my team
since I've been playing with them...

365
00:15:45,150 --> 00:15:46,480
the whole season.

366
00:15:46,950 --> 00:15:48,820
It looks like Seong Beom, Hye Seon,

367
00:15:49,190 --> 00:15:50,650
- and I will form an alliance.
- Yes.

368
00:15:50,650 --> 00:15:52,190
It could be a 3-3-2 split.

369
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:53,890
Or it could be a 3-2-2-1 split.

370
00:15:53,890 --> 00:15:55,760
You guys can discuss that
and decide what you want to do.

371
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,160
- Yes. Sounds good.
- Should we do that?

372
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:58,460
- Yes. It doesn't matter.
- All right.

373
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,560
That should be all right.

374
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,630
Why? I'll play on my own.

375
00:16:01,630 --> 00:16:02,870
Playing solo? That's cool.

376
00:16:02,870 --> 00:16:04,000
I'll play on my own.

377
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:08,410
If we have to pick our team,
isn't it better that we team up?

378
00:16:08,940 --> 00:16:11,110
Or we could invite Keun Woo
and make it a three-player team.

379
00:16:11,240 --> 00:16:13,280
Given the history, Ji Hoo will team up...

380
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:15,410
with Seung Yong. Right?

381
00:16:15,410 --> 00:16:17,950
Let's say we play together. Keun Woo...

382
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:19,950
Having three people on the team
could be tough.

383
00:16:19,950 --> 00:16:21,920
Keun Woo, do you want to play with us?

384
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:23,520
- What?
- How about the three of us?

385
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:25,620
My gosh. What's the point? I'll just play.

386
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:26,960
Join us. Let's play together.

387
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:30,390
Or it could be a 3-2-1-1-1 split.

388
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:32,700
Yes. That's pretty cool.

389
00:16:32,930 --> 00:16:35,330
If we do that,
they won't know our dynamic.

390
00:16:35,330 --> 00:16:37,100
- Right.
- It might confuse them.

391
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,700
- It could be like we're going solo.
- Yes.

392
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:42,310
- I want to be on my own today.
- Okay.

393
00:16:42,510 --> 00:16:43,570
- On your own?
- Yes.

394
00:16:44,140 --> 00:16:46,380
I want to play the first round
on my own too.

395
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:48,550
Do you want to play individually?

396
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:49,980
Their alliance won't put us
at a disadvantage.

397
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,180
- Not necessarily.
- Right.

398
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:53,180
No one can figure out our predictions
or our dynamic.

399
00:16:53,950 --> 00:16:56,020
- Yes. Sure.
- I want to play on my own.

400
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:58,420
I made it this far
by relying on other people.

401
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:01,190
I just want to play on my own
before I leave the show.

402
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,990
- I'll stop piggybacking on other people.
- Exactly.

403
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:06,660
I think I have an upper hand here.

404
00:17:07,360 --> 00:17:09,530
As for Sung Joo, I can persuade him...

405
00:17:10,100 --> 00:17:11,800
to join me whenever I want.

406
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:14,270
As I expected, Team P3...

407
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:17,340
formed an alliance all on their own.

408
00:17:17,710 --> 00:17:19,010
By doing so,

409
00:17:19,610 --> 00:17:22,480
they have shut down any possibilities
to other alliances...

410
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,650
even before the game.

411
00:17:24,280 --> 00:17:26,420
Here's what we discussed.

412
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,450
We don't want to form an alliance out
in the open from the get-go.

413
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:30,850
They're openly working together.

414
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:34,120
In my opinion,
it might actually backfire...

415
00:17:34,120 --> 00:17:37,390
because they can easily become targets.

416
00:17:37,590 --> 00:17:38,830
- I see.
- Okay.

417
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:42,370
If you want to go after anyone,

418
00:17:43,130 --> 00:17:45,000
I think going after them makes more sense.

419
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,810
- We have to see the order of turns first.
- Right.

420
00:17:49,370 --> 00:17:51,780
Hye Seon has the largest amount
of personal funds.

421
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:56,350
Come to the Voting Room and
decide the order of turns for the players.

422
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:00,450
They might struggle
to understand the game.

423
00:18:00,550 --> 00:18:01,590
I put them first.

424
00:18:02,050 --> 00:18:04,150
I see. I think
the order you have looks pretty good.

425
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:07,260
I think switching the 1st and 3rd players
could be better.

426
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:08,330
The 1st and 3rd players?

427
00:18:08,330 --> 00:18:10,730
I wanted to separate the players
from other alliances...

428
00:18:10,730 --> 00:18:13,160
while placing ourselves back-to-back.

429
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:25,140
Ta-da.

430
00:18:25,610 --> 00:18:27,340
You have submitted the order.

431
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:30,150
- Please go back to the main hall.
- Thank you.

432
00:18:32,750 --> 00:18:34,690
Here's the order of turns.

433
00:18:36,220 --> 00:18:39,560
The red car with number one goes
to Jeong Keun Woo.

434
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:40,960
I'm first?

435
00:18:41,230 --> 00:18:43,990
The sky blue car with number two goes
to Kang Ji Hoo.

436
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,900
The yellow car with number three goes
to YunB.

437
00:18:48,870 --> 00:18:51,840
The green car with number four goes
to Heo Seong Beom.

438
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:55,570
The blue car with number five goes
to Hong Jin Ho.

439
00:18:56,340 --> 00:18:59,340
The purple car with number six goes
to Choi Hye Seon.

440
00:19:00,740 --> 00:19:03,810
The white car with number seven goes
to Hyun Sung Joo.

441
00:19:04,550 --> 00:19:08,590
The black car with number eight goes
to Shin Seung Yong.

442
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,320
(Jeong Keun Woo, Kang Ji Hoo, YunB,
Heo Seong Beom, Hong Jin Ho,)

443
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:15,460
(Choi Hye Seon, Hyun Sung Joo,
Shin Seung Yong)

444
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,560
(Jeong Keun Woo)

445
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:20,560
(The 1st player of Round 1)

446
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:22,700
You want to get rid of me first.
Is that it?

447
00:19:23,300 --> 00:19:24,400
Right? You want me gone first.

448
00:19:25,340 --> 00:19:28,140
I thought it would take some time...

449
00:19:28,310 --> 00:19:30,970
to get the hang of it
for the first player.

450
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:33,180
He might be at a disadvantage
in Round One.

451
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:34,650
But there will be a point
when his position will come in handy...

452
00:19:34,650 --> 00:19:36,080
as we keep playing.

453
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:40,550
I thought he might not maximize
the advantage as much as the others.

454
00:19:40,750 --> 00:19:42,950
And Seong Beom is number four...

455
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:46,160
which means he could be
the first one to play in the last round.

456
00:19:46,620 --> 00:19:48,260
That's why I put down...

457
00:19:48,630 --> 00:19:50,630
Seong Beom, Jin Ho, and me
for numbers 4, 5, and 6.

458
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:54,460
Actually,
going second is the absolute worst.

459
00:19:55,730 --> 00:19:58,000
The game will end in 20 rounds.

460
00:19:58,300 --> 00:20:00,300
I'll go last in Round 19.

461
00:20:00,670 --> 00:20:02,670
And I'll be the penultimate player
in Round 20.

462
00:20:02,870 --> 00:20:04,370
She gave me that spot.

463
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:08,050
Then she kept me and Seung Yong as far
as possible, so we couldn't control...

464
00:20:08,050 --> 00:20:09,380
the flow of the game.

465
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:12,720
I sensed
that this wouldn't be an easy one.

466
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:16,490
You will now predict your rank
in the race.

467
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:19,920
Enter the Voting Room in order.

468
00:20:22,260 --> 00:20:23,390
How will you predict yours?

469
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:27,100
I think they'll predict
1st, 2nd, and 3rd place.

470
00:20:27,800 --> 00:20:29,330
You think they'd be that foolish?

471
00:20:29,630 --> 00:20:31,230
It's such a foolish thing to do.

472
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:32,800
One of them has to settle
for a lower place.

473
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:36,970
I see. So they might predict
1st, 2nd, and 8th place?

474
00:20:37,240 --> 00:20:38,640
That's possible.

475
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:40,910
With three people on the team,

476
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,410
one of them should go
for a spot in the top three.

477
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:43,950
Another one for the middle ranks.

478
00:20:43,950 --> 00:20:45,420
And the last one
for either 7th or 8th place.

479
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:48,920
They'd think whoever goes for the bottom
would get their prediction right for sure.

480
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:51,620
If I were playing individually,
I was going to pick 7th or 8th place.

481
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:54,390
There's a risk,

482
00:20:54,390 --> 00:20:56,090
but getting the prediction right...

483
00:20:56,090 --> 00:20:58,060
would increase the chances
of advancing to the final match.

484
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,670
But if we're playing as a team,

485
00:21:02,230 --> 00:21:03,700
one of us should go for a spot
in the top three.

486
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:07,240
And the other one should go for a spot
in the middle three.

487
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,570
I think we should go for higher ranks.

488
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:11,310
Go for it. Pick either 2nd or 3rd place.

489
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,410
I'll take one in the low-middle tier.

490
00:21:13,910 --> 00:21:16,210
- So second place?
- Go with that.

491
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:18,020
That might be a better strategy.

492
00:21:18,980 --> 00:21:20,850
We need to come up with a strategy
with the best...

493
00:21:20,850 --> 00:21:23,520
- The most-balanced strategy?
- Yes, the most-balanced strategy.

494
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,720
If we all correctly predict our ranks,

495
00:21:26,990 --> 00:21:28,560
- the one with a higher rank wins.
- Yes.

496
00:21:28,760 --> 00:21:30,760
But if we fail to predict our ranks,

497
00:21:30,930 --> 00:21:32,500
the one with a higher rank
in the race wins.

498
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,460
Getting our prediction right
is the most important.

499
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:35,900
But that might be difficult.

500
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:37,800
Only four of us can advance.

501
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,970
Let's say
all of us correctly predict our ranks.

502
00:21:39,970 --> 00:21:42,270
Only the top four players can advance.
The race rankings...

503
00:21:42,710 --> 00:21:45,580
We don't have to go for 6th or 7th place.

504
00:21:46,880 --> 00:21:48,710
I think we'll be safe
up to 4th and 5th place.

505
00:21:49,880 --> 00:21:52,850
Most importantly,
our predictions can't overlap.

506
00:21:54,020 --> 00:21:55,090
Right.

507
00:21:55,450 --> 00:21:57,490
I want to drive my race car...

508
00:21:57,520 --> 00:21:59,490
in style right to the very end.

509
00:21:59,490 --> 00:22:01,860
- You can drive it or sabotage it.
- Yes.

510
00:22:02,090 --> 00:22:03,490
- It might even overturn.
- Exactly.

511
00:22:03,490 --> 00:22:04,930
- You could get in someone's way.
- Sure.

512
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:07,860
I'm a man with a driver's license.

513
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:13,400
Is it helpful for you if we speed up...

514
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:15,010
the race?

515
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:18,680
- She's feeling you out.
- I'll start with a bang.

516
00:22:18,810 --> 00:22:20,610
- That will be better for you?
- Yes. I'm going first.

517
00:22:20,810 --> 00:22:23,610
When players fail
to predict their rank correctly,

518
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:27,250
top finishers in the race will advance.

519
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:30,350
I had a feeling that a lot of players...

520
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:34,420
probably chose a spot in the top three.

521
00:22:35,190 --> 00:22:37,660
Keun Woo, please head to the Voting Room.

522
00:22:43,470 --> 00:22:44,470
Keun Woo,

523
00:22:44,470 --> 00:22:47,040
choose your predicted rank in the race.

524
00:22:47,770 --> 00:22:49,040
I was playing on my own.

525
00:22:49,040 --> 00:22:53,080
I thought about ways to win the game
while going solo.

526
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:57,150
Keun Woo,
you predicted you would be in sixth place.

527
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:02,320
I shouldn't try to beat the alliance.

528
00:23:02,650 --> 00:23:05,460
I'll be a little behind the middle group.

529
00:23:05,690 --> 00:23:09,390
I decided to take things slow
when the game began.

530
00:23:09,630 --> 00:23:11,900
So I predicted I'd be in sixth place.

531
00:23:22,970 --> 00:23:26,140
Ji Hoo, you predicted
you would be in second place.

532
00:23:27,010 --> 00:23:28,380
My strategy is simple.

533
00:23:28,580 --> 00:23:30,450
I'll pretend
I really want to win first place.

534
00:23:30,810 --> 00:23:33,020
I'll try to pull ahead
right out of the gate.

535
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:35,420
When I do that,
they'll try to pull me back.

536
00:23:36,190 --> 00:23:38,520
I'll pretend that they got their way.
But at the end...

537
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:41,590
"I really wanted to win 1st place,
but I'm in 2nd place."

538
00:23:41,960 --> 00:23:43,960
"But actually, I wanted second place."

539
00:23:43,960 --> 00:23:45,530
Tricking them is my strategy.

540
00:23:50,630 --> 00:23:53,840
YunB, choose your predicted rank.

541
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,240
The best-case scenario is...

542
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:59,610
finishing the race
in the rank I predicted.

543
00:23:59,880 --> 00:24:02,810
I sort of got the big picture.

544
00:24:03,580 --> 00:24:06,080
Seong Beom, choose your predicted rank.

545
00:24:06,980 --> 00:24:08,080
I have a good feeling about this.

546
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:09,390
Jin Ho,

547
00:24:09,990 --> 00:24:11,720
choose your predicted rank.

548
00:24:11,720 --> 00:24:12,820
(Hong Jin Ho completes his prediction.)

549
00:24:12,820 --> 00:24:13,890
Okay.

550
00:24:15,090 --> 00:24:17,860
Hye Seon, choose your predicted rank.

551
00:24:22,230 --> 00:24:23,370
Sung Joo,

552
00:24:24,230 --> 00:24:26,100
choose your predicted rank.

553
00:24:28,770 --> 00:24:31,410
Seung Yong, choose your predicted rank.

554
00:24:33,310 --> 00:24:36,280
(Seung Yong completes his prediction too.)

555
00:24:36,910 --> 00:24:39,450
Predictions for the race rankings
have ended.

556
00:24:39,450 --> 00:24:41,790
(Predictions have ended.)

557
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:44,590
I can see it in your eyes
that you picked third place.

558
00:24:46,190 --> 00:24:47,720
I can't keep a poker face.
Don't say stuff like that.

559
00:24:49,490 --> 00:24:51,060
It looks like you put down third place.

560
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,130
Did you bet on coming in last?

561
00:24:56,230 --> 00:24:57,270
First place or last place?

562
00:24:57,270 --> 00:24:58,800
Will you end the race early
or after Round 20?

563
00:24:58,800 --> 00:25:00,640
You three must be on the same boat, right?

564
00:25:04,470 --> 00:25:06,540
Round One will begin now.

565
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:09,580
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

566
00:25:10,810 --> 00:25:15,120
(Keun Woo)

567
00:25:15,650 --> 00:25:20,890
Place 1 of your colored cards
numbered 1 through 5...

568
00:25:21,260 --> 00:25:24,460
in one of the areas from A to D where
your target movement card is located.

569
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:26,700
The player with...

570
00:25:26,700 --> 00:25:29,200
the highest number in each area
claims the cards.

571
00:25:29,900 --> 00:25:32,800
If two or more players put down
the same number,

572
00:25:32,940 --> 00:25:35,810
the player with the next-highest number
claims the cards.

573
00:25:36,610 --> 00:25:38,710
I think we can try for C.

574
00:25:39,140 --> 00:25:41,980
But I'm going to put down a one
in this round.

575
00:25:42,810 --> 00:25:44,980
You can put down a five for C.

576
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:46,880
We thought about
getting Hye Seon's car to move forward.

577
00:25:46,880 --> 00:25:49,820
To make that happen,
winning Area C would give her an edge.

578
00:25:49,820 --> 00:25:51,820
But other people might also bet a five.

579
00:25:52,390 --> 00:25:53,860
Should I put down a four for C?

580
00:25:55,230 --> 00:25:56,960
That's iffy. Hear me out.

581
00:25:57,230 --> 00:26:00,200
Betting a 4 makes sense
if someone else bets a 5 simultaneously.

582
00:26:00,660 --> 00:26:02,330
- That's the only possibility you'd win.
- I see.

583
00:26:02,330 --> 00:26:05,640
Or 1 of us can help you win with a 4.

584
00:26:05,800 --> 00:26:07,140
- But...
- That's unnecessary.

585
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:09,570
I'm not sure if it's the right move
considering the opportunity cost.

586
00:26:09,570 --> 00:26:11,110
- I agree. That doesn't sound right.
- Okay.

587
00:26:12,240 --> 00:26:15,350
In anticipation of tied numbers
in one area,

588
00:26:16,080 --> 00:26:18,750
if other players from the alliance play
low numbers together,

589
00:26:18,880 --> 00:26:21,020
it boosts the alliance's chances
of securing the cards.

590
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:23,250
Is it necessary to burn our cards
in the beginning?

591
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:26,690
Taking an early lead won't be good
in my opinion...

592
00:26:26,690 --> 00:26:28,430
because there's a booster.

593
00:26:28,430 --> 00:26:30,590
It's better to be trailing behind
up until the second half.

594
00:26:31,660 --> 00:26:33,800
In Round One,
I'm letting other players take a lead,

595
00:26:33,800 --> 00:26:35,900
so I can stay back
and try to read other players' strategies.

596
00:26:36,030 --> 00:26:38,400
There's no point
in winning the target cards.

597
00:26:41,300 --> 00:26:44,510
Jin Ho. You've placed Card One in Area C.

598
00:26:44,770 --> 00:26:47,180
I decided to discard low numbers
in Round One.

599
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:50,410
- Card One to Area B.
- Seong Beom.

600
00:26:50,410 --> 00:26:52,750
You've placed Card One in Area B.

601
00:26:53,080 --> 00:26:55,120
I wasn't trying to win anything,
so I put down a one.

602
00:26:55,550 --> 00:26:56,690
These are mine.

603
00:26:59,290 --> 00:27:00,320
Hello.

604
00:27:02,230 --> 00:27:03,330
Sung Joo.

605
00:27:03,790 --> 00:27:06,100
Place your card
in the area of your choice.

606
00:27:06,500 --> 00:27:07,760
I wanted to show them...

607
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:10,300
my car moving forward aggressively
with the cards I won.

608
00:27:11,030 --> 00:27:12,270
I'll put it down in Area C.

609
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:16,110
Sung Joo.
You've placed Card Five in Area C.

610
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:18,540
(Area C already has 2 5s.)

611
00:27:18,540 --> 00:27:20,740
The best-case scenario is that...

612
00:27:21,080 --> 00:27:24,410
we win Area C and move forward.

613
00:27:24,710 --> 00:27:25,720
Yes.

614
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:28,350
I'll put down a five in Area C.

615
00:27:28,490 --> 00:27:29,490
Okay.

616
00:27:29,490 --> 00:27:31,790
Then why don't you put down a one there?

617
00:27:33,090 --> 00:27:35,230
I think it's a good idea
that you come into Area C.

618
00:27:36,690 --> 00:27:38,230
We might get a tie with five.

619
00:27:39,460 --> 00:27:41,200
Putting down a one there...

620
00:27:41,200 --> 00:27:43,100
doesn't sound efficient
even if we anticipate that.

621
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:46,000
So you want to play for the area
no one will go for, right?

622
00:27:46,470 --> 00:27:48,540
Area D doesn't look that popular.

623
00:27:48,870 --> 00:27:50,140
I'm still thinking.

624
00:27:51,670 --> 00:27:52,880
Ji Hoo.

625
00:27:53,010 --> 00:27:55,450
You've placed Card Five in Area C.

626
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:01,580
- I'll go here.
- Seung Yong.

627
00:28:01,580 --> 00:28:03,990
You've placed Card One in Area A.

628
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:07,120
What's that called?
There are two slots on the gear board.

629
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:10,230
So that gives us only 16 available slots
for the cards, right?

630
00:28:10,690 --> 00:28:11,800
- Right.
- Okay.

631
00:28:11,800 --> 00:28:12,900
But you don't have to put down any cards.

632
00:28:13,630 --> 00:28:15,100
- Is that allowed?
- Yes, it's allowed.

633
00:28:15,100 --> 00:28:16,800
We have three minutes
to put down our cards.

634
00:28:16,930 --> 00:28:19,100
During those three minutes,
we don't have to put down any cards.

635
00:28:19,940 --> 00:28:21,600
Keun Woo, how is it
that you understood the rules so well?

636
00:28:22,670 --> 00:28:23,770
You know what?

637
00:28:24,270 --> 00:28:25,680
He's a master of survival shows.

638
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:27,540
- The cards get discarded.
- Yes.

639
00:28:28,010 --> 00:28:29,250
Because I was on my own,

640
00:28:29,250 --> 00:28:33,020
I was able to understand the rules
super quickly.

641
00:28:33,150 --> 00:28:34,620
I had no one else to rely on.

642
00:28:34,780 --> 00:28:36,120
Even before the game began,

643
00:28:36,120 --> 00:28:38,290
I had already understood
all of the game rules.

644
00:28:38,690 --> 00:28:40,260
What if two players put down...

645
00:28:40,260 --> 00:28:41,420
the same number?

646
00:28:41,420 --> 00:28:42,490
- That area disappears then?
- It's a bust then.

647
00:28:42,490 --> 00:28:43,630
- It's a bust?
- No one can claim the cards.

648
00:28:43,630 --> 00:28:44,690
It's a bust then.

649
00:28:45,300 --> 00:28:46,830
Ask me about the rules, Hye Seon.
I know every rule.

650
00:28:46,830 --> 00:28:47,860
- Right.
- Yes.

651
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:53,240
(Jeong Keun Woo...)

652
00:28:53,240 --> 00:28:56,470
(and YunB place their bet.)

653
00:28:57,870 --> 00:28:59,640
All players have placed their bets.

654
00:29:00,010 --> 00:29:02,180
I will announce the betting results.

655
00:29:02,850 --> 00:29:03,910
Announce them now.

656
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:06,580
Area A...

657
00:29:07,950 --> 00:29:11,150
- goes to Seung Yong.
- Yes.

658
00:29:11,190 --> 00:29:12,420
How big of a number did you put down?

659
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:13,760
(Seung Yong claims the cards with a 1.)

660
00:29:13,760 --> 00:29:18,090
- Darn it.
- Area B goes to Seong Beom.

661
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:21,030
(Seong Beom also claims the cards
with a 1.)

662
00:29:21,700 --> 00:29:22,730
Area C goes...

663
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:25,240
That's mine.

664
00:29:26,070 --> 00:29:28,370
to YunB.

665
00:29:30,310 --> 00:29:34,110
Area D goes to Keun Woo.

666
00:29:35,210 --> 00:29:37,150
We're all starting from zero.

667
00:29:37,380 --> 00:29:39,120
Who would pick a reverse card?

668
00:29:41,990 --> 00:29:44,390
If I win the cards, then I win.
If I don't, then I don't.

669
00:29:46,090 --> 00:29:50,990
I put down my lowest value card
to test the waters.

670
00:29:51,560 --> 00:29:52,660
And I won.

671
00:29:53,460 --> 00:29:54,860
- Area C must've been a bust.
- Wait.

672
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:56,700
- Right, it was a bust.
- I didn't win either.

673
00:29:56,700 --> 00:29:59,170
I put down a one there
in case it was a bust.

674
00:29:59,170 --> 00:30:00,940
(Jin Ho put down a 1 in Area C
in case Hye Seon's card was wasted.)

675
00:30:01,240 --> 00:30:02,810
She put down a five.

676
00:30:02,810 --> 00:30:04,370
We had a feeling
the others would put down a five too.

677
00:30:04,370 --> 00:30:06,310
As a contingency plan,

678
00:30:06,310 --> 00:30:08,140
I decided to put down a 1 or a 2...

679
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:09,780
in case 2 or more players put down a 5,
so we could win the cards.

680
00:30:10,280 --> 00:30:14,050
- YunB must've put down 2, 3, or 4.
- Yes.

681
00:30:14,250 --> 00:30:15,350
(The competition was intense
to become the winner of Area C.)

682
00:30:15,350 --> 00:30:16,620
I won the cards.

683
00:30:19,390 --> 00:30:21,890
You've placed Card Four in Area C.

684
00:30:22,730 --> 00:30:26,160
I was certain that
someone would put down a five in Area C.

685
00:30:26,260 --> 00:30:28,500
So I put down a four as insurance.

686
00:30:28,770 --> 00:30:30,570
(Distributing the movement cards)

687
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:31,900
Okay. Thank you.

688
00:30:32,570 --> 00:30:35,240
You will now place your movement cards.

689
00:30:35,540 --> 00:30:38,240
Keun Woo, please place your cards.

690
00:30:39,010 --> 00:30:40,540
- Where will you place them?
- What?

691
00:30:40,540 --> 00:30:42,410
- Where will you place them?
- I have a reverse card.

692
00:30:46,420 --> 00:30:49,420
(Keun Woo places the movement cards
on Seung Yong's board,)

693
00:30:49,420 --> 00:30:50,990
(so he can move forward.)

694
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,120
Holy moly.

695
00:30:53,860 --> 00:30:55,190
Good for you, Seung Yong.

696
00:30:55,230 --> 00:30:56,260
Vroom.

697
00:30:56,260 --> 00:30:57,490
Gosh, I can't believe this.

698
00:30:57,490 --> 00:30:59,330
He made it back
from the Deathmatch yesterday.

699
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,370
I'm testing the waters.

700
00:31:02,370 --> 00:31:04,400
My guess is almost everyone probably...

701
00:31:04,400 --> 00:31:06,900
wanted to place at the top.

702
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:08,370
"Okay. Go for it."

703
00:31:08,370 --> 00:31:10,410
I was testing the waters
by helping him move forward.

704
00:31:10,510 --> 00:31:12,410
You now have one minute left.

705
00:31:13,210 --> 00:31:16,410
(He places the reverse card
on YunB's gear board.)

706
00:31:17,950 --> 00:31:19,620
Gosh, it's impossible to guess his moves.

707
00:31:19,950 --> 00:31:21,450
It's impossible to guess his moves.

708
00:31:21,680 --> 00:31:22,820
My goodness.

709
00:31:23,490 --> 00:31:25,090
Keun Woo hates me.

710
00:31:25,820 --> 00:31:27,190
I really like Keun Woo.

711
00:31:27,190 --> 00:31:28,490
But I think he hates me...

712
00:31:28,490 --> 00:31:29,930
if I'm being honest with you.

713
00:31:30,030 --> 00:31:31,290
I don't know when it started.

714
00:31:31,290 --> 00:31:34,500
But it might have started
when I wanted to get rid of Ji Min.

715
00:31:34,900 --> 00:31:37,030
YunB, please place your cards.

716
00:31:37,030 --> 00:31:38,970
(He won the movement cards,
but he can't move forward now.)

717
00:31:38,970 --> 00:31:41,070
You can't move forward anyway, right?

718
00:31:41,070 --> 00:31:42,910
What happens if I have a reverse card...

719
00:31:43,270 --> 00:31:44,770
and a two?

720
00:31:44,870 --> 00:31:46,380
We're at the starting line.
You can't move...

721
00:31:46,380 --> 00:31:47,440
- backward.
- Exactly.

722
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,150
I don't think
you can move forward in this round.

723
00:31:49,280 --> 00:31:50,350
- He can't.
- Right.

724
00:31:50,350 --> 00:31:51,750
- I can't do anything, right?
- Right.

725
00:31:51,750 --> 00:31:53,320
So you can help me instead.

726
00:31:55,920 --> 00:31:57,790
- You're a go-getter.
- Yes.

727
00:31:57,790 --> 00:32:00,120
Placing a number card on the right slot
doesn't do anything for me, right?

728
00:32:00,120 --> 00:32:01,460
Right.

729
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:03,660
- I need to finish near the top.
- What?

730
00:32:03,660 --> 00:32:05,030
- I need to finish near the top.
- Okay.

731
00:32:05,030 --> 00:32:07,160
If you don't have any use for them,

732
00:32:07,260 --> 00:32:09,170
could you help me this time?

733
00:32:09,200 --> 00:32:10,370
You need to finish near the top.

734
00:32:10,370 --> 00:32:12,270
Should we share our prediction
and keep it between us?

735
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:13,770
- I'll tell you mine.
- Okay.

736
00:32:13,770 --> 00:32:14,900
I need to finish second.

737
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,940
That's a relief. I need to finish third.

738
00:32:16,940 --> 00:32:18,780
- Okay.
- Right.

739
00:32:20,780 --> 00:32:24,010
(YunB predicted he'd be in 3rd place.)

740
00:32:24,080 --> 00:32:26,850
I chose third place for a simple reason.

741
00:32:27,050 --> 00:32:30,620
I don't have to be aggressive
in the beginning of the game.

742
00:32:30,850 --> 00:32:34,490
With third place, I have more options
to trick other players.

743
00:32:34,620 --> 00:32:36,890
Ji Hoo's prediction was second place.

744
00:32:37,160 --> 00:32:40,060
Given our predictions,
forming an alliance works in our favor.

745
00:32:40,060 --> 00:32:41,260
Second and third place.

746
00:32:41,830 --> 00:32:43,530
We might be able
to win 2nd and 3rd place...

747
00:32:43,530 --> 00:32:45,400
toward the end.

748
00:32:46,100 --> 00:32:48,640
YunB, you now have one minute left.

749
00:32:49,140 --> 00:32:50,570
(Placing a 4 on Ji Hoo's gear board)

750
00:32:50,570 --> 00:32:52,280
He's helping Ji Hoo move forward.

751
00:32:53,810 --> 00:32:55,110
He's going straight ahead.

752
00:32:56,250 --> 00:32:57,550
Ji Hoo is in the lead.

753
00:32:58,750 --> 00:33:00,180
- Give me one too.
- YunB,

754
00:33:00,180 --> 00:33:02,020
your time is up.

755
00:33:02,020 --> 00:33:03,690
Your cards will be discarded.

756
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:04,690
(The rest of the cards are discarded.)

757
00:33:04,690 --> 00:33:06,260
What a waste.

758
00:33:06,660 --> 00:33:08,290
Watching the cards get discarded...

759
00:33:08,290 --> 00:33:09,360
felt like such a waste.

760
00:33:09,490 --> 00:33:11,360
YunB must want to finish
between 5th and 7th place.

761
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,160
It must be somewhere around there.

762
00:33:13,260 --> 00:33:15,470
Seong Beom, please place your cards.

763
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:16,830
I'll move forward first.

764
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:19,040
Yes. You can do that.

765
00:33:20,270 --> 00:33:22,070
Jin Ho. Hye Seon. Does anyone want a card?

766
00:33:22,070 --> 00:33:23,710
Me. Help me move forward.

767
00:33:25,340 --> 00:33:28,750
(He places a 2 and a 3 on his gear board.)

768
00:33:29,550 --> 00:33:31,650
(He places a 1 on Hye Seon's gear board.)

769
00:33:31,780 --> 00:33:34,220
Seung Yong, please place your cards.

770
00:33:35,590 --> 00:33:36,950
- Do you want to move forward?
- Yes.

771
00:33:37,750 --> 00:33:39,720
- What should I do?
- Help me start the engine.

772
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:41,360
What do you want? What should I do?

773
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:44,290
Put down a three on my board.

774
00:33:44,290 --> 00:33:45,560
Then play safe with the rest.

775
00:33:47,160 --> 00:33:48,870
All right.

776
00:33:49,300 --> 00:33:50,700
Ji Hoo must be in a hurry.

777
00:33:50,700 --> 00:33:51,870
Help him move forward.

778
00:33:52,270 --> 00:33:54,140
They're working together.
Of course, he has to do that.

779
00:33:54,570 --> 00:33:56,510
(Placing a 3 on Ji Hoo's gear board)

780
00:33:57,340 --> 00:33:58,440
Go ahead.

781
00:33:58,440 --> 00:33:59,710
(Placing a 1 on Hye Seon's gear board)

782
00:34:00,140 --> 00:34:01,280
Don't move.

783
00:34:02,080 --> 00:34:03,310
Moving back zero spaces.

784
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:05,980
All the movement cards have been placed.

785
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:09,150
(Ji Hoo, Seong Beom, Hye Seon,
and Seung Yong can move their car.)

786
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:12,190
Ji Hoo, please pick your starting space.

787
00:34:13,690 --> 00:34:14,890
I'll start here.

788
00:34:15,390 --> 00:34:17,930
Ji Hoo, you chose Lane Six.

789
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:19,630
Three spaces forward...

790
00:34:19,630 --> 00:34:21,330
and one space left.

791
00:34:23,530 --> 00:34:25,370
Look at you, pulling ahead.

792
00:34:25,370 --> 00:34:26,770
That's so cool.

793
00:34:27,270 --> 00:34:29,610
YunB, you cannot move.

794
00:34:30,370 --> 00:34:32,510
Seong Beom,
please pick your starting space.

795
00:34:32,510 --> 00:34:33,810
I'll choose Lane Four.

796
00:34:33,810 --> 00:34:35,780
Seong Beom, you chose Lane Four.

797
00:34:35,780 --> 00:34:36,850
(Seong Beom chooses to start from Lane 4.)

798
00:34:37,410 --> 00:34:38,950
Two spaces forward...

799
00:34:38,950 --> 00:34:40,780
and one space right.

800
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:43,520
(Seong Beom)

801
00:34:43,520 --> 00:34:44,920
My booster could get activated.

802
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:48,560
(As he's right behind Ji Hoo,
his booster may be activated in Round 2.)

803
00:34:48,590 --> 00:34:49,890
Ji Hoo is going before you.

804
00:34:50,290 --> 00:34:51,360
He'll try to get away.

805
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:53,500
- If he can't move, you'll get it.
- Right.

806
00:34:53,960 --> 00:34:56,500
Hye Seon, please pick your starting space.

807
00:34:57,530 --> 00:34:58,800
I'll choose...

808
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:00,970
- Which one?
- Lane Four.

809
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:04,110
One space forward.

810
00:35:06,010 --> 00:35:08,740
Seung Yong,
please pick your starting space.

811
00:35:09,850 --> 00:35:11,150
I'll go with Lane Six.

812
00:35:11,180 --> 00:35:14,050
One space forward and one space left.

813
00:35:15,120 --> 00:35:17,590
(Seung Yong)

814
00:35:17,790 --> 00:35:19,790
I just helped you get out on the road.

815
00:35:19,790 --> 00:35:20,820
Thank you.

816
00:35:21,590 --> 00:35:23,360
I guess I can expect a similar pattern.

817
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,390
- Right.
- Yes.

818
00:35:24,460 --> 00:35:26,400
All players have completed their moves.

819
00:35:27,460 --> 00:35:29,370
Getting the car to move
is harder than I thought.

820
00:35:29,670 --> 00:35:32,340
Please don't make it difficult for me,
Keun Woo.

821
00:35:32,340 --> 00:35:33,500
I made it difficult for you?

822
00:35:34,140 --> 00:35:35,270
You gave me a reverse card.

823
00:35:35,270 --> 00:35:37,210
I see. You have to finish near the top?

824
00:35:37,540 --> 00:35:38,840
- I...
- Do you need to go forward quickly?

825
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,110
That's better for me.

826
00:35:41,780 --> 00:35:44,450
I don't even know
who gave what card in Round One.

827
00:35:44,450 --> 00:35:46,080
What if YunB predicted he'd finish eighth?

828
00:35:47,980 --> 00:35:50,090
Look at him. He's acting again.

829
00:35:50,750 --> 00:35:52,860
Round Two will begin now.

830
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:56,290
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

831
00:35:57,090 --> 00:35:59,400
(Ji Hoo)

832
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:01,960
(Ji Hoo)

833
00:36:07,570 --> 00:36:09,840
After looking at the numbers,
I went in as fast as possible.

834
00:36:15,380 --> 00:36:17,810
I put down a four...

835
00:36:18,080 --> 00:36:20,980
to win 2, 1, and 3 in Round 2.

836
00:36:21,180 --> 00:36:23,890
With 2, 1, and 3,

837
00:36:23,890 --> 00:36:27,190
people will think
that they'd be able to pull ahead.

838
00:36:27,190 --> 00:36:29,260
If I go for these numbers,
they might think I went for a high rank.

839
00:36:29,260 --> 00:36:31,660
I wanted to confuse them a little.

840
00:36:32,130 --> 00:36:34,100
- How do you decide so fast?
- What?

841
00:36:35,670 --> 00:36:37,000
When someone decides quickly,

842
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:39,600
the other players will feel
a sense of urgency.

843
00:36:39,600 --> 00:36:42,000
Going into the Voting Room fast
was one of my strategies.

844
00:36:44,110 --> 00:36:46,010
- Do you have to move forward?
- What?

845
00:36:46,010 --> 00:36:47,140
You haven't left yet, right?

846
00:36:47,140 --> 00:36:49,510
(His white race car hasn't crossed
the starting line yet.)

847
00:36:49,650 --> 00:36:51,280
It's not up to me, you know?

848
00:36:52,080 --> 00:36:53,450
You can make it happen this time.

849
00:36:55,420 --> 00:36:56,520
I have to win to do that.

850
00:36:56,620 --> 00:36:57,620
Let me know if you need help.

851
00:36:57,620 --> 00:36:59,090
I'm going to play on my own for this game.

852
00:36:59,160 --> 00:37:01,160
There might come a time
when you need help.

853
00:37:01,160 --> 00:37:02,860
You can't be on your own
from start to finish.

854
00:37:03,090 --> 00:37:04,260
I want to see how it pans out.

855
00:37:05,830 --> 00:37:08,300
During the first half of the game,
I thought behaving in a way...

856
00:37:08,300 --> 00:37:09,770
that they couldn't guess my prediction...

857
00:37:10,330 --> 00:37:11,900
was the most important.

858
00:37:12,300 --> 00:37:13,870
It didn't matter
if I won the cards or not.

859
00:37:13,870 --> 00:37:15,340
That wasn't important in the first half.

860
00:37:15,400 --> 00:37:17,210
They'll give me a new set of cards
once I run out.

861
00:37:17,210 --> 00:37:19,180
Should I just put down a four in Area B?

862
00:37:19,280 --> 00:37:20,510
- To play offense?
- Yes.

863
00:37:22,510 --> 00:37:23,680
- That sounds good too.
- Yes.

864
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:24,780
(Area B has a reverse card.)

865
00:37:24,780 --> 00:37:26,250
A lot of them moved ahead.

866
00:37:27,050 --> 00:37:28,150
Which area will you go for?

867
00:37:28,990 --> 00:37:31,390
If I want to win the cards,
I should pick an area with better odds.

868
00:37:32,460 --> 00:37:34,960
I'll put down a three
considering the possibility...

869
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:36,390
that it might be a bust.

870
00:37:36,960 --> 00:37:39,630
In the previous round,
we put down a five...

871
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:41,130
and a one.

872
00:37:41,130 --> 00:37:43,270
But other players put down the same card.

873
00:37:43,270 --> 00:37:45,400
I thought
that might not be a good strategy.

874
00:37:45,400 --> 00:37:47,300
And I also thought
that we should split up for this round.

875
00:37:47,970 --> 00:37:49,840
(Hye Seon bets a 4 on Area B.)

876
00:37:50,870 --> 00:37:52,340
I'll do this.

877
00:37:53,940 --> 00:37:55,910
(Seong Beom bets a 3 on Area C.)

878
00:37:56,380 --> 00:37:59,480
Seong Beom.
You've placed Card Three in Area C.

879
00:37:59,480 --> 00:38:00,880
- Is that right?
- Yes.

880
00:38:01,350 --> 00:38:03,050
Are you going to bet low this round?

881
00:38:04,450 --> 00:38:06,760
I think I need to bet high this round
and get a head start...

882
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:08,590
because after this round,

883
00:38:08,590 --> 00:38:10,730
I'm late in the turn order.

884
00:38:11,060 --> 00:38:13,230
It doesn't matter if I win good cards.

885
00:38:13,230 --> 00:38:16,000
If they place bad cards on my gear board
to hold me back,

886
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:17,630
I won't be able to use
any of my good cards.

887
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:20,940
If I win the cards
and am the first one to place the cards,

888
00:38:21,340 --> 00:38:23,240
I can place them wherever I want.

889
00:38:23,270 --> 00:38:24,610
If I'm late in the turn order,

890
00:38:24,840 --> 00:38:26,080
winning the cards doesn't matter.

891
00:38:26,080 --> 00:38:28,110
My gear board could be full by my turn.

892
00:38:28,280 --> 00:38:29,650
So I wouldn't be able to place
any of my cards.

893
00:38:29,650 --> 00:38:31,110
When I'm going first,

894
00:38:31,250 --> 00:38:33,880
I have to bet high
in order to win the cards no matter what.

895
00:38:34,120 --> 00:38:36,390
When I'm late in the turn order,
I have to bet low...

896
00:38:36,390 --> 00:38:38,450
and get rid of the low value cards.

897
00:38:38,450 --> 00:38:39,690
So...

898
00:38:39,690 --> 00:38:42,290
there was a set of cards with 3 and 4.

899
00:38:42,530 --> 00:38:45,330
This set of cards was the best
for pushing ahead.

900
00:38:45,430 --> 00:38:46,960
I was determined to win these cards.

901
00:38:47,060 --> 00:38:48,300
I was the first one to place cards.

902
00:38:48,300 --> 00:38:50,030
So I wanted to move forward
by placing them on my board.

903
00:38:51,670 --> 00:38:53,800
- What did you and YunB talk about?
- What?

904
00:38:53,800 --> 00:38:55,140
What did you and YunB talk about?

905
00:38:57,840 --> 00:38:59,240
He needs to finish third.

906
00:39:00,680 --> 00:39:02,710
So we promised to help each other.

907
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:06,180
I revealed mine,
but I didn't reveal yours.

908
00:39:06,580 --> 00:39:07,680
Ji Hoo.

909
00:39:07,980 --> 00:39:09,090
Come here.

910
00:39:10,490 --> 00:39:12,790
So you and I know...

911
00:39:12,790 --> 00:39:13,890
each other's rank.

912
00:39:14,220 --> 00:39:16,490
Can you intervene,
so Seung Yong doesn't see me...

913
00:39:17,060 --> 00:39:18,090
as his competition?

914
00:39:18,590 --> 00:39:20,330
- Could you relay the message?
- Sure.

915
00:39:20,330 --> 00:39:21,360
You go.

916
00:39:21,360 --> 00:39:23,730
(Ji Hoo is passing messages
between YunB and Seung Yong.)

917
00:39:23,730 --> 00:39:25,500
YunB wanted me to tell you that...

918
00:39:25,630 --> 00:39:28,370
he didn't want you to see him
as competition.

919
00:39:28,540 --> 00:39:31,070
Just tell him
that he and I won't have to...

920
00:39:31,070 --> 00:39:32,170
- compete.
- Okay.

921
00:39:35,880 --> 00:39:38,180
Seung Yong doesn't need to compete
against you.

922
00:39:38,550 --> 00:39:39,720
- Is that so?
- Yes.

923
00:39:40,150 --> 00:39:42,920
So our ranks must not overlap.

924
00:39:43,190 --> 00:39:44,220
That's a relief.

925
00:39:44,620 --> 00:39:46,060
I take it
his predicted rank isn't that high?

926
00:39:48,690 --> 00:39:50,590
For now, Seung Yong...

927
00:39:51,130 --> 00:39:53,400
is still on the fence
about bringing YunB...

928
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:55,030
into our alliance.

929
00:39:55,230 --> 00:39:56,970
So, I shared my information...

930
00:39:56,970 --> 00:39:58,570
while keeping Seung Yong's info safe.

931
00:39:58,770 --> 00:40:00,800
I kept going back and forth
between them...

932
00:40:01,100 --> 00:40:02,440
to discuss strategy.

933
00:40:02,770 --> 00:40:05,040
It's bad if we go to the same one,
so I'll tell you.

934
00:40:05,310 --> 00:40:08,340
I'm going to bet a four on C.

935
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:10,280
C?

936
00:40:11,850 --> 00:40:13,480
Ji Hoo, you've bet on Area C...

937
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:14,650
(The three split up and bet.)

938
00:40:14,650 --> 00:40:16,150
YunB, you've bet on Area A...

939
00:40:17,790 --> 00:40:20,960
Seung Yong, you've placed Card Two
in Area D.

940
00:40:23,230 --> 00:40:24,890
I want to go just one space this time.

941
00:40:25,800 --> 00:40:28,300
If we don't go from the starting line,

942
00:40:28,300 --> 00:40:30,670
doesn't that count as last place?

943
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:32,100
Probably.

944
00:40:32,100 --> 00:40:33,470
But that's practically impossible.

945
00:40:33,470 --> 00:40:35,500
- Right? It's 20 rounds.
- It's impossible.

946
00:40:35,500 --> 00:40:36,670
Someone will put a card there.

947
00:40:36,670 --> 00:40:39,910
Yes, they'll think
that someone bet on last place.

948
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:43,110
I will announce the betting results.

949
00:40:44,080 --> 00:40:47,720
Area A goes to Keun Woo.

950
00:40:47,720 --> 00:40:49,220
- He's taking all of them.
- Goodness.

951
00:40:49,590 --> 00:40:51,690
You can't predict my moves.

952
00:40:51,690 --> 00:40:53,120
It's so unpredictable.

953
00:40:53,290 --> 00:40:54,290
Area B...

954
00:40:54,820 --> 00:40:56,930
goes to Hye Seon.

955
00:40:56,930 --> 00:40:58,030
Gosh, thank you.

956
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:02,900
Area C goes to Ji Hoo.

957
00:41:03,770 --> 00:41:06,500
Area D goes to Jin Ho.

958
00:41:06,500 --> 00:41:07,700
I got one.

959
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:10,310
Ji Hoo won big. I bet he'll go hard...

960
00:41:10,310 --> 00:41:11,310
to get ahead.

961
00:41:11,310 --> 00:41:13,780
I'm an auction expert.

962
00:41:13,780 --> 00:41:14,940
I won two bids.

963
00:41:14,940 --> 00:41:16,750
You're good at this.

964
00:41:17,580 --> 00:41:20,080
Ji Hoo, please place your card.

965
00:41:20,950 --> 00:41:22,750
I would like to go forward.

966
00:41:24,650 --> 00:41:26,890
(Ji Hoo puts a 2 in YunB's gear board.)

967
00:41:27,620 --> 00:41:28,620
(And he gives the rest to himself.)

968
00:41:28,620 --> 00:41:30,890
- He's going fast.
- I'm so jealous.

969
00:41:31,330 --> 00:41:34,130
I want to keep that car there.

970
00:41:34,130 --> 00:41:36,370
- Which car?
- At the starting line.

971
00:41:36,370 --> 00:41:37,500
- Whose car?
- Yours.

972
00:41:37,500 --> 00:41:38,670
Son of a...

973
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:41,670
Come on, Keun Woo.

974
00:41:41,670 --> 00:41:43,040
I thought we were friends.

975
00:41:43,470 --> 00:41:44,840
- Which one is your car?
- That one.

976
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:46,480
- I should throw it away.
- If...

977
00:41:46,710 --> 00:41:49,650
I get a reverse card,
I'm going to win it...

978
00:41:49,650 --> 00:41:51,410
so I can keep sending him back.

979
00:41:51,410 --> 00:41:52,850
Don't do that. You can be my superior.

980
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:57,620
Jin Ho, please place your card.

981
00:41:57,620 --> 00:42:00,020
(Round 2, Ji Hoo, Jin Ho, Hye Seon,
Keun Woo)

982
00:42:00,020 --> 00:42:01,720
(He places a 3 in his zone.)

983
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:03,660
Let me go forward.

984
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:06,460
Should I give one to Seong Beom?

985
00:42:06,930 --> 00:42:07,930
Sure.

986
00:42:07,930 --> 00:42:09,600
(He places a 1 in Seong Beom's area.)

987
00:42:09,730 --> 00:42:11,600
I can put three in my area,

988
00:42:11,600 --> 00:42:12,940
and Hye Seon can put two in mine.

989
00:42:12,940 --> 00:42:14,100
- What?
- Seung Yong, you went forward.

990
00:42:14,100 --> 00:42:15,200
You should keep going.

991
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:16,640
- Are you sure I can go?
- With zero.

992
00:42:16,640 --> 00:42:17,640
(He gives Seung Yong a 0.)

993
00:42:18,310 --> 00:42:19,310
- Keun Woo.
- Let me go forward.

994
00:42:19,580 --> 00:42:21,780
Can you give it to me
if you're throwing it away?

995
00:42:21,780 --> 00:42:23,610
- I'll make the decisions.
- Okay.

996
00:42:23,610 --> 00:42:26,280
Don't tell me what to do with my cards.

997
00:42:26,280 --> 00:42:27,880
Sorry.

998
00:42:29,180 --> 00:42:31,320
Hye Seon, please place your cards.

999
00:42:31,990 --> 00:42:34,320
Hye Seon, how are you going to attack?

1000
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:36,460
It's all meaningless now.

1001
00:42:36,460 --> 00:42:40,160
(She planned on attacking Ji Hoo,
but his board is already full.)

1002
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:42,400
You can give them to YunB.

1003
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:45,070
Jin Ho, you should go.

1004
00:42:45,500 --> 00:42:47,000
(She gives a 2 to Jin Ho.)

1005
00:42:47,470 --> 00:42:49,270
- What about you, Hye Seon?
- You could send me off.

1006
00:42:49,710 --> 00:42:51,440
- Why isn't Ms. Choi going?
- What should I do?

1007
00:42:52,240 --> 00:42:55,210
Why don't we help each other out?

1008
00:42:55,710 --> 00:42:56,880
Ms. Choi...

1009
00:42:56,880 --> 00:42:57,980
With this?

1010
00:42:57,980 --> 00:43:00,150
(Round 2, Ji Hoo, Jin Ho, Hye Seon,
Keun Woo)

1011
00:43:00,150 --> 00:43:01,920
I didn't know how scary you were.

1012
00:43:02,380 --> 00:43:03,390
You're really...

1013
00:43:03,390 --> 00:43:04,790
I thought you wanted it.

1014
00:43:04,790 --> 00:43:07,290
(She gives a 1 to Seong Beom.)

1015
00:43:07,290 --> 00:43:09,790
(She gives the reverse card to YunB.)

1016
00:43:09,960 --> 00:43:12,090
- Sorry.
- Oh, no.

1017
00:43:12,090 --> 00:43:14,100
(Round 2, Ji Hoo, Jin Ho, Hye Seon,
Keun Woo)

1018
00:43:14,100 --> 00:43:16,170
Team P3's biggest mistake is...

1019
00:43:16,170 --> 00:43:18,570
still playing too closely together...

1020
00:43:18,570 --> 00:43:20,300
when it's an individual match now.

1021
00:43:20,300 --> 00:43:21,600
Like, "We're Team P3."

1022
00:43:21,600 --> 00:43:22,740
I hate it.

1023
00:43:23,270 --> 00:43:25,810
Keun Woo, please place your cards.

1024
00:43:25,810 --> 00:43:28,380
I don't care about anyone else now.
I'm going to go forward.

1025
00:43:28,840 --> 00:43:30,910
- You should.
- It's about time.

1026
00:43:32,210 --> 00:43:33,650
I went through a lot to win these.

1027
00:43:34,180 --> 00:43:36,250
Oh, my gosh.

1028
00:43:36,450 --> 00:43:37,590
Goodness.

1029
00:43:37,590 --> 00:43:39,360
- You're going so fast.
- Gosh.

1030
00:43:40,360 --> 00:43:41,560
Take one, Sung Joo.

1031
00:43:41,560 --> 00:43:42,760
(He gives a 2 to Sung Joo.)

1032
00:43:42,960 --> 00:43:45,660
He benefited just by sitting there.

1033
00:43:45,790 --> 00:43:47,200
Take one, Sung Joo.

1034
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:49,200
I put one here.

1035
00:43:50,800 --> 00:43:52,370
Did you bet on placing eighth?

1036
00:43:54,140 --> 00:43:56,170
- He's keeping a poker face.
- You don't seem so happy.

1037
00:43:56,170 --> 00:43:57,540
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1038
00:43:57,540 --> 00:44:00,880
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, Seong Beom,
and Jin Ho can move.)

1039
00:44:01,880 --> 00:44:05,850
Ji Hoo, 3 spaces forward and 1 space left.

1040
00:44:05,850 --> 00:44:07,850
(Ji Hoo)

1041
00:44:07,980 --> 00:44:09,690
Oh, man.

1042
00:44:09,690 --> 00:44:10,690
This is going to end soon.

1043
00:44:10,690 --> 00:44:12,120
The game might end in Round Seven.

1044
00:44:12,120 --> 00:44:14,120
- Ji Hoo might finish it.
- Yes.

1045
00:44:14,860 --> 00:44:17,130
YunB, you cannot move.

1046
00:44:17,130 --> 00:44:18,130
(YunB's gear board is reset.)

1047
00:44:18,290 --> 00:44:20,960
Seong Beom, one space forward.

1048
00:44:21,230 --> 00:44:22,400
Vroom, vroom.

1049
00:44:23,570 --> 00:44:26,200
Jin Ho, please pick your starting space.

1050
00:44:26,400 --> 00:44:27,900
I'll go from Lane Three.

1051
00:44:28,400 --> 00:44:31,570
Two spaces forward and one space right.

1052
00:44:31,810 --> 00:44:34,480
Keun Woo, please pick your starting space.

1053
00:44:34,480 --> 00:44:36,010
(Keun Woo)

1054
00:44:36,010 --> 00:44:37,780
- I have 3 and 1, right?
- Yes, 3 and 1.

1055
00:44:37,980 --> 00:44:40,750
You could get on someone's back.

1056
00:44:40,750 --> 00:44:41,750
Exactly.

1057
00:44:42,950 --> 00:44:44,790
I had to start,

1058
00:44:44,990 --> 00:44:46,490
but I couldn't go before anybody else.

1059
00:44:46,760 --> 00:44:47,890
I'll take Lane Four.

1060
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:49,530
I decided to collide.

1061
00:44:50,260 --> 00:44:51,330
Lane Four?

1062
00:44:51,530 --> 00:44:52,530
Yes.

1063
00:44:52,730 --> 00:44:53,800
Isn't that Hye Seon's?

1064
00:44:54,760 --> 00:44:55,960
He must have a plan.

1065
00:44:56,330 --> 00:45:00,400
Keun Woo, 1 space forward
and 2 spaces left.

1066
00:45:00,400 --> 00:45:01,400
Okay.

1067
00:45:01,570 --> 00:45:04,010
You've collided with Hye Seon's race car.

1068
00:45:04,640 --> 00:45:06,080
Oh, it happens instantly.

1069
00:45:06,080 --> 00:45:07,310
- Instantly.
- Yes.

1070
00:45:07,310 --> 00:45:09,110
- From the starting line?
- We don't jump over it.

1071
00:45:09,110 --> 00:45:11,080
- All players have completed their moves.
- Okay.

1072
00:45:11,650 --> 00:45:14,120
(Hye Seon's purple car is stuck
from the start.)

1073
00:45:14,350 --> 00:45:15,350
So heavy.

1074
00:45:15,350 --> 00:45:16,390
- Sorry.
- Is someone on your back?

1075
00:45:16,390 --> 00:45:17,520
It's so heavy.

1076
00:45:18,620 --> 00:45:19,820
It's a carpool.

1077
00:45:20,120 --> 00:45:21,120
Seriously.

1078
00:45:21,290 --> 00:45:24,030
- Keun Woo, did you bet on eighth place?
- What?

1079
00:45:24,030 --> 00:45:25,160
Did you bet on eighth place?

1080
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:26,500
- Me? You can't figure it out, right?
- Yes.

1081
00:45:26,500 --> 00:45:27,630
Why aren't you going forward?

1082
00:45:28,460 --> 00:45:31,630
I realized that he either bet...

1083
00:45:31,630 --> 00:45:33,040
on 8th or 7th.

1084
00:45:33,670 --> 00:45:34,870
This is tough.

1085
00:45:35,640 --> 00:45:38,040
(Round 2 Movement Results)

1086
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:39,210
(Player, predicted rank)

1087
00:45:39,210 --> 00:45:40,380
(Ji Hoo: 2nd, Keun Woo: 6th, YunB: 3rd)

1088
00:45:40,680 --> 00:45:42,880
Round Three will now begin.

1089
00:45:43,250 --> 00:45:45,980
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1090
00:45:45,980 --> 00:45:50,190
(YunB)

1091
00:45:51,390 --> 00:45:54,190
If that team gets Area C, I'm doomed.

1092
00:45:55,490 --> 00:45:57,360
They can bring my car four spaces back.

1093
00:45:57,360 --> 00:45:58,960
(Ji Hoo)

1094
00:45:59,290 --> 00:46:01,160
So, I think it's best...

1095
00:46:01,160 --> 00:46:03,270
if you bet 5 and I bet 3.

1096
00:46:03,270 --> 00:46:04,530
Okay. That doesn't sound so bad.

1097
00:46:04,970 --> 00:46:09,270
I showed them
that I was trying to place first.

1098
00:46:09,270 --> 00:46:11,870
So, it was an important round...

1099
00:46:11,870 --> 00:46:14,340
where I had to win the reverse card
to protect myself.

1100
00:46:15,910 --> 00:46:19,680
Seung Yong, you've placed Card Five
in Area C.

1101
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:22,350
Ji Hoo, you've placed Card Three...

1102
00:46:22,350 --> 00:46:23,690
in Area C. Is that correct?

1103
00:46:23,690 --> 00:46:24,690
Yes, it is.

1104
00:46:25,550 --> 00:46:27,290
All players have placed their bets.

1105
00:46:28,060 --> 00:46:30,260
I will announce the betting results.

1106
00:46:31,030 --> 00:46:34,600
Area A goes to YunB.

1107
00:46:34,600 --> 00:46:38,500
Area B goes to Jin Ho.

1108
00:46:38,500 --> 00:46:39,500
I won with that?

1109
00:46:40,400 --> 00:46:41,400
Area C...

1110
00:46:42,800 --> 00:46:45,410
goes to Ji Hoo.

1111
00:46:46,280 --> 00:46:49,550
Seong Beom, you've placed Card Five
in Area C.

1112
00:46:50,280 --> 00:46:52,650
Seung Yong bets five, the highest number,

1113
00:46:53,120 --> 00:46:55,220
and in case there are 2 players betting 5,

1114
00:46:55,220 --> 00:46:57,020
I also bet three.

1115
00:46:57,020 --> 00:47:00,220
It was a strategy to guarantee
that I win Area C.

1116
00:47:00,290 --> 00:47:02,860
(He's secured Area C
according to his plan.)

1117
00:47:03,090 --> 00:47:06,030
Area D has no winners.

1118
00:47:06,260 --> 00:47:07,330
No way.

1119
00:47:07,700 --> 00:47:09,000
No one bet on it?

1120
00:47:10,230 --> 00:47:11,330
(Round 3 Betting Results)

1121
00:47:11,330 --> 00:47:12,530
(Area A: YunB 5, Area B: Jin Ho 5,)

1122
00:47:12,530 --> 00:47:13,570
(Area C: Ji Hoo 3)

1123
00:47:13,840 --> 00:47:17,140
- You will now place your movement cards.
- Let's go.

1124
00:47:17,140 --> 00:47:18,870
YunB, please place your cards.

1125
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:23,680
- Hye Seon's car is under Keun Woo's car.
- Yes.

1126
00:47:23,680 --> 00:47:25,410
Jin Ho is slightly ahead.

1127
00:47:25,410 --> 00:47:28,420
Maybe I should place a one
on Jin Ho's gear board.

1128
00:47:28,420 --> 00:47:31,590
Because he has fewer spaces
to go forward than Seong Beom.

1129
00:47:31,590 --> 00:47:33,520
- Because they're on one side?
- Yes.

1130
00:47:33,520 --> 00:47:35,560
- To hold Jin Ho in check.
- It makes sense.

1131
00:47:37,690 --> 00:47:40,030
(He places a 2 and a 3 in his slot.)

1132
00:47:42,730 --> 00:47:45,430
(He places a 1 in Jin Ho's slot.)

1133
00:47:45,700 --> 00:47:50,040
To me, it looked like
Jin Ho and Seong Beom...

1134
00:47:50,040 --> 00:47:52,870
were trying to go forward
as fast as possible.

1135
00:47:52,870 --> 00:47:54,080
We noticed that,

1136
00:47:54,080 --> 00:47:57,010
so we decided to disrupt their plan.

1137
00:47:57,880 --> 00:47:59,980
Jin Ho, please place your cards.

1138
00:47:59,980 --> 00:48:01,050
You're done already?

1139
00:48:01,880 --> 00:48:03,220
YunB is getting ahead.

1140
00:48:04,190 --> 00:48:05,250
(Jin Ho)

1141
00:48:05,250 --> 00:48:07,690
Oh, he blocked my right side.

1142
00:48:07,690 --> 00:48:08,820
(Jin Ho)

1143
00:48:08,820 --> 00:48:11,130
(Round 3, YunB, Jin Ho, Ji Hoo)

1144
00:48:11,930 --> 00:48:13,130
I'll have to go forward.

1145
00:48:14,700 --> 00:48:16,470
And the other one...

1146
00:48:16,470 --> 00:48:19,800
(Jin Ho: 3, 0)

1147
00:48:19,900 --> 00:48:21,300
Ji Hoo, you should crash.

1148
00:48:21,840 --> 00:48:23,410
(Ji Hoo can't move to the right.)

1149
00:48:23,410 --> 00:48:24,970
(Not allowed)

1150
00:48:25,110 --> 00:48:27,110
(Ji Hoo: Reverse, 2, 4)

1151
00:48:27,110 --> 00:48:29,180
- Who should get three?
- Give me.

1152
00:48:29,180 --> 00:48:30,210
- What?
- Right.

1153
00:48:30,210 --> 00:48:32,810
- This one is too good.
- Give it to Seong Beom.

1154
00:48:32,810 --> 00:48:33,950
I will.

1155
00:48:33,950 --> 00:48:35,920
You're in the center,
so you're good to go, right?

1156
00:48:35,920 --> 00:48:37,650
- Yes.
- Take it.

1157
00:48:37,750 --> 00:48:39,790
(He places a 3 in Seong Beom's slot.)

1158
00:48:40,460 --> 00:48:41,760
Wasn't that a mistake?

1159
00:48:42,020 --> 00:48:43,590
- What?
- Wasn't that a mistake?

1160
00:48:43,590 --> 00:48:44,690
- Why?
- Oh, no.

1161
00:48:45,130 --> 00:48:46,600
- How is it a mistake?
- Why?

1162
00:48:46,600 --> 00:48:47,600
He made a mistake.

1163
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:50,370
Because I have the reverse card.

1164
00:48:50,370 --> 00:48:51,770
- I see.
- I could...

1165
00:48:51,770 --> 00:48:52,970
I don't mind going back.

1166
00:48:52,970 --> 00:48:54,540
What if I had already calculated that?

1167
00:48:55,600 --> 00:48:56,940
You could be playing a mind game.

1168
00:48:56,940 --> 00:48:59,110
That's intense.

1169
00:48:59,110 --> 00:49:01,480
(Ji Hoo: Reverse, 2, 4)

1170
00:49:02,380 --> 00:49:04,610
Ji Hoo, please place your cards.

1171
00:49:04,610 --> 00:49:05,850
Let's see.

1172
00:49:06,110 --> 00:49:07,120
Give him the reverse card.

1173
00:49:07,420 --> 00:49:08,480
This is tricky.

1174
00:49:09,420 --> 00:49:10,420
Reverse him.

1175
00:49:11,850 --> 00:49:12,850
Okay.

1176
00:49:13,290 --> 00:49:14,560
I went through all that to go forward...

1177
00:49:14,560 --> 00:49:16,090
only to go back now.

1178
00:49:16,090 --> 00:49:18,660
(Ji Hoo: 2, 4)

1179
00:49:18,660 --> 00:49:20,860
Please give it to me!

1180
00:49:21,530 --> 00:49:22,860
(He places the rest of the cards.)

1181
00:49:22,860 --> 00:49:25,470
All the movement cards have been placed.

1182
00:49:25,800 --> 00:49:27,640
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1183
00:49:27,640 --> 00:49:31,810
(YunB, Seong Beom, Jin Ho,
and Seung Yong can move.)

1184
00:49:32,340 --> 00:49:34,840
The race cars will start moving now.

1185
00:49:35,040 --> 00:49:37,580
YunB, please pick your starting space.

1186
00:49:38,150 --> 00:49:40,150
- That's...
- I'll go from Lane Three.

1187
00:49:40,150 --> 00:49:42,680
- This is a tough one.
- YunB has chosen Lane Three.

1188
00:49:42,920 --> 00:49:44,090
He'll crash into Jin Ho.

1189
00:49:44,490 --> 00:49:48,160
YunB, 2 spaces forward and 1 space right.

1190
00:49:48,320 --> 00:49:49,320
What?

1191
00:49:49,560 --> 00:49:50,560
He's on top of you.

1192
00:49:50,690 --> 00:49:52,160
(He collides with Jin Ho.)

1193
00:49:52,160 --> 00:49:53,530
(YunB)

1194
00:49:53,530 --> 00:49:56,000
- YunB!
- You've collided with Jin Ho's race car.

1195
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:57,200
Stop coming on to me.

1196
00:49:58,830 --> 00:50:01,070
Seong Beom, three spaces backward.

1197
00:50:01,070 --> 00:50:03,710
(Seong Beom)

1198
00:50:03,910 --> 00:50:06,170
You've collided
with Seung Yong's race car.

1199
00:50:06,310 --> 00:50:07,410
What happened?

1200
00:50:07,410 --> 00:50:08,440
It's a three-layer burger.

1201
00:50:09,380 --> 00:50:12,550
Jin Ho's race car cannot move.

1202
00:50:13,280 --> 00:50:16,450
Seung Yong's race car cannot move.

1203
00:50:17,820 --> 00:50:19,860
The three cars underneath
can't do anything.

1204
00:50:21,320 --> 00:50:23,760
I saw YunB behind me...

1205
00:50:23,760 --> 00:50:25,060
and thought he wouldn't attack me...

1206
00:50:25,060 --> 00:50:28,160
because I thought
he was still neutral at the time.

1207
00:50:28,160 --> 00:50:29,800
Then, YunB and Ji Hoo...

1208
00:50:29,800 --> 00:50:32,900
started whispering into each other's ears.

1209
00:50:33,240 --> 00:50:34,840
I thought it was strange,

1210
00:50:34,840 --> 00:50:37,010
and YunB instantly got on my back.

1211
00:50:37,910 --> 00:50:39,540
Although it's the early stage,

1212
00:50:39,540 --> 00:50:43,410
that move deeply hurt me.

1213
00:50:43,550 --> 00:50:44,780
(Round 3 Movement Results)

1214
00:50:44,780 --> 00:50:48,150
(Ji Hoo, YunB, Jin Ho, Seong Beom,
Seung Yong, Keun Woo, Hye Seon, Sung Joo)

1215
00:50:49,550 --> 00:50:51,450
Round Four will begin now.

1216
00:50:52,350 --> 00:50:54,990
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1217
00:50:54,990 --> 00:50:57,390
(Seong Beom)

1218
00:51:07,240 --> 00:51:10,770
(Keun Woo humming)

1219
00:51:11,370 --> 00:51:15,040
(He heads straight into the Voting Room.)

1220
00:51:19,980 --> 00:51:21,220
Keun Woo,

1221
00:51:22,080 --> 00:51:24,650
place your card
in the area of your choice.

1222
00:51:25,790 --> 00:51:28,790
Keun Woo, you've placed Card Three
in Area D.

1223
00:51:28,790 --> 00:51:29,860
- Is that correct?
- Yes.

1224
00:51:30,590 --> 00:51:33,060
I simply have to make my own choices,
plan by myself,

1225
00:51:33,060 --> 00:51:34,560
and make a move by myself.

1226
00:51:34,860 --> 00:51:37,930
But I'm also calculating things.

1227
00:51:39,630 --> 00:51:42,800
I'm not sure if I want to leave
Sung Joo's car alone.

1228
00:51:42,800 --> 00:51:45,640
(Sung Joo's race car hasn't departed yet.)

1229
00:51:46,070 --> 00:51:47,210
Did he really bet on eighth place?

1230
00:51:47,340 --> 00:51:48,410
He might have.

1231
00:51:48,780 --> 00:51:50,250
Sung Joo's car also...

1232
00:51:50,250 --> 00:51:52,310
didn't move an inch.

1233
00:51:52,310 --> 00:51:55,520
I realized he bet on 7th or 8th.

1234
00:51:55,580 --> 00:51:57,490
I ate too much breakfast. I had a salad.

1235
00:52:06,390 --> 00:52:07,630
What's your predicted rank?

1236
00:52:08,060 --> 00:52:09,660
- What?
- What's your predicted rank?

1237
00:52:10,000 --> 00:52:11,200
Did you bet on eighth?

1238
00:52:11,200 --> 00:52:12,370
You look too relaxed.

1239
00:52:14,770 --> 00:52:16,170
You know what? Forget it.

1240
00:52:23,610 --> 00:52:27,220
Sung Joo, you've placed Card Three
in Area B.

1241
00:52:27,220 --> 00:52:28,220
(He bets a 3 on Area B.)

1242
00:52:28,220 --> 00:52:29,320
(Round 4 Betting Results)

1243
00:52:29,320 --> 00:52:30,720
All players have placed their bets.

1244
00:52:30,720 --> 00:52:32,290
(Sung Joo 3, Seung Yong 3, Keun Woo 3)

1245
00:52:32,390 --> 00:52:34,620
I will announce the betting results.

1246
00:52:35,020 --> 00:52:38,060
Area A has no winners.

1247
00:52:39,860 --> 00:52:43,370
Area B goes to Sung Joo.

1248
00:52:43,370 --> 00:52:45,270
(Sung Joo wins Area B.)

1249
00:52:45,400 --> 00:52:48,770
Area C goes to Seung Yong.

1250
00:52:49,700 --> 00:52:53,340
Area D goes to Keun Woo.

1251
00:52:53,340 --> 00:52:55,110
- Keun Woo is good at bidding.
- Another one?

1252
00:52:55,340 --> 00:52:58,710
Three wins! I might have a shot.

1253
00:52:58,710 --> 00:53:01,050
He has to be a genius.

1254
00:53:01,050 --> 00:53:02,150
He's good.

1255
00:53:04,020 --> 00:53:05,190
I'll remain as an observer this time.

1256
00:53:06,390 --> 00:53:08,260
I can't believe I won that bid.

1257
00:53:09,420 --> 00:53:11,960
You will now place your movement cards.

1258
00:53:12,130 --> 00:53:14,360
Sung Joo, please place your cards.

1259
00:53:18,300 --> 00:53:20,500
(He places a 3 in his slot.)

1260
00:53:23,040 --> 00:53:24,210
Everyone, get on someone's back.

1261
00:53:24,310 --> 00:53:25,470
- We should.
- Get on.

1262
00:53:25,470 --> 00:53:27,080
(He places a 3 in Hye Seon's slot.)

1263
00:53:29,840 --> 00:53:30,880
Which one?

1264
00:53:31,410 --> 00:53:33,880
(He places a 2 in Keun Woo's slot.)

1265
00:53:33,880 --> 00:53:35,320
Thank you very much.

1266
00:53:35,620 --> 00:53:37,720
Seung Yong, please place your cards.

1267
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:39,690
Move.

1268
00:53:41,060 --> 00:53:42,220
You got me out of the way.

1269
00:53:43,630 --> 00:53:46,130
(He places the remaining cards
in Seong Beom's and Ji Hoo's slots.)

1270
00:53:46,760 --> 00:53:49,200
Keun Woo, please place your cards.

1271
00:53:49,400 --> 00:53:50,500
Okay.

1272
00:53:51,400 --> 00:53:52,430
Let's find out.

1273
00:53:58,710 --> 00:54:01,580
(He places a 1 in his slot.)

1274
00:54:01,580 --> 00:54:02,780
I think I made a mistake.

1275
00:54:03,650 --> 00:54:04,710
I'll discard this one.

1276
00:54:05,880 --> 00:54:07,250
- He's so manly.
- So manly.

1277
00:54:08,150 --> 00:54:11,320
"Your precious card means nothing to me."

1278
00:54:11,590 --> 00:54:14,390
"You must be quick and firm
when you discard cards."

1279
00:54:14,690 --> 00:54:17,290
- I can't predict Keun Woo's next moves.
- All the movement cards have been placed.

1280
00:54:17,290 --> 00:54:18,590
He scares me.

1281
00:54:18,590 --> 00:54:20,460
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1282
00:54:20,460 --> 00:54:24,700
(Keun Woo, Seong Beom,
Hye Seon, and Sung Joo can move.)

1283
00:54:24,870 --> 00:54:26,800
The race cars will start moving.

1284
00:54:26,800 --> 00:54:28,000
(The race cars start moving.)

1285
00:54:28,000 --> 00:54:31,770
- Seong Beom, one space backward.
- Okay.

1286
00:54:31,770 --> 00:54:34,210
Hye Seon, you cannot move.

1287
00:54:34,210 --> 00:54:35,380
Okay.

1288
00:54:35,380 --> 00:54:37,780
Sung Joo, please pick your starting space.

1289
00:54:38,550 --> 00:54:40,180
Which one...

1290
00:54:40,180 --> 00:54:41,420
Seven!

1291
00:54:41,420 --> 00:54:43,490
Sung Joo, you've chosen Lane Seven.

1292
00:54:43,490 --> 00:54:46,420
I can't tell
if you're doing it on purpose.

1293
00:54:46,420 --> 00:54:47,720
- Right?
- He's...

1294
00:54:47,720 --> 00:54:50,390
- starting to confuse me.
- Two spaces forward and one space left.

1295
00:54:50,530 --> 00:54:54,000
(Sung Joo)

1296
00:54:54,160 --> 00:54:56,230
Keun Woo, one space forward...

1297
00:54:56,230 --> 00:54:58,070
and one space left.

1298
00:54:58,670 --> 00:54:59,670
Thanks.

1299
00:54:59,770 --> 00:55:02,300
Ji Hoo, you cannot move.

1300
00:55:02,300 --> 00:55:04,140
All players have completed their moves.

1301
00:55:04,370 --> 00:55:05,640
(Round 4 Movement Results)

1302
00:55:05,640 --> 00:55:08,540
(Ji Hoo, Keun Woo, YunB, Jin Ho, Sung Joo,
Seung Yong, Hye Seon, Seong Beom)

1303
00:55:08,610 --> 00:55:10,580
Round Five will begin now.

1304
00:55:10,780 --> 00:55:13,480
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1305
00:55:13,480 --> 00:55:14,680
(Jin Ho)

1306
00:55:15,820 --> 00:55:16,950
How should we use these cards?

1307
00:55:17,420 --> 00:55:19,750
We have to stop Ji Hoo,

1308
00:55:19,750 --> 00:55:22,690
get YunB away from us,
and move Seung Yong forward.

1309
00:55:22,690 --> 00:55:24,060
We have to do all three of these at once.

1310
00:55:24,390 --> 00:55:26,590
Who's going first?

1311
00:55:27,330 --> 00:55:28,560
I'm going first.

1312
00:55:29,000 --> 00:55:31,400
You'll place the cards first, right?

1313
00:55:31,570 --> 00:55:33,070
Yes, Hye Seon and I.

1314
00:55:36,170 --> 00:55:38,470
- Let's win Area B.
- Okay.

1315
00:55:39,740 --> 00:55:42,180
We put this card here.

1316
00:55:42,180 --> 00:55:43,180
(Seung Yong)

1317
00:55:43,180 --> 00:55:45,450
This one goes to Ji Hoo.

1318
00:55:45,850 --> 00:55:47,050
Give this one...

1319
00:55:47,050 --> 00:55:48,680
(Seung Yong, Ji Hoo)

1320
00:55:48,680 --> 00:55:49,850
to YunB.

1321
00:55:49,980 --> 00:55:51,790
Because we have to get this
out of the way.

1322
00:55:51,790 --> 00:55:53,590
(YunB, Jin Ho)

1323
00:55:54,360 --> 00:55:55,920
Tell Hye Seon to bet on Area C,

1324
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:57,760
and you and I will bet on this.

1325
00:55:58,890 --> 00:56:00,560
I'll bet a three on Area C.

1326
00:56:00,560 --> 00:56:01,630
Okay.

1327
00:56:06,530 --> 00:56:09,600
Hye Seon, you've placed Card Three
in Area C.

1328
00:56:10,140 --> 00:56:12,740
- The second one.
- Jin Ho...

1329
00:56:13,540 --> 00:56:16,640
Seong Beom, you've placed Card Four
in Area B.

1330
00:56:16,640 --> 00:56:18,810
Place your card
in the area of your choice.

1331
00:56:19,250 --> 00:56:20,720
Please move to the main hall.

1332
00:56:20,720 --> 00:56:21,750
(Keun Woo and Sung Joo finish betting.)

1333
00:56:21,750 --> 00:56:23,250
All players have placed their bets.

1334
00:56:23,850 --> 00:56:26,220
I will announce the betting results.

1335
00:56:27,120 --> 00:56:31,060
Area A goes to Ji Hoo.

1336
00:56:31,060 --> 00:56:32,160
Nice.

1337
00:56:32,930 --> 00:56:33,930
Area B...

1338
00:56:35,360 --> 00:56:37,970
goes to Keun Woo.

1339
00:56:39,330 --> 00:56:40,940
Four wins in a row?

1340
00:56:42,940 --> 00:56:46,410
Keun Woo, you've placed Card Five
in Area B.

1341
00:56:46,410 --> 00:56:47,410
(He bet a 5 on Area B.)

1342
00:56:47,410 --> 00:56:48,440
I won another one.

1343
00:56:48,440 --> 00:56:51,480
Do you think other people
will have a 5 in Round 5?

1344
00:56:51,710 --> 00:56:52,950
I don't think so.

1345
00:56:53,010 --> 00:56:54,420
They obviously used all of them.

1346
00:56:54,420 --> 00:56:57,290
I knew I'd win that area
the moment I placed a five.

1347
00:56:57,620 --> 00:57:01,020
It was insane. The evil second baseman.

1348
00:57:01,020 --> 00:57:03,320
He hit a home run every time
he was at bat. How is that possible?

1349
00:57:03,560 --> 00:57:05,360
A batter should wait to see...

1350
00:57:05,360 --> 00:57:06,730
if it's a ball or a strike.

1351
00:57:06,730 --> 00:57:09,630
But he hit a home run
every time he swung that bat.

1352
00:57:09,630 --> 00:57:11,070
I just...

1353
00:57:11,200 --> 00:57:12,730
couldn't compete.

1354
00:57:13,200 --> 00:57:14,840
Keun Woo is on a roll.

1355
00:57:14,840 --> 00:57:16,370
He's so good.

1356
00:57:17,310 --> 00:57:21,180
Area C goes to Hye Seon.

1357
00:57:21,180 --> 00:57:22,410
They could get in your way.

1358
00:57:23,310 --> 00:57:24,810
(Ji Hoo sighing)

1359
00:57:24,810 --> 00:57:26,150
We lost the reverse card,

1360
00:57:26,550 --> 00:57:28,750
which went to Team P3.

1361
00:57:28,880 --> 00:57:30,450
I was in danger.

1362
00:57:30,590 --> 00:57:34,660
Area D goes to YunB.

1363
00:57:34,890 --> 00:57:36,660
Nice.

1364
00:57:37,130 --> 00:57:39,290
How is Keun Woo so good at this?

1365
00:57:39,290 --> 00:57:41,030
- It makes no sense.
- That's awesome.

1366
00:57:41,030 --> 00:57:42,060
Jeez.

1367
00:57:42,330 --> 00:57:44,700
I won 4 out of 5 times.

1368
00:57:44,700 --> 00:57:46,100
That's incredible.

1369
00:57:46,200 --> 00:57:48,200
I'm reading your mind like an open book.

1370
00:57:48,670 --> 00:57:49,970
(Round 5 Betting Results)

1371
00:57:49,970 --> 00:57:53,510
(Ji Hoo 2, Keun Woo 5, Hye Seon 3, YunB 3)

1372
00:57:53,810 --> 00:57:56,640
You will now place your movement cards.

1373
00:57:56,950 --> 00:57:59,150
Hye Seon, please place your cards.

1374
00:58:01,580 --> 00:58:04,420
It looks like Keun Woo is joining them.

1375
00:58:09,620 --> 00:58:11,690
Are you and Keun Woo close?

1376
00:58:12,060 --> 00:58:13,390
- No.
- Not at all?

1377
00:58:13,390 --> 00:58:14,560
Why do you ask?

1378
00:58:15,500 --> 00:58:17,100
Doesn't it look like he's joining them?

1379
00:58:22,070 --> 00:58:23,140
What's your plan, Keun Woo?

1380
00:58:23,610 --> 00:58:24,810
- What?
- What's your plan?

1381
00:58:24,810 --> 00:58:26,670
I'm torn.

1382
00:58:26,670 --> 00:58:28,380
- What do you mean?
- I'm trying to decide.

1383
00:58:29,140 --> 00:58:30,810
I usually go straight in real life,

1384
00:58:31,750 --> 00:58:33,580
but I occasionally want
to take the scenic route.

1385
00:58:36,650 --> 00:58:39,190
It does feel good...

1386
00:58:39,190 --> 00:58:40,490
- to win 4 out of 5 bids.
- I know, right?

1387
00:58:40,490 --> 00:58:43,260
How did you bet
exactly the right amount every time?

1388
00:58:43,260 --> 00:58:44,530
That's so cool.

1389
00:58:45,060 --> 00:58:46,130
What are you going to do?

1390
00:58:46,330 --> 00:58:47,400
I can't decide.

1391
00:58:48,030 --> 00:58:49,660
Aren't you going to go forward?

1392
00:58:49,660 --> 00:58:50,670
Me?

1393
00:58:50,670 --> 00:58:51,800
I should.

1394
00:58:51,800 --> 00:58:52,870
Or you could give it to me.

1395
00:58:54,740 --> 00:58:55,900
Then...

1396
00:58:57,940 --> 00:59:00,240
- What I'm saying is...
- I think...

1397
00:59:00,640 --> 00:59:02,880
Could we ask Keun Woo to put this here?

1398
00:59:03,210 --> 00:59:04,210
Four?

1399
00:59:05,110 --> 00:59:06,280
That's not bad.

1400
00:59:06,610 --> 00:59:07,720
It was 25 percent, right?

1401
00:59:07,720 --> 00:59:09,180
- That one.
- What?

1402
00:59:09,180 --> 00:59:10,690
Get that yellow car out of the way.

1403
00:59:11,290 --> 00:59:13,290
- Whose car is it?
- YunB's.

1404
00:59:13,620 --> 00:59:14,960
Oh, it's YunB's?

1405
00:59:15,120 --> 00:59:16,220
And we'll take the blue one down.

1406
00:59:16,390 --> 00:59:17,390
He's too far ahead.

1407
00:59:17,390 --> 00:59:19,190
But the blue one isn't trying to go.

1408
00:59:19,490 --> 00:59:21,060
- He didn't have a chance.
- He just couldn't.

1409
00:59:21,060 --> 00:59:22,630
We crashed into him earlier.

1410
00:59:24,400 --> 00:59:27,800
I had to go as slowly as possible,

1411
00:59:27,800 --> 00:59:30,940
so I couldn't decide...

1412
00:59:30,940 --> 00:59:33,310
whether to turn it over, stop other cars,

1413
00:59:33,310 --> 00:59:34,580
or collide with them.

1414
00:59:35,910 --> 00:59:37,650
- Just...
- Who should I give the reverse to?

1415
00:59:38,610 --> 00:59:39,710
It's obvious.

1416
00:59:39,710 --> 00:59:42,050
Place it on the right side
of Ji Hoo's slot.

1417
00:59:45,820 --> 00:59:47,160
Ji Hoo is too far ahead of us.

1418
00:59:48,520 --> 00:59:49,590
Too far ahead.

1419
00:59:50,330 --> 00:59:53,390
(The reverse card goes to Ji Hoo.)

1420
00:59:56,560 --> 00:59:58,030
(Placing a 0 and a 3
in Seong Beom's slots)

1421
00:59:58,300 --> 01:00:00,370
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

1422
01:00:01,000 --> 01:00:02,070
Okay.

1423
01:00:02,540 --> 01:00:05,970
We can't have someone pull ahead
early in the game.

1424
01:00:07,710 --> 01:00:09,340
- Are you serious, Keun Woo?
- Yes.

1425
01:00:09,340 --> 01:00:10,510
You'll really do it?

1426
01:00:11,210 --> 01:00:12,510
- Go away.
- Will you really do it?

1427
01:00:12,510 --> 01:00:13,580
Let's see.

1428
01:00:15,050 --> 01:00:16,320
You'll...

1429
01:00:16,420 --> 01:00:18,090
Can you at least reduce it to two?

1430
01:00:19,120 --> 01:00:20,390
Reduce it to two...

1431
01:00:20,390 --> 01:00:23,320
(He places a 4 in Ji Hoo's slot.)

1432
01:00:23,390 --> 01:00:24,630
Nice.

1433
01:00:29,900 --> 01:00:32,430
I begged him, but he still placed a four.

1434
01:00:33,030 --> 01:00:35,340
The Majority Alliance I was worried about
has formed.

1435
01:00:35,740 --> 01:00:38,210
If they keep pulling me back
by 4 or 3 spaces,

1436
01:00:38,740 --> 01:00:40,140
I could be in real trouble.

1437
01:00:40,140 --> 01:00:42,780
In my mind, I still feel like...

1438
01:00:42,940 --> 01:00:44,280
the skin is nearer than the shirt.

1439
01:00:44,950 --> 01:00:47,650
I tried to help Team P3...

1440
01:00:47,650 --> 01:00:51,050
with their strategies a bit.

1441
01:00:51,520 --> 01:00:52,590
Let's see.

1442
01:00:53,090 --> 01:00:54,390
You could move it here.

1443
01:00:54,820 --> 01:00:56,790
You could give it to YunB or Hye Seon.

1444
01:00:56,790 --> 01:00:58,290
Anything would be fine.

1445
01:00:58,290 --> 01:01:01,430
YunB is having a fright.
He's scared of heights.

1446
01:01:01,660 --> 01:01:04,000
- What?
- You're scared of heights, YunB.

1447
01:01:04,000 --> 01:01:05,630
(YunB's car is on top of Jin Ho's car.)

1448
01:01:05,870 --> 01:01:07,170
Seung Yong.

1449
01:01:07,800 --> 01:01:08,800
Too bad.

1450
01:01:08,800 --> 01:01:10,140
(He places it in YunB's slot.)

1451
01:01:12,740 --> 01:01:15,380
You guys suddenly come to me
and butter me up.

1452
01:01:15,580 --> 01:01:16,810
You guys...

1453
01:01:18,150 --> 01:01:20,010
I felt like I became rich.

1454
01:01:20,110 --> 01:01:22,550
They came to me to ask a favor and so on.

1455
01:01:22,720 --> 01:01:24,620
This is nothing to me,

1456
01:01:24,720 --> 01:01:26,150
so I can place the cards...

1457
01:01:26,150 --> 01:01:28,060
without much thought.

1458
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:32,030
I just did it thinking about
Tae Gyun and Ji Min who had to leave.

1459
01:01:32,590 --> 01:01:34,830
Kang Ji Hoo, please place your cards.

1460
01:01:34,960 --> 01:01:37,730
In this case, there's nothing we can do.

1461
01:01:38,500 --> 01:01:39,600
Right.

1462
01:01:39,600 --> 01:01:41,200
We need to wait for the others
to move first.

1463
01:01:41,200 --> 01:01:42,540
Let's make this a total mess.

1464
01:01:43,140 --> 01:01:44,270
Two and three?

1465
01:01:45,470 --> 01:01:46,910
- Two and three?
- Yes.

1466
01:01:48,110 --> 01:01:49,410
- To you?
- Yes.

1467
01:01:49,740 --> 01:01:51,010
Okay. I'll do this.

1468
01:01:51,350 --> 01:01:52,580
Where should I place a one?

1469
01:01:52,910 --> 01:01:53,980
Me.

1470
01:01:54,580 --> 01:01:55,950
- Should I?
- Give it to Hye Seon.

1471
01:01:55,950 --> 01:01:57,090
We'll return you one next time.

1472
01:01:57,090 --> 01:01:58,520
Let's do that.

1473
01:01:58,690 --> 01:02:00,660
- How about Keun Woo?
- What do you want?

1474
01:02:00,660 --> 01:02:02,020
I don't want anything.

1475
01:02:02,390 --> 01:02:03,520
Just discard it.

1476
01:02:05,060 --> 01:02:06,130
Seriously.

1477
01:02:06,530 --> 01:02:08,160
Give it to me.

1478
01:02:08,660 --> 01:02:10,230
I'm at the starting line.

1479
01:02:10,530 --> 01:02:12,630
- This looks fine.
- If Seong Beom leaves, I'll be alone.

1480
01:02:14,000 --> 01:02:15,570
(He places the cards
in Seung Yong and Sung Joo's slots.)

1481
01:02:15,570 --> 01:02:16,740
- One, two, three.
- You are so mean.

1482
01:02:17,270 --> 01:02:19,240
YunB, please place your cards.

1483
01:02:19,670 --> 01:02:22,110
Should I push Jin Ho to the left?

1484
01:02:23,480 --> 01:02:24,580
With 1 and 3?

1485
01:02:25,050 --> 01:02:26,510
Who's moving first?

1486
01:02:27,520 --> 01:02:28,750
Jin Ho...

1487
01:02:29,080 --> 01:02:31,020
Since this is Round Six...

1488
01:02:31,020 --> 01:02:33,620
Good. You need to move first though.

1489
01:02:33,720 --> 01:02:36,560
(Jin Ho's car can't move
no matter what card they put in his slot.)

1490
01:02:36,820 --> 01:02:38,760
- That's a good idea.
- Like this.

1491
01:02:39,590 --> 01:02:42,200
(He places a 3 and a 1 in Jin Ho's slots.)

1492
01:02:42,800 --> 01:02:43,830
Two...

1493
01:02:45,270 --> 01:02:47,370
You could put a two in Sung Joo's slot.

1494
01:02:47,540 --> 01:02:50,170
Since Sung Joo plays alone,
he'd have predicted himself lower.

1495
01:02:53,910 --> 01:02:56,240
(He places the remaining card
in Sung Joo's slot.)

1496
01:02:56,380 --> 01:02:58,880
All the movement cards have been placed.

1497
01:02:58,910 --> 01:03:00,310
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1498
01:03:00,310 --> 01:03:04,190
(Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom, Jin Ho,
Sung Joo, and Seung Yong can move.)

1499
01:03:04,390 --> 01:03:06,590
The race cars will start moving now.

1500
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:09,020
Hong Jin Ho. You cannot move.

1501
01:03:09,290 --> 01:03:10,360
Too bad.

1502
01:03:10,860 --> 01:03:11,990
You can't move anyway.

1503
01:03:11,990 --> 01:03:13,260
Mine will be gone anyway.

1504
01:03:17,700 --> 01:03:20,640
I miscalculated.
I thought we were in Round Six.

1505
01:03:21,670 --> 01:03:22,670
I'm sorry.

1506
01:03:22,800 --> 01:03:23,910
It's okay.

1507
01:03:24,710 --> 01:03:28,480
Hyun Sung Joo,
1 space forward and 1 space left.

1508
01:03:29,640 --> 01:03:30,880
You're pulling ahead.

1509
01:03:32,350 --> 01:03:34,150
An underdog's rebellion.

1510
01:03:34,520 --> 01:03:38,290
Shin Seung Yong, 2 spaces forward
and 1 space right.

1511
01:03:38,820 --> 01:03:40,960
- Yes.
- So chummy.

1512
01:03:41,590 --> 01:03:44,160
Kang Ji Hoo, four spaces backward.

1513
01:03:45,390 --> 01:03:46,530
Yes, I'm in the lead.

1514
01:03:47,730 --> 01:03:50,300
YunB is racing fast.

1515
01:03:52,530 --> 01:03:54,640
Showing my intention to win...

1516
01:03:55,400 --> 01:03:56,870
might prove to be a bad mistake.

1517
01:03:57,070 --> 01:03:58,640
I resented Keun Woo.

1518
01:03:59,410 --> 01:04:01,040
YunB is racing fast.

1519
01:04:01,140 --> 01:04:03,040
- Isn't that a slipstream for YunB?
- You're right.

1520
01:04:03,040 --> 01:04:04,050
It is.

1521
01:04:05,410 --> 01:04:07,420
YunB wanted to stay behind.

1522
01:04:07,480 --> 01:04:10,220
YunB, booster activated.

1523
01:04:10,220 --> 01:04:12,120
You will start two spaces ahead.

1524
01:04:13,120 --> 01:04:16,390
One space forward and one space right.

1525
01:04:17,930 --> 01:04:19,360
(YunB takes the lead.)

1526
01:04:19,360 --> 01:04:20,760
It's not bad, actually.

1527
01:04:22,230 --> 01:04:24,170
I have no idea how it's going to go.

1528
01:04:24,170 --> 01:04:25,300
Me too. It's so difficult.

1529
01:04:25,300 --> 01:04:28,300
- It's completely different from just now.
- You need to factor in many things...

1530
01:04:28,340 --> 01:04:29,970
because you need to move others' cars too.

1531
01:04:29,970 --> 01:04:31,040
Right. This is fun.

1532
01:04:31,040 --> 01:04:33,840
Heo Seong Beom, three spaces right.

1533
01:04:34,540 --> 01:04:35,540
Ouch.

1534
01:04:35,980 --> 01:04:37,510
Flip over.

1535
01:04:37,680 --> 01:04:39,680
You've collided with the wall.

1536
01:04:40,650 --> 01:04:41,650
(Seong Beom's race car flipped over.)

1537
01:04:41,650 --> 01:04:44,990
Your race car has flipped over,
and you cannot move until the next round.

1538
01:04:44,990 --> 01:04:46,120
Okay.

1539
01:04:46,390 --> 01:04:49,690
I couldn't exactly go anywhere
with the other players around,

1540
01:04:50,090 --> 01:04:52,930
so I decided to crash into the wall.

1541
01:04:53,230 --> 01:04:56,060
When I do, I can't reverse either.

1542
01:04:56,060 --> 01:04:58,600
I can skip one round
without anyone messing with me.

1543
01:04:58,600 --> 01:05:00,700
So I decided to let it go...

1544
01:05:00,700 --> 01:05:02,300
and think about the next move.

1545
01:05:02,700 --> 01:05:04,170
(Round 5 Movement Results)

1546
01:05:04,170 --> 01:05:05,770
(Player, predicted rank)

1547
01:05:05,770 --> 01:05:07,410
(YunB, Sung Joo, Seung Yong, Ji Hoo,)

1548
01:05:07,410 --> 01:05:08,810
(Keun Woo, Jin Ho, Seong Beom, Hye Seon)

1549
01:05:09,210 --> 01:05:10,210
Goodness.

1550
01:05:12,580 --> 01:05:14,320
Seong Beom might've predicted himself
as a lower rank.

1551
01:05:15,280 --> 01:05:17,490
He wouldn't make
such an obvious mistake otherwise.

1552
01:05:17,490 --> 01:05:18,550
It's definitely not a mistake.

1553
01:05:18,550 --> 01:05:22,190
He moved 2 spaces forward
and will take a break for 1 round.

1554
01:05:24,660 --> 01:05:27,660
And Sung Joo definitely didn't
predict himself to be in first place.

1555
01:05:27,660 --> 01:05:30,000
- No.
- It'll be good...

1556
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:32,200
to make him first place.

1557
01:05:32,470 --> 01:05:34,840
Seong Beom might've predicted himself
a lower rank,

1558
01:05:34,840 --> 01:05:36,640
but not 7th or 8th place, I think.

1559
01:05:37,040 --> 01:05:38,710
So we could put him in that rank.

1560
01:05:39,310 --> 01:05:40,340
Let's see.

1561
01:05:41,140 --> 01:05:42,210
This is interesting.

1562
01:05:42,980 --> 01:05:44,510
What a nice, fun mess.

1563
01:05:46,410 --> 01:05:49,050
Keun Woo said he predicted sixth place.

1564
01:05:49,050 --> 01:05:50,080
That overlaps with me.

1565
01:05:52,150 --> 01:05:54,660
Heo Seong Beom,
choose your predicted rank.

1566
01:05:55,390 --> 01:05:56,860
I choose sixth.

1567
01:05:57,220 --> 01:05:58,260
I have a good feeling about it.

1568
01:05:58,260 --> 01:06:00,560
(Heo Seong Beom's predicted rank is 6th.)

1569
01:06:01,500 --> 01:06:04,670
(Keun Woo and Seong Beom talked
before placing the movement cards.)

1570
01:06:05,800 --> 01:06:08,270
I chose a lower rank.
I predicted myself as sixth.

1571
01:06:10,200 --> 01:06:12,370
(Seong Beom has the same predicted rank
as Keun Woo.)

1572
01:06:12,440 --> 01:06:13,510
He overlaps with you.

1573
01:06:17,110 --> 01:06:19,080
That explains why he's playing like that.

1574
01:06:19,080 --> 01:06:20,110
Yes.

1575
01:06:21,920 --> 01:06:25,020
Before Round Six starts,
the hidden rule will be revealed.

1576
01:06:27,220 --> 01:06:30,590
The hidden rule of Prediction Race is
changing the predictions.

1577
01:06:31,660 --> 01:06:35,060
After Round Six ends,
the player with the lowest rank...

1578
01:06:35,500 --> 01:06:38,270
can change their predicted rank once.

1579
01:06:38,470 --> 01:06:40,530
- Only the lowest rank? Who is it?
- Only the lowest rank?

1580
01:06:40,630 --> 01:06:42,640
(Currently in last place
is Choi Hye Seon.)

1581
01:06:43,100 --> 01:06:44,510
(4 candidates of the hidden rule)

1582
01:06:44,510 --> 01:06:45,840
(Heo Seong Beom, Hong Jin Ho,
Choi Hye Seon, Jeong Keun Woo)

1583
01:06:52,380 --> 01:06:54,320
It means nothing
unless you're in last place.

1584
01:06:54,580 --> 01:06:55,580
Change it?

1585
01:06:56,250 --> 01:06:58,050
Round Six will begin now.

1586
01:06:59,020 --> 01:07:01,890
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1587
01:07:01,890 --> 01:07:03,960
(Hye Seon)

1588
01:07:04,730 --> 01:07:06,690
- They'll give us new betting cards.
- Yes.

1589
01:07:08,260 --> 01:07:10,560
I can't move in this round.

1590
01:07:23,040 --> 01:07:26,080
Jeong Keun Woo, here is your betting card.

1591
01:07:26,080 --> 01:07:27,620
Thank you.

1592
01:07:31,090 --> 01:07:34,520
You've placed Card Four in Area D.

1593
01:07:34,520 --> 01:07:35,560
- Is that right?
- Yes.

1594
01:07:35,890 --> 01:07:38,160
- I want to...
- You can do that.

1595
01:07:38,160 --> 01:07:40,090
I want to take Area B.

1596
01:07:40,530 --> 01:07:41,530
- Area B?
- Yes.

1597
01:07:41,530 --> 01:07:43,860
It's easier for you to move that way.

1598
01:07:45,200 --> 01:07:47,230
I don't think...

1599
01:07:47,230 --> 01:07:50,400
people will bet this round aggressively.

1600
01:07:51,540 --> 01:07:52,970
Keun Woo already went inside.

1601
01:07:53,870 --> 01:07:55,640
We'll lose the moment we bet
on the same area as Keun Woo.

1602
01:07:57,340 --> 01:07:59,650
- He's really good at betting.
- How does betting a four on Area B sound?

1603
01:08:00,080 --> 01:08:01,250
Four on Area B?

1604
01:08:03,150 --> 01:08:05,190
We have time.
Let's think about it more together.

1605
01:08:05,290 --> 01:08:06,490
Yes, let's take it slow.

1606
01:08:06,890 --> 01:08:08,220
A isn't bad, but...

1607
01:08:08,220 --> 01:08:09,520
Which area will you choose?

1608
01:08:09,520 --> 01:08:11,360
I'll discard the lower one.

1609
01:08:12,230 --> 01:08:14,760
Shall we play this round individually?
So nobody knows what will happen.

1610
01:08:15,600 --> 01:08:17,670
I don't move first,

1611
01:08:17,970 --> 01:08:19,930
so I don't need to risk it by going to C.

1612
01:08:20,570 --> 01:08:23,770
I think B is the safe option.

1613
01:08:24,840 --> 01:08:27,980
Shin Seung Yong.
You've placed Card One in Area D.

1614
01:08:29,080 --> 01:08:32,150
Kang Ji Hoo.
You've placed Card One in Area C.

1615
01:08:32,150 --> 01:08:35,280
YunB. You've placed Card One in Area B.

1616
01:08:35,280 --> 01:08:36,420
- Is that right?
- Yes.

1617
01:08:37,890 --> 01:08:40,020
I bet a one on B.

1618
01:08:42,090 --> 01:08:45,230
They'll get in the way of
whoever they want, so it's pointless.

1619
01:08:46,830 --> 01:08:49,100
Seong Beom has very sharp ears.

1620
01:08:49,100 --> 01:08:50,830
- We need to speak softer.
- What?

1621
01:08:51,070 --> 01:08:53,500
Seong Beom has very sharp ears,
so we need to speak softer.

1622
01:08:54,200 --> 01:08:56,040
- And don't use gestures.
- Okay.

1623
01:09:03,510 --> 01:09:04,680
What will you do?

1624
01:09:05,150 --> 01:09:06,380
- What?
- What will you do?

1625
01:09:06,680 --> 01:09:09,580
My head hurts.
Listening to me won't help you anyway.

1626
01:09:10,420 --> 01:09:12,190
He's bluffing again.

1627
01:09:19,460 --> 01:09:22,830
Hyun Sung Joo.
You've placed Card Five in Area A.

1628
01:09:24,400 --> 01:09:27,270
Keun Woo. I'll lose
if I bet on the same area as you.

1629
01:09:27,270 --> 01:09:30,040
So just tell me which area I should avoid.

1630
01:09:31,110 --> 01:09:32,970
You might lose real bad.

1631
01:09:34,380 --> 01:09:35,580
I'll avoid that area.

1632
01:09:36,640 --> 01:09:39,380
I'll do this.

1633
01:09:39,380 --> 01:09:42,620
Choi Hye Seon.
You've placed Card Two in Area B.

1634
01:09:43,150 --> 01:09:44,350
I'll go big.

1635
01:09:45,220 --> 01:09:47,090
- Four.
- Hong Jin Ho.

1636
01:09:47,390 --> 01:09:49,620
You've placed Card Four in Area C.

1637
01:09:49,620 --> 01:09:52,860
Heo Seong Beom.
You've placed Card One in Area C.

1638
01:09:52,860 --> 01:09:54,460
- Is that right?
- Yes.

1639
01:09:55,300 --> 01:09:57,030
All players have placed their bets.

1640
01:09:57,400 --> 01:09:59,600
I will announce the betting results.

1641
01:10:00,270 --> 01:10:03,640
Area A goes to Hyun Sung Joo.

1642
01:10:04,610 --> 01:10:06,310
Area B goes to...

1643
01:10:06,310 --> 01:10:07,940
- Choi Hye Seon.
- Yes.

1644
01:10:07,940 --> 01:10:09,640
What? Lucky her.

1645
01:10:10,280 --> 01:10:13,350
Area C goes to Hong Jin Ho.

1646
01:10:14,280 --> 01:10:15,420
I actually got this?

1647
01:10:15,820 --> 01:10:18,590
Area D goes to Jeong Keun Woo.

1648
01:10:18,590 --> 01:10:20,250
You're incredible, Keun Woo.

1649
01:10:20,920 --> 01:10:21,990
Seriously.

1650
01:10:22,590 --> 01:10:23,720
Goodness.

1651
01:10:23,720 --> 01:10:25,090
What's happening?

1652
01:10:25,090 --> 01:10:26,230
He's a deity.

1653
01:10:26,590 --> 01:10:28,100
How did you do it?

1654
01:10:28,330 --> 01:10:31,170
Do I stink?

1655
01:10:31,230 --> 01:10:32,500
Do you avoid the areas I bet on?

1656
01:10:33,630 --> 01:10:35,170
- This is ridiculous.
- You're amazing.

1657
01:10:35,170 --> 01:10:36,900
- Do I stink?
- This is impossible.

1658
01:10:37,400 --> 01:10:39,370
It's as expected.

1659
01:10:39,770 --> 01:10:41,210
I'm the king of successful bids.

1660
01:10:41,810 --> 01:10:44,650
They started buzzing.

1661
01:10:45,580 --> 01:10:47,380
I didn't simply bid.

1662
01:10:47,850 --> 01:10:51,390
What cards are useless to them...

1663
01:10:51,420 --> 01:10:53,290
but useful to me?

1664
01:10:54,120 --> 01:10:55,490
- My gosh.
- You will now...

1665
01:10:55,490 --> 01:10:57,490
place your movement cards.

1666
01:10:57,490 --> 01:10:58,690
(Placing the movement cards)

1667
01:10:58,890 --> 01:11:00,660
Choi Hye Seon, please place your cards.

1668
01:11:00,660 --> 01:11:03,700
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1669
01:11:03,700 --> 01:11:04,830
Look.

1670
01:11:05,100 --> 01:11:06,700
What move will be the best?

1671
01:11:09,900 --> 01:11:11,670
You can move forward. Do you want to?

1672
01:11:12,570 --> 01:11:14,580
Yes, it doesn't matter.

1673
01:11:14,940 --> 01:11:16,980
- What's that?
- Should we move Ji Hoo...

1674
01:11:16,980 --> 01:11:18,850
right or left?

1675
01:11:18,850 --> 01:11:20,010
(Kang Ji Hoo)

1676
01:11:20,010 --> 01:11:21,750
- Right is better.
- Right is better, right?

1677
01:11:21,750 --> 01:11:23,720
- Yes.
- Then we'll do this.

1678
01:11:23,920 --> 01:11:24,950
Nice.

1679
01:11:24,950 --> 01:11:27,490
It's about time we move things around
to suit our needs.

1680
01:11:27,490 --> 01:11:30,320
Why don't we stop hiding...

1681
01:11:30,390 --> 01:11:32,690
and make our moves aggressively?

1682
01:11:33,890 --> 01:11:35,200
Sorry, Ji Hoo.

1683
01:11:35,760 --> 01:11:37,600
- Where should I place three?
- Should I go?

1684
01:11:38,600 --> 01:11:39,870
- You can go.
- We can do 1 and 3, right?

1685
01:11:39,870 --> 01:11:41,240
- Then you can pull ahead.
- Yes.

1686
01:11:41,240 --> 01:11:43,100
(Choi Hye Seon, 1, 3)

1687
01:11:43,100 --> 01:11:44,340
I'm no longer in last place.

1688
01:11:44,340 --> 01:11:46,310
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1689
01:11:46,310 --> 01:11:48,240
In Round Six, Hye Seon placed...

1690
01:11:48,240 --> 01:11:49,680
zero on my right slot.

1691
01:11:49,680 --> 01:11:52,450
Which means she wants me to flip over
to the left.

1692
01:11:52,450 --> 01:11:54,080
I was very grateful for it.

1693
01:11:54,080 --> 01:11:55,250
I want to flip over.

1694
01:11:55,250 --> 01:11:57,420
That way, they can't make me go backward.

1695
01:11:57,420 --> 01:11:58,520
I'm so glad.

1696
01:11:58,920 --> 01:12:01,790
I can flip over and defend one round.

1697
01:12:01,990 --> 01:12:03,260
Where will you place yours?

1698
01:12:03,760 --> 01:12:04,990
- What?
- Where will you place yours?

1699
01:12:05,330 --> 01:12:06,560
Hye Seon needs to place hers first.

1700
01:12:07,830 --> 01:12:09,030
Once she's done,

1701
01:12:09,030 --> 01:12:10,960
I can see which slots are still available.

1702
01:12:11,670 --> 01:12:13,370
The outer line means last place.

1703
01:12:13,900 --> 01:12:15,800
They're making Seong Beom place last.

1704
01:12:16,270 --> 01:12:17,840
You're very confident in your predictions.

1705
01:12:19,170 --> 01:12:20,270
How cocky.

1706
01:12:21,510 --> 01:12:22,880
I used to be like that.

1707
01:12:24,040 --> 01:12:26,610
Should I help or not?
I'll just do my own thing.

1708
01:12:26,610 --> 01:12:27,780
Is there a way?

1709
01:12:28,180 --> 01:12:29,280
I'll do my thing.

1710
01:12:30,780 --> 01:12:34,890
(Hyun Sung Joo, 2, 1)

1711
01:12:35,360 --> 01:12:37,490
I can't tell
how the game is going to play out.

1712
01:12:37,990 --> 01:12:39,790
You now have one minute left.

1713
01:12:39,790 --> 01:12:41,500
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1714
01:12:41,500 --> 01:12:43,530
(Hyun Sung Joo discards Movement Card 2.)

1715
01:12:43,530 --> 01:12:44,870
- What did he discard?
- Two.

1716
01:12:45,770 --> 01:12:47,570
- Three.
- Wasn't it two?

1717
01:12:47,570 --> 01:12:49,770
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1718
01:12:49,770 --> 01:12:50,940
I discarded two.

1719
01:12:52,140 --> 01:12:53,640
Let's see.

1720
01:12:54,680 --> 01:12:55,780
It's my turn, right?

1721
01:12:55,940 --> 01:12:58,150
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

1722
01:13:04,180 --> 01:13:05,220
My gosh.

1723
01:13:05,220 --> 01:13:06,490
(Jeong Keun Woo, 1 and reverse)

1724
01:13:06,490 --> 01:13:07,550
What?

1725
01:13:08,620 --> 01:13:10,090
You want to place last?

1726
01:13:10,090 --> 01:13:11,590
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1727
01:13:11,590 --> 01:13:14,530
No. I'm going to cause a ruckus.

1728
01:13:16,600 --> 01:13:17,930
Please help me.

1729
01:13:19,100 --> 01:13:21,470
It's meaningless anyway.
I'll change everything.

1730
01:13:22,370 --> 01:13:23,500
You take it, Jin Ho.

1731
01:13:23,500 --> 01:13:25,810
(He places Movement Card 3
in Jin Ho's R slot.)

1732
01:13:26,470 --> 01:13:28,840
Hong Jin Ho, please place your cards.

1733
01:13:29,780 --> 01:13:32,580
I'll think about who I should give
the remaining cards to.

1734
01:13:32,750 --> 01:13:33,810
For now...

1735
01:13:34,580 --> 01:13:36,420
Place yours first.

1736
01:13:36,420 --> 01:13:38,120
We have three minutes to think.

1737
01:13:38,590 --> 01:13:39,950
Jin Ho, you have a three in your slot.

1738
01:13:41,620 --> 01:13:43,590
(His friend Keun Woo placed a 3
in his slot.)

1739
01:13:43,590 --> 01:13:45,290
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1740
01:13:45,290 --> 01:13:48,000
Keun Woo. Did you help me?

1741
01:13:48,730 --> 01:13:50,200
- No.
- Or do you hate me?

1742
01:13:50,330 --> 01:13:52,900
I wanted to add variables
to your calculations.

1743
01:13:52,900 --> 01:13:55,340
He decided my moves for me.

1744
01:13:55,340 --> 01:13:56,700
- Yes.
- You...

1745
01:13:56,700 --> 01:13:58,740
Don't offend me, or you'll all die.

1746
01:13:58,740 --> 01:14:00,510
I won 5 out of 6 bids.

1747
01:14:01,410 --> 01:14:02,440
Darn it.

1748
01:14:03,110 --> 01:14:05,880
You guys... There are so many variables.

1749
01:14:05,880 --> 01:14:08,520
(Round 6, Hye Seon, Sung Joo,
Keun Woo, Jin Ho)

1750
01:14:08,520 --> 01:14:10,850
(Hong Jin Ho, L and 3)

1751
01:14:10,850 --> 01:14:12,450
(Hong Jin Ho, 4, 3)

1752
01:14:12,950 --> 01:14:14,250
What will you do?

1753
01:14:14,250 --> 01:14:15,390
- Discard?
- Me?

1754
01:14:15,390 --> 01:14:16,990
Seung Yong? YunB?

1755
01:14:17,120 --> 01:14:18,130
Discard!

1756
01:14:19,860 --> 01:14:22,160
What's wrong with you?

1757
01:14:22,860 --> 01:14:24,430
Get you a bit excited.

1758
01:14:25,600 --> 01:14:27,000
I almost got excited.

1759
01:14:27,300 --> 01:14:28,570
Get you a bit excited.

1760
01:14:29,300 --> 01:14:30,500
This is fun.

1761
01:14:32,310 --> 01:14:33,540
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1762
01:14:33,540 --> 01:14:36,080
All the movement cards have been placed.

1763
01:14:36,410 --> 01:14:38,780
The race cars will start moving now.

1764
01:14:38,780 --> 01:14:40,710
I can't tell how they'll change.

1765
01:14:40,710 --> 01:14:41,720
(Race cars start moving.)

1766
01:14:41,780 --> 01:14:43,620
Choi Hye Seon, one space forward...

1767
01:14:43,620 --> 01:14:45,450
and two spaces right.

1768
01:14:45,720 --> 01:14:47,150
There.

1769
01:14:47,150 --> 01:14:48,990
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1770
01:14:48,990 --> 01:14:50,860
Hyun Sung Joo, one space forward,

1771
01:14:50,860 --> 01:14:52,660
and one space left.

1772
01:14:52,890 --> 01:14:54,230
He's pulling ahead.

1773
01:14:54,900 --> 01:14:56,000
Yes.

1774
01:14:56,360 --> 01:14:58,670
Jeong Keun Woo, one space backward.

1775
01:14:58,670 --> 01:15:00,630
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

1776
01:15:00,630 --> 01:15:02,770
Hong Jin Ho, booster activated.

1777
01:15:02,770 --> 01:15:04,610
You will start two spaces ahead.

1778
01:15:06,210 --> 01:15:09,080
Three spaces forward, and one space left.

1779
01:15:09,780 --> 01:15:11,610
(Hyun Sung Joo)

1780
01:15:11,880 --> 01:15:12,950
What would you like, Sung Joo?

1781
01:15:12,950 --> 01:15:14,850
Should I move or stay?

1782
01:15:15,720 --> 01:15:17,120
- Do whatever you want.
- Whatever I want?

1783
01:15:17,120 --> 01:15:19,020
You've collided with Sung Joo's race car.

1784
01:15:19,390 --> 01:15:22,790
I wasn't targeting Sung Joo specifically.

1785
01:15:22,960 --> 01:15:25,460
He was just on the way.
So I got on his car.

1786
01:15:25,660 --> 01:15:27,130
You can't plan this ahead...

1787
01:15:27,690 --> 01:15:30,630
because you need to see
how others arrange the orders...

1788
01:15:30,630 --> 01:15:32,870
and how the cars move.

1789
01:15:33,230 --> 01:15:35,200
You can't plan ahead.
That's just how the game is.

1790
01:15:36,700 --> 01:15:38,510
All players have completed their moves.

1791
01:15:38,510 --> 01:15:39,870
(Round 6 movements completed)

1792
01:15:39,870 --> 01:15:40,970
Next round onward,

1793
01:15:40,970 --> 01:15:43,280
Heo Seong Beom's race car can move.

1794
01:15:43,280 --> 01:15:45,580
- Hurrah.
- Good for you.

1795
01:15:47,810 --> 01:15:50,850
Jeong Keun Woo,
who is in last place for Round Six,

1796
01:15:51,290 --> 01:15:53,490
can change your predicted rank.

1797
01:15:54,690 --> 01:15:55,760
The predicted rank...

1798
01:15:56,760 --> 01:15:58,160
You need to change it, right?

1799
01:15:58,430 --> 01:15:59,860
- I can change it however I want, right?
- Yes.

1800
01:16:00,990 --> 01:16:03,930
Was today's hidden rule made for Keun Woo?

1801
01:16:05,400 --> 01:16:09,000
"The hidden rule.
The person in last place..."

1802
01:16:09,300 --> 01:16:11,770
"can change their predicted rank."
When I heard that,

1803
01:16:11,970 --> 01:16:15,080
I decided to win the bid,

1804
01:16:15,580 --> 01:16:18,450
use a reverse card, become last place,

1805
01:16:18,810 --> 01:16:22,750
and change my predicted rank.

1806
01:16:23,420 --> 01:16:24,580
Jeong Keun Woo.

1807
01:16:24,950 --> 01:16:26,990
Will you change your predicted rank?

1808
01:16:27,650 --> 01:16:29,720
I'll change it to seventh place.

1809
01:16:30,590 --> 01:16:33,630
When I'm in 7th place,
I just need to be mindful of 8th place.

1810
01:16:33,630 --> 01:16:36,830
But when I'm in 6th place, I need to keep
both 7th and 8th places in check.

1811
01:16:37,160 --> 01:16:40,570
So I planned to move one space backward...

1812
01:16:40,570 --> 01:16:42,670
and change my predicted rank
to seventh place.

1813
01:16:43,070 --> 01:16:44,270
(Round 7, Sung Joo)

1814
01:16:44,270 --> 01:16:46,170
Round Seven will begin now.

1815
01:16:47,010 --> 01:16:49,710
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1816
01:16:51,550 --> 01:16:52,910
This is really hard.

1817
01:16:53,580 --> 01:16:55,220
I can't predict what will happen at all.

1818
01:17:00,220 --> 01:17:02,160
Sung Joo finds this situation
uncomfortable.

1819
01:17:02,690 --> 01:17:04,590
- I'm happy.
- Jin Ho needs to move.

1820
01:17:04,590 --> 01:17:05,830
I'll do what I can.

1821
01:17:06,760 --> 01:17:08,160
(Sung Joo's car is under Jin Ho's.)

1822
01:17:08,160 --> 01:17:09,900
Sung Joo resents Jin Ho yet again today.

1823
01:17:11,200 --> 01:17:12,370
I've never resented him.

1824
01:17:12,530 --> 01:17:14,230
I was grateful yesterday,
and I'm grateful today.

1825
01:17:16,640 --> 01:17:19,140
It's my turn. I'll start.

1826
01:17:24,850 --> 01:17:25,980
Where did you bet on?

1827
01:17:25,980 --> 01:17:27,150
- I'll avoid you.
- Area D.

1828
01:17:27,910 --> 01:17:30,920
I used a low card. No need to go big now.

1829
01:17:32,220 --> 01:17:33,320
It's not necessary yet.

1830
01:17:33,320 --> 01:17:34,960
(YunB wants to save up
on his betting cards.)

1831
01:17:34,960 --> 01:17:36,060
I'll stay still.

1832
01:17:41,660 --> 01:17:43,430
- Do you want to move forward?
- Yes.

1833
01:17:43,800 --> 01:17:45,830
If you don't move,
my booster will be activated.

1834
01:17:46,270 --> 01:17:48,100
- I'll move no matter what.
- You'll move no matter what?

1835
01:17:48,100 --> 01:17:49,800
- You'll move no matter what?
- No matter what.

1836
01:17:50,140 --> 01:17:52,210
- Don't stop me.
- And...

1837
01:17:52,210 --> 01:17:53,970
Hye Seon will step on you.

1838
01:17:54,570 --> 01:17:56,410
Poor Ji Hoo. Is he crying?

1839
01:17:57,740 --> 01:17:59,810
Ji Hoo... A cheetah always smiles.

1840
01:17:59,980 --> 01:18:01,310
It can run later.

1841
01:18:01,550 --> 01:18:03,520
How philosophical.

1842
01:18:04,850 --> 01:18:05,950
Let's sit.

1843
01:18:06,420 --> 01:18:07,720
We need to plan.

1844
01:18:08,890 --> 01:18:10,020
We have no time to waste.

1845
01:18:11,690 --> 01:18:14,060
Which cards should we get? They...

1846
01:18:14,060 --> 01:18:15,400
If you were them,
which cards would you go for?

1847
01:18:15,700 --> 01:18:20,000
I think they'll go for B or C.

1848
01:18:21,030 --> 01:18:24,170
One of us could go
for a less competitive area,

1849
01:18:24,500 --> 01:18:26,270
and two could bet on the same area...

1850
01:18:26,270 --> 01:18:28,510
to support one of us.

1851
01:18:28,510 --> 01:18:29,780
Like what we did just now.

1852
01:18:30,080 --> 01:18:31,610
I'll bet a one on this.

1853
01:18:31,610 --> 01:18:33,850
Later, as we get closer to Round Ten,

1854
01:18:34,050 --> 01:18:35,880
we'll need cards with higher numbers.

1855
01:18:36,280 --> 01:18:38,550
Everyone seems to be saving up
on higher cards.

1856
01:18:38,820 --> 01:18:40,990
We need to use Card One sooner or later,

1857
01:18:40,990 --> 01:18:42,620
so we'll have to give up on one round.
We don't have a choice.

1858
01:18:43,790 --> 01:18:46,260
Seung Yong went 2nd in Round 7,

1859
01:18:46,260 --> 01:18:48,230
so he could lead the bets.

1860
01:18:48,230 --> 01:18:49,730
It was a very important moment.

1861
01:18:50,500 --> 01:18:51,670
Shin Seung Yong.

1862
01:18:51,670 --> 01:18:53,770
You've placed Card Four in Area B.

1863
01:18:53,900 --> 01:18:56,100
Seung Yong bet Card Four,

1864
01:18:56,100 --> 01:18:58,670
and I discarded my card.

1865
01:19:00,140 --> 01:19:01,270
Kang Ji Hoo.

1866
01:19:01,270 --> 01:19:03,380
You've placed Card Two in Area A.

1867
01:19:07,010 --> 01:19:08,010
You look relaxed.

1868
01:19:08,010 --> 01:19:09,020
- Sorry?
- You look relaxed.

1869
01:19:09,020 --> 01:19:10,150
Right?

1870
01:19:10,480 --> 01:19:12,650
It's fascinating.
How did I win all the bids?

1871
01:19:14,860 --> 01:19:16,660
- It is pretty fascinating.
- Right?

1872
01:19:16,660 --> 01:19:17,720
It's impossible.

1873
01:19:17,720 --> 01:19:20,090
I'm playing all by myself,

1874
01:19:20,090 --> 01:19:21,930
and I won 5 out of 6 bids.

1875
01:19:22,260 --> 01:19:24,000
Sometimes,

1876
01:19:24,530 --> 01:19:26,100
thinking too much doesn't help.

1877
01:19:26,100 --> 01:19:27,200
Yes.

1878
01:19:27,570 --> 01:19:29,100
A straightforward approach
works best sometimes.

1879
01:19:31,740 --> 01:19:34,510
Here are the betting results
of each area in Round Seven.

1880
01:19:34,510 --> 01:19:36,140
(Round 7 Betting Results)

1881
01:19:37,440 --> 01:19:40,010
Area A has no winners.

1882
01:19:40,780 --> 01:19:43,250
You will now place your movement cards.

1883
01:19:44,220 --> 01:19:46,190
Shin Seung Yong, please place your cards.

1884
01:19:47,250 --> 01:19:48,460
What will you do?

1885
01:19:48,960 --> 01:19:51,320
If you look at this...

1886
01:19:51,590 --> 01:19:52,660
If you don't move,

1887
01:19:52,660 --> 01:19:54,390
you'll be moved three spaces backward.

1888
01:19:54,930 --> 01:19:56,000
Hold on.

1889
01:19:56,000 --> 01:19:58,060
Whatever card I use on you,
you'll flip over.

1890
01:20:00,270 --> 01:20:01,470
I think that's better.

1891
01:20:01,670 --> 01:20:02,700
You want that?

1892
01:20:03,940 --> 01:20:06,410
Seung Yong made me flip over
to the left with Card Four.

1893
01:20:06,410 --> 01:20:08,840
And he moved forward using 2 pieces
of Card 2.

1894
01:20:09,780 --> 01:20:11,680
Seung Yong is pulling ahead.

1895
01:20:15,850 --> 01:20:18,250
Heo Seong Beom, please place your cards.

1896
01:20:19,020 --> 01:20:21,760
We can use this together
because we're next to each other.

1897
01:20:21,760 --> 01:20:24,160
You can do as you like.

1898
01:20:25,290 --> 01:20:26,660
The attack...

1899
01:20:27,390 --> 01:20:29,530
If you use a three...

1900
01:20:29,930 --> 01:20:31,430
Here's Seung Yong and here's Ji Hoo.

1901
01:20:31,430 --> 01:20:34,300
(The spaces Seung Yong and Ji Hoo
will move to)

1902
01:20:34,830 --> 01:20:36,200
Or you can get on top of Seung Yong's car.

1903
01:20:36,400 --> 01:20:38,240
- I can do that.
- Yes, you can.

1904
01:20:38,910 --> 01:20:39,940
Should I do that?

1905
01:20:39,940 --> 01:20:41,010
(Hye Seon can collide into Seung Yong
by using Seong Beom and Jin Ho's Card 3s.)

1906
01:20:41,110 --> 01:20:42,340
Using 2 Card 3s?

1907
01:20:42,340 --> 01:20:43,910
I'll go this way.

1908
01:20:43,910 --> 01:20:45,050
Two and one.

1909
01:20:46,150 --> 01:20:47,610
- You get it, right?
- Okay.

1910
01:20:48,320 --> 01:20:50,180
You now have one minute left.

1911
01:20:50,480 --> 01:20:51,650
I'll do that.

1912
01:20:51,950 --> 01:20:53,020
- Okay.
- Okay.

1913
01:20:55,820 --> 01:20:57,920
You have 30 seconds left.

1914
01:20:59,630 --> 01:21:01,260
Who wants to reverse?

1915
01:21:02,460 --> 01:21:03,630
Seung Yong.

1916
01:21:03,900 --> 01:21:05,100
You want to reverse, Seung Yong?

1917
01:21:05,100 --> 01:21:06,230
There's no slot left.

1918
01:21:06,870 --> 01:21:08,300
Time's up.

1919
01:21:08,300 --> 01:21:09,400
It's discarded.

1920
01:21:09,400 --> 01:21:11,240
(Heo Seong Beom's reverse card
is discarded.)

1921
01:21:11,540 --> 01:21:13,810
Hong Jin Ho, please place your cards.

1922
01:21:13,970 --> 01:21:15,240
Then...

1923
01:21:15,240 --> 01:21:16,310
That one.

1924
01:21:16,310 --> 01:21:18,180
If you don't have a card, go away.

1925
01:21:20,180 --> 01:21:21,480
Hye Seon...

1926
01:21:21,720 --> 01:21:23,720
Hye Seon is racing fast.

1927
01:21:25,920 --> 01:21:27,050
Move forward.

1928
01:21:28,220 --> 01:21:30,220
You've already discussed beforehand.

1929
01:21:30,620 --> 01:21:31,830
We're double-checking.

1930
01:21:31,860 --> 01:21:33,460
I will just...

1931
01:21:33,490 --> 01:21:35,400
- Watch your mouth.
- Please.

1932
01:21:35,400 --> 01:21:36,900
I only moved two spaces...

1933
01:21:36,900 --> 01:21:38,230
in three hours. Don't touch me.

1934
01:21:38,330 --> 01:21:39,400
Give me one.

1935
01:21:39,400 --> 01:21:40,800
- What?
- I can't move anyway.

1936
01:21:40,930 --> 01:21:41,970
No.

1937
01:21:42,100 --> 01:21:43,140
Sung Joo can't move anyway.

1938
01:21:43,140 --> 01:21:44,700
You can't move unless I do.

1939
01:21:45,040 --> 01:21:46,370
But I don't plan to move.

1940
01:21:46,470 --> 01:21:47,570
Why?

1941
01:21:48,340 --> 01:21:49,680
Or give it to YunB.

1942
01:21:49,940 --> 01:21:51,480
YunB feels upset at being left out.

1943
01:21:51,950 --> 01:21:53,950
But he has no plans to move.

1944
01:21:54,380 --> 01:21:56,020
Like this. Go big.

1945
01:21:56,150 --> 01:21:57,580
(He places 0 in YunB's slot.)

1946
01:21:57,580 --> 01:21:58,590
Go big.

1947
01:21:58,590 --> 01:21:59,590
(He places 0 in YunB's slot.)

1948
01:21:59,850 --> 01:22:02,590
You won't give it to your friend.

1949
01:22:03,460 --> 01:22:05,290
It's a bad card.

1950
01:22:05,290 --> 01:22:06,960
- It's a bad card?
- It's a bad card.

1951
01:22:07,160 --> 01:22:08,260
It's a bad card?

1952
01:22:08,500 --> 01:22:09,560
Seriously.

1953
01:22:10,900 --> 01:22:13,400
All the movement cards have been placed.

1954
01:22:13,400 --> 01:22:15,640
(Ji Hoo, Seong Beom, Hye Seon,
and Seung Yong can move.)

1955
01:22:15,970 --> 01:22:18,370
The race cars will start moving now.

1956
01:22:18,370 --> 01:22:19,410
(Race cars start moving.)

1957
01:22:19,640 --> 01:22:22,140
Shin Seung Yong, two spaces forward.

1958
01:22:22,980 --> 01:22:24,110
Yes.

1959
01:22:25,010 --> 01:22:27,880
Kang Ji Hoo, four spaces left.

1960
01:22:28,050 --> 01:22:29,620
You've collided into the wall.

1961
01:22:29,620 --> 01:22:31,280
Your race car has flipped over,

1962
01:22:31,280 --> 01:22:33,390
and you cannot move until the next round.

1963
01:22:34,890 --> 01:22:36,860
Heo Seong Beom, one space forward,

1964
01:22:36,860 --> 01:22:38,560
and one space left.

1965
01:22:38,730 --> 01:22:40,130
Does it mean
Hye Seon activates her booster?

1966
01:22:41,360 --> 01:22:42,730
Get on my back.

1967
01:22:43,660 --> 01:22:46,030
Choi Hye Seon, booster activated.

1968
01:22:46,030 --> 01:22:48,100
You will start two spaces ahead.

1969
01:22:48,500 --> 01:22:50,000
Get on Seung Yong's back.

1970
01:22:50,570 --> 01:22:52,410
Three spaces forward.

1971
01:22:53,170 --> 01:22:55,380
- Get on it.
- Vroom.

1972
01:22:56,240 --> 01:22:57,310
- You've collided...
- It's carpool.

1973
01:22:57,310 --> 01:22:58,350
with Seung Yong's race car.

1974
01:22:58,350 --> 01:22:59,450
Oh, my gosh.

1975
01:23:00,180 --> 01:23:01,310
- We move forward regardless.
- All players have...

1976
01:23:01,310 --> 01:23:02,550
- How fascinating.
- completed their moves.

1977
01:23:03,080 --> 01:23:04,850
- This is interesting.
- Right?

1978
01:23:04,850 --> 01:23:06,620
Things are getting interesting.

1979
01:23:08,390 --> 01:23:10,120
Let's go win the bid.

1980
01:23:11,390 --> 01:23:13,490
Round Eight will begin now.

1981
01:23:14,160 --> 01:23:17,030
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

1982
01:23:17,030 --> 01:23:18,400
(Round 8, Seung Yong)

1983
01:23:19,070 --> 01:23:22,070
Things are starting to get harder.

1984
01:23:22,700 --> 01:23:24,300
I'm getting a headache.

1985
01:23:26,040 --> 01:23:28,710
I'm so envious of Keun Woo.

1986
01:23:28,710 --> 01:23:30,180
For us,

1987
01:23:30,910 --> 01:23:32,080
it doesn't really matter...

1988
01:23:32,080 --> 01:23:33,850
- if we make a move or not.
- Right.

1989
01:23:33,850 --> 01:23:35,010
They're the ones who need to start moving.

1990
01:23:35,050 --> 01:23:37,020
They must be discussing...

1991
01:23:37,380 --> 01:23:41,450
whether to defend the reverse card or not.

1992
01:23:42,990 --> 01:23:46,660
Hye Seon, Seong Beom, and Jin Ho.

1993
01:23:46,660 --> 01:23:47,860
I still can't figure out...

1994
01:23:47,860 --> 01:23:50,030
who predicted higher rank
and who predicted lower.

1995
01:23:50,760 --> 01:23:52,770
- What do you think?
- Sorry?

1996
01:23:52,770 --> 01:23:54,000
What do you think?

1997
01:23:54,000 --> 01:23:55,170
I'm not sure either.

1998
01:23:55,240 --> 01:23:56,340
But...

1999
01:23:56,570 --> 01:23:59,910
Seong Beom must've predicted
2nd, 3rd, or 4th place.

2000
01:24:00,210 --> 01:24:02,610
I think that's what he'll do,
given his personality.

2001
01:24:04,440 --> 01:24:06,680
The typical move would be...

2002
01:24:07,510 --> 01:24:09,220
Seong Beom and Jin Ho
predicting higher ranks...

2003
01:24:09,220 --> 01:24:11,520
and Hye Seon predicting a lower rank.

2004
01:24:11,520 --> 01:24:13,290
I think it's their typical move.

2005
01:24:14,090 --> 01:24:17,160
But seeing how Hye Seon is pulling ahead,

2006
01:24:17,690 --> 01:24:19,230
I'm starting to think I might be wrong.

2007
01:24:19,230 --> 01:24:20,460
They're probably doing what we're doing.

2008
01:24:20,460 --> 01:24:22,730
They don't play aggressively at first
to fool the others...

2009
01:24:22,730 --> 01:24:23,760
and...

2010
01:24:24,130 --> 01:24:26,100
Either the ranks early in the game
are not important,

2011
01:24:26,100 --> 01:24:28,370
or they're making strange moves
to hide their intentions.

2012
01:24:28,470 --> 01:24:31,640
That's why the last round is important
for me.

2013
01:24:32,510 --> 01:24:34,440
It's not bad for Rounds 18 and 19
because YunB and I are the 1st players.

2014
01:24:34,470 --> 01:24:35,880
But I'm worried about this.

2015
01:24:35,880 --> 01:24:37,710
(He's worried that the 1st player for
Round 20, the final round, is Seong Beom.)

2016
01:24:37,710 --> 01:24:39,280
We must stop them in this round.

2017
01:24:39,550 --> 01:24:42,320
For now, I'll stay as neutral as I can...

2018
01:24:42,320 --> 01:24:43,920
and support you if I can.

2019
01:24:44,080 --> 01:24:46,750
At the end,

2020
01:24:46,750 --> 01:24:49,690
it's best to work with YunB.

2021
01:24:49,960 --> 01:24:51,120
I'll get going.

2022
01:24:56,730 --> 01:24:59,730
Here are the betting results
of each area in Round Eight.

2023
01:24:59,730 --> 01:25:01,370
(Round 8 Betting Results)

2024
01:25:01,500 --> 01:25:02,940
The winners are spread out evenly.

2025
01:25:04,040 --> 01:25:05,570
Let's see what we can do.

2026
01:25:07,040 --> 01:25:09,310
I have no idea what's going to happen.

2027
01:25:10,840 --> 01:25:13,010
I'll support you until mid-to-late game,

2028
01:25:13,010 --> 01:25:14,610
so help me just once later in the game.

2029
01:25:14,610 --> 01:25:15,680
You bet.

2030
01:25:16,650 --> 01:25:19,320
You will now place your movement cards.

2031
01:25:20,220 --> 01:25:22,320
Shin Seung Yong, please place your cards.

2032
01:25:24,260 --> 01:25:25,930
Nyom nyom.

2033
01:25:26,030 --> 01:25:27,890
Nyom nyom.

2034
01:25:29,300 --> 01:25:31,500
Do allow me to move now.

2035
01:25:33,130 --> 01:25:34,600
I've been parked for too long.

2036
01:25:34,930 --> 01:25:36,940
Right. You need to get rid of Hye Seon.

2037
01:25:36,970 --> 01:25:38,640
- Waste of fuel...
- Why get rid of me?

2038
01:25:39,410 --> 01:25:40,870
From Seung Yong's perspective, I mean.

2039
01:25:41,010 --> 01:25:42,110
That's right.

2040
01:25:42,480 --> 01:25:43,840
- I will...
- Wise choice.

2041
01:25:43,840 --> 01:25:46,380
send YunB forward
and make Keun Woo's ranking go up.

2042
01:25:51,920 --> 01:25:53,190
(Jeong Keun Woo, 2, 3)

2043
01:25:53,190 --> 01:25:54,690
(YunB, 0, 1)

2044
01:25:55,150 --> 01:25:56,190
My gosh.

2045
01:25:56,590 --> 01:25:58,460
Keun Woo's choices are gone.

2046
01:25:59,030 --> 01:26:01,490
You've ruined...

2047
01:26:01,490 --> 01:26:03,430
my plan.

2048
01:26:03,430 --> 01:26:05,730
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

2049
01:26:06,770 --> 01:26:07,900
I want to move forward too.

2050
01:26:07,900 --> 01:26:10,040
I was thinking about that.

2051
01:26:12,340 --> 01:26:13,870
That looks good.

2052
01:26:14,610 --> 01:26:15,810
Let's go with 3 and 3.

2053
01:26:16,110 --> 01:26:17,410
I'm thinking of doing that
and messing up the whole thing.

2054
01:26:17,410 --> 01:26:18,950
- Three collisions.
- Three burgers?

2055
01:26:18,980 --> 01:26:20,550
- Three burgers.
- Not there.

2056
01:26:20,550 --> 01:26:22,420
- Two and three look nice too.
- Why're you doing this?

2057
01:26:22,420 --> 01:26:23,880
- Let's go with 3 and 3.
- Why?

2058
01:26:23,880 --> 01:26:25,490
- No.
- Move Hye Seon and Jin Ho.

2059
01:26:25,490 --> 01:26:27,590
Keun Woo, I need a three too.

2060
01:26:28,090 --> 01:26:30,220
- Hold on.
- I could make use of the three.

2061
01:26:30,620 --> 01:26:32,030
- Everyone.
- You guys.

2062
01:26:32,030 --> 01:26:34,630
- Today's key is Keun Woo.
- Hold on.

2063
01:26:34,630 --> 01:26:36,960
You demand the cards from me...

2064
01:26:36,960 --> 01:26:38,770
without giving me a single cent.

2065
01:26:38,970 --> 01:26:40,630
You demand and take everything...

2066
01:26:40,630 --> 01:26:41,800
from me.

2067
01:26:43,900 --> 01:26:46,010
He's become the joker.

2068
01:26:46,970 --> 01:26:48,780
Sung Joo, do you want to advance?

2069
01:26:49,240 --> 01:26:50,410
- I can't.
- He can't.

2070
01:26:50,410 --> 01:26:51,540
That's why I'm giving it to you.

2071
01:26:51,540 --> 01:26:52,550
(Hyun Sung Joo, L and 2)

2072
01:26:52,550 --> 01:26:53,710
You're just giving it to him?

2073
01:26:53,980 --> 01:26:55,950
- You have one minute left.
- Okay.

2074
01:26:56,420 --> 01:26:57,420
(Choi Hye Seon, L and 3)

2075
01:26:57,420 --> 01:26:58,420
Okay.

2076
01:26:59,890 --> 01:27:01,350
Make Seong Beom reverse?

2077
01:27:01,690 --> 01:27:04,060
Kang Ji Hoo, please place your cards.

2078
01:27:04,460 --> 01:27:05,990
Jin Ho or Seong Beom.

2079
01:27:06,260 --> 01:27:07,660
Who's better?

2080
01:27:09,260 --> 01:27:10,400
Seong Beom?

2081
01:27:11,500 --> 01:27:12,770
We got very lucky...

2082
01:27:12,770 --> 01:27:14,100
when a three was placed
in Seong Beom's slot.

2083
01:27:14,100 --> 01:27:16,300
I could place a reverse card next to it...

2084
01:27:16,500 --> 01:27:18,070
and send him back three spaces.

2085
01:27:18,340 --> 01:27:20,870
Had Keun Woo not placed a three
in Seong Beom's slot,

2086
01:27:20,870 --> 01:27:24,210
I could have only made him go back
two spaces with the cards I had.

2087
01:27:24,210 --> 01:27:27,280
I was really happy
I could send him back three spaces.

2088
01:27:27,550 --> 01:27:30,420
It's not a bad idea to send
Seong Beom back using the reverse card.

2089
01:27:30,420 --> 01:27:31,580
I'm going to do that.

2090
01:27:33,350 --> 01:27:34,890
- Here?
- I'll put this here.

2091
01:27:34,890 --> 01:27:35,960
(Heo Seong Beom, 3 and reverse)

2092
01:27:36,090 --> 01:27:37,160
- Reverse and a three?
- Yes.

2093
01:27:37,290 --> 01:27:38,320
I'm moving backward.

2094
01:27:39,190 --> 01:27:40,660
- Should I discard this?
- Or Hye Seon?

2095
01:27:40,660 --> 01:27:42,030
We can make them collide.

2096
01:27:42,030 --> 01:27:43,860
- You have ten seconds left.
- We can flip it over.

2097
01:27:43,960 --> 01:27:45,260
- Just discard it.
- Don't do this.

2098
01:27:45,430 --> 01:27:46,700
Gosh, you're...

2099
01:27:46,700 --> 01:27:48,670
- so mean.
- Kang Ji Hoo, you've discarded a card.

2100
01:27:50,340 --> 01:27:51,540
This is fun.

2101
01:27:52,540 --> 01:27:55,510
At this point,
it's just a personal grudge.

2102
01:27:55,610 --> 01:27:57,680
He just hates me.

2103
01:27:57,980 --> 01:27:59,950
And I think...

2104
01:27:59,950 --> 01:28:02,550
the reverse card is very important
in playing Prediction Race.

2105
01:28:02,550 --> 01:28:05,850
And he used it on me,
which was a wrong move.

2106
01:28:05,850 --> 01:28:07,790
It's that team's mistake,

2107
01:28:07,790 --> 01:28:09,420
but I could see it clearly,
which made it more fun.

2108
01:28:09,420 --> 01:28:11,320
I could feel the hostility.

2109
01:28:11,320 --> 01:28:13,560
Choi Hye Seon, please place your cards.

2110
01:28:17,760 --> 01:28:20,970
Should I stay on your back forever?

2111
01:28:21,330 --> 01:28:22,740
- Should I stay...
- Me?

2112
01:28:22,740 --> 01:28:24,470
on your back forever?

2113
01:28:24,570 --> 01:28:26,410
Just scrap it.

2114
01:28:26,740 --> 01:28:28,810
Should I just stay there?

2115
01:28:30,980 --> 01:28:34,250
I think we should put a zero here.

2116
01:28:34,850 --> 01:28:36,150
- Seung Yong?
- Yes.

2117
01:28:36,350 --> 01:28:37,780
We have no use for a zero.

2118
01:28:37,780 --> 01:28:39,250
- You have no use...
- I can discard it.

2119
01:28:39,250 --> 01:28:40,450
- for a zero,
- It's unnecessary.

2120
01:28:40,590 --> 01:28:42,220
but if you're going to discard it,
it's better to place it there.

2121
01:28:42,720 --> 01:28:44,060
- As a gift.
- Why are you doing this to me?

2122
01:28:44,060 --> 01:28:45,190
I'll increase your chance...

2123
01:28:45,190 --> 01:28:46,330
- of getting flipped over.
- I let you go...

2124
01:28:46,330 --> 01:28:48,460
earlier.

2125
01:28:49,930 --> 01:28:52,130
- Then...
- YunB will go like this.

2126
01:28:53,270 --> 01:28:55,640
Then you get your booster on.

2127
01:28:55,700 --> 01:28:57,840
So you can take off.
Isn't it better that way?

2128
01:28:58,540 --> 01:28:59,670
You're right.

2129
01:28:59,940 --> 01:29:01,070
Ta-da.

2130
01:29:01,540 --> 01:29:02,940
Jin Ho can move one space.

2131
01:29:02,940 --> 01:29:05,180
Jin Ho, do you want to move
and let Sung Joo go?

2132
01:29:05,310 --> 01:29:06,710
Sung Joo...

2133
01:29:06,780 --> 01:29:08,380
Don't move me.

2134
01:29:08,450 --> 01:29:10,250
- You don't want to?
- No.

2135
01:29:10,780 --> 01:29:12,150
- Discard it.
- Discard it.

2136
01:29:12,150 --> 01:29:14,350
(Choi Hye Seon discards Movement Card 1.)

2137
01:29:14,720 --> 01:29:16,720
All the movement cards have been placed.

2138
01:29:16,720 --> 01:29:19,130
The race cars will start moving now.

2139
01:29:19,930 --> 01:29:21,860
Jeong Keun Woo, two spaces forward...

2140
01:29:21,860 --> 01:29:23,930
and one space right.

2141
01:29:24,000 --> 01:29:25,160
Vroom.

2142
01:29:25,160 --> 01:29:27,400
- We've come a long way in three hours.
- We sure have.

2143
01:29:28,000 --> 01:29:30,700
YunB, one space right.

2144
01:29:33,370 --> 01:29:35,880
Heo Seong Beom, three spaces backward.

2145
01:29:37,110 --> 01:29:38,280
Thank you.

2146
01:29:40,250 --> 01:29:41,710
When you made it this far.

2147
01:29:42,050 --> 01:29:44,020
Choi Hye Seon, booster activated.

2148
01:29:44,020 --> 01:29:46,050
You will start two spaces ahead.

2149
01:29:46,220 --> 01:29:48,820
- You're pulling ahead.
- Nice, right?

2150
01:29:48,820 --> 01:29:50,360
Yes, it's a long way to London.

2151
01:29:50,360 --> 01:29:53,390
Three spaces forward and one space left.

2152
01:29:53,660 --> 01:29:55,830
That's so far ahead.

2153
01:29:56,300 --> 01:29:58,970
- You're like Usain Bolt.
- The distance between us is crazy.

2154
01:29:58,970 --> 01:30:00,030
Oh, dear.

2155
01:30:00,030 --> 01:30:02,000
- You're like Usain Bolt.
- It's like the sky and the ground.

2156
01:30:02,000 --> 01:30:03,500
- She's so far ahead.
- How to catch up?

2157
01:30:03,500 --> 01:30:04,770
I feel proud.

2158
01:30:05,910 --> 01:30:07,040
(Round 8 Movement Results)

2159
01:30:07,040 --> 01:30:08,240
(Player, predicted rank:
1. Choi Hye Seon, 2. YunB,)

2160
01:30:08,240 --> 01:30:09,440
(3. Hong Jin Ho, 4. Hyun Sung Joo,
5. Shin Seung Yong, 6. Kang Ji Ho,)

2161
01:30:09,440 --> 01:30:10,640
(7. Jeong Keun Woo, 8. Heo Seong Beom)

2162
01:30:11,510 --> 01:30:13,580
Round Nine starts now.

2163
01:30:15,150 --> 01:30:17,920
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

2164
01:30:17,920 --> 01:30:19,190
(Round 9, Keun Woo starts 1st.)

2165
01:30:21,820 --> 01:30:25,760
(Jeong Keun Woo plays 1st in Round 9.)

2166
01:30:27,560 --> 01:30:31,860
(Once again, he heads straight
to the Voting Room.)

2167
01:30:36,670 --> 01:30:37,740
(Jeong Keun Woo bets a 3 on an Area.)

2168
01:30:37,740 --> 01:30:39,440
You've placed Card Three.

2169
01:30:39,440 --> 01:30:40,770
The game was so easy.

2170
01:30:46,280 --> 01:30:53,850
(The situation makes him whistle.)

2171
01:30:54,820 --> 01:31:00,090
(Singing)

2172
01:31:00,590 --> 01:31:04,960
(He even feels a bit bored.)

2173
01:31:12,710 --> 01:31:15,010
The cards for Round Nine were revealed.

2174
01:31:15,740 --> 01:31:18,240
Reverse and a four came up together.

2175
01:31:18,310 --> 01:31:20,150
(Ji Hoo is currently in 6th place,
his predicted rank being 2nd.)

2176
01:31:20,150 --> 01:31:22,010
(Kang Ji Hoo)

2177
01:31:22,010 --> 01:31:24,120
It won't be easy
if they try to pull me back.

2178
01:31:24,520 --> 01:31:25,790
I must win the bid.

2179
01:31:26,150 --> 01:31:27,450
(Seung Yong's remaining cards,
Ji Hoo's remaining cards)

2180
01:31:27,450 --> 01:31:28,890
I'll bet a five on Area C.

2181
01:31:29,290 --> 01:31:31,490
(Nodding)

2182
01:31:33,590 --> 01:31:36,860
Shin Seung Yong, place a card
in the area of your choosing.

2183
01:31:38,660 --> 01:31:41,500
(Shin Seung Yong bets a 5 on Area C.)

2184
01:31:46,070 --> 01:31:47,870
In case it doesn't work out,

2185
01:31:47,870 --> 01:31:50,080
you should bet a 3 or a 4 on Area C.

2186
01:31:50,380 --> 01:31:51,840
- To the same area?
- Yes.

2187
01:31:53,810 --> 01:31:55,750
Since Hye Seon is pulling too far ahead,

2188
01:31:55,750 --> 01:31:57,680
we could send her four spaces backward.

2189
01:31:57,820 --> 01:31:58,820
(Hye Seon is leading with a big gap.)

2190
01:31:58,820 --> 01:32:01,650
(Choi Hye Seon)

2191
01:32:05,090 --> 01:32:06,660
I think this is better.

2192
01:32:08,130 --> 01:32:09,130
What's the reason?

2193
01:32:10,300 --> 01:32:12,300
Because I think they'll want to win this.

2194
01:32:12,500 --> 01:32:15,100
This isn't too bad either.

2195
01:32:15,100 --> 01:32:16,800
We could just be wasting
our betting cards.

2196
01:32:22,210 --> 01:32:25,110
They could attack you with this.

2197
01:32:27,310 --> 01:32:28,380
Anyway,

2198
01:32:29,620 --> 01:32:31,780
we must stop Hye Seon.

2199
01:32:33,220 --> 01:32:36,320
- We must win Area C.
- You'll do it?

2200
01:32:36,320 --> 01:32:39,890
I bet a five on Area C,

2201
01:32:39,890 --> 01:32:41,690
but it'll definitely become null.

2202
01:32:42,730 --> 01:32:45,870
So I'd like you to bet a 4 or a 3
on Area C.

2203
01:32:46,200 --> 01:32:47,470
But I don't know which is better.

2204
01:32:47,470 --> 01:32:49,640
- I think we need both 4 and 3.
- What?

2205
01:32:49,640 --> 01:32:51,540
We need to bet both 4 and 3.

2206
01:32:52,310 --> 01:32:53,910
That doesn't sound bad.

2207
01:32:53,910 --> 01:32:54,970
(Seung Yong Alliance plans
to secure Area C by playing safe.)

2208
01:32:56,180 --> 01:32:57,340
Do you have a 3 or a 4?

2209
01:32:57,810 --> 01:32:58,810
I have a four.

2210
01:32:58,810 --> 01:32:59,810
(YunB's remaining cards)

2211
01:33:00,480 --> 01:33:02,520
Can you bet a four on Area C?

2212
01:33:03,120 --> 01:33:04,620
A four on Area C?

2213
01:33:04,620 --> 01:33:06,390
So we'll bet a 3, a 4, and a 5.

2214
01:33:07,620 --> 01:33:09,760
I don't think they'll bet that eagerly
on Area C.

2215
01:33:11,820 --> 01:33:13,790
I think they will.

2216
01:33:14,960 --> 01:33:15,960
Shall we talk over there?

2217
01:33:15,960 --> 01:33:18,730
(Kang Ji Hoo, predicted rank, 2nd place)

2218
01:33:19,300 --> 01:33:20,500
- Yes.
- They will...

2219
01:33:21,300 --> 01:33:24,400
definitely bet a 5 and a 4 on Area C.

2220
01:33:25,300 --> 01:33:26,740
You're 100 percent sure?

2221
01:33:26,740 --> 01:33:27,770
(Nodding)

2222
01:33:27,770 --> 01:33:28,840
Okay, then.

2223
01:33:32,880 --> 01:33:34,410
I'll bet a four on Area C.

2224
01:33:37,250 --> 01:33:38,920
(Kang Ji Hoo bets a 3 on Area C.)

2225
01:33:39,120 --> 01:33:40,390
It means I need to counter them...

2226
01:33:40,690 --> 01:33:42,560
and you need to back me up.

2227
01:33:42,790 --> 01:33:45,090
(Team P3 Alliance also comes up with
a backup plan...)

2228
01:33:45,090 --> 01:33:46,590
(in case their votes become null.)

2229
01:33:50,300 --> 01:33:52,830
(Choi Hye Seon has placed her bet.)

2230
01:33:54,900 --> 01:33:56,970
(Heo Seong Beom has placed his bet.)

2231
01:34:00,470 --> 01:34:03,710
(All the players have placed their bets.)

2232
01:34:04,580 --> 01:34:06,810
I will announce the betting results.

2233
01:34:06,810 --> 01:34:08,380
(Round 9 Betting Results)

2234
01:34:08,580 --> 01:34:10,750
Area A goes to Choi Hye Seon.

2235
01:34:10,980 --> 01:34:12,920
Area B goes to Heo Seong Beom.

2236
01:34:13,950 --> 01:34:16,020
Area C goes to Shin Seung Yong.

2237
01:34:17,020 --> 01:34:19,930
Area D goes to Jeong Keun Woo.

2238
01:34:19,930 --> 01:34:21,630
You're seriously...

2239
01:34:21,630 --> 01:34:23,460
You're a master. You win every round.

2240
01:34:23,960 --> 01:34:25,530
Didn't he win almost every round?

2241
01:34:25,530 --> 01:34:27,700
Did you rig it?

2242
01:34:28,500 --> 01:34:30,070
(Round 9 Betting Results)

2243
01:34:30,070 --> 01:34:31,640
(A, Choi Hye Seon, B, Heo Seong Beom,
C, Shin Seung Yong, D, Jeong Keun Woo)

2244
01:34:31,640 --> 01:34:34,170
(Team P3 Alliance did not bet on Area C.)

2245
01:34:39,510 --> 01:34:42,150
I think it was a wrong move.

2246
01:34:42,920 --> 01:34:45,220
We just wasted a four.

2247
01:34:45,220 --> 01:34:46,850
What are you guys doing?

2248
01:34:48,590 --> 01:34:50,560
We secured the reverse card as planned,

2249
01:34:50,920 --> 01:34:53,930
but the opposing alliance won
all the other three bids.

2250
01:34:56,230 --> 01:34:58,060
Even if Hye Seon pulls ahead,

2251
01:34:58,630 --> 01:34:59,670
you won't keep going.

2252
01:34:59,670 --> 01:35:01,470
They'll focus on Hye Seon
to try and stop her.

2253
01:35:01,930 --> 01:35:03,100
It's not bad, actually.

2254
01:35:06,510 --> 01:35:09,480
Choi Hye Seon, choose your predicted rank.

2255
01:35:10,310 --> 01:35:12,110
You predicted you would be in third place.

2256
01:35:12,110 --> 01:35:13,510
(Choi Hye Seon's predicted rank is
3rd place.)

2257
01:35:13,510 --> 01:35:15,410
If I pull ahead from the start,

2258
01:35:15,410 --> 01:35:16,650
I could become a target,

2259
01:35:16,650 --> 01:35:18,620
or someone could get on top of my car.

2260
01:35:18,620 --> 01:35:22,520
Or I could unintentionally serve
as a booster for someone else.

2261
01:35:22,520 --> 01:35:26,830
So I'll pull ahead as a test
or as a bluff,

2262
01:35:26,830 --> 01:35:29,900
and they'll follow behind me
while I act as a shield.

2263
01:35:29,900 --> 01:35:32,030
That was our strategy.

2264
01:35:32,030 --> 01:35:33,200
(She's playing the tank role
of the alliance.)

2265
01:35:33,530 --> 01:35:36,370
They could attack you with this.

2266
01:35:36,370 --> 01:35:37,840
What's the point of sending me back?

2267
01:35:38,440 --> 01:35:39,670
It's not bad for me, though.

2268
01:35:41,310 --> 01:35:44,640
I knew how important a reverse card was.

2269
01:35:44,640 --> 01:35:47,910
It's much easier to make
unconventional moves with it.

2270
01:35:47,910 --> 01:35:50,820
But, despite that,

2271
01:35:50,820 --> 01:35:53,890
if we could win two areas
and get six cards,

2272
01:35:53,890 --> 01:35:56,190
we could use them to defend ourselves.

2273
01:35:56,590 --> 01:35:59,390
You will now place your movement cards.

2274
01:35:59,390 --> 01:36:00,530
(Placing movement cards)

2275
01:36:06,170 --> 01:36:08,330
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

2276
01:36:08,330 --> 01:36:10,240
(The first player is Jeong Keun Woo.)

2277
01:36:10,340 --> 01:36:14,570
(Round 9, Keun Woo, Seong Beom,
Hye Seon, Seung Yong)

2278
01:36:15,910 --> 01:36:17,840
(Placing)

2279
01:36:18,510 --> 01:36:19,650
My gosh.

2280
01:36:24,120 --> 01:36:25,120
(Kang Ji Hoo, currently in 6th place)

2281
01:36:25,120 --> 01:36:26,720
(He will become 3rd place at once.)

2282
01:36:26,720 --> 01:36:28,350
(3rd place)

2283
01:36:30,920 --> 01:36:32,660
You're really changing the whole game.

2284
01:36:33,430 --> 01:36:34,630
I can't predict your moves.

2285
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:37,930
You all are dead today.

2286
01:36:38,760 --> 01:36:40,100
I can't predict your moves.

2287
01:36:41,930 --> 01:36:44,300
(He places the remaining 3
in Heo Seong Beom's slot.)

2288
01:36:44,770 --> 01:36:46,710
Are you including me in this race?

2289
01:36:46,840 --> 01:36:47,870
- You're way behind.
- That's right.

2290
01:36:47,870 --> 01:36:49,640
- He's way behind.
- You're way behind.

2291
01:36:49,640 --> 01:36:51,040
(He placed the movement cards evenly
to both alliances.)

2292
01:36:51,210 --> 01:36:53,780
He let me get on top of Jin Ho,
who is on top of Sung Joo,

2293
01:36:53,780 --> 01:36:55,810
to the third level.

2294
01:36:55,810 --> 01:36:59,150
He made the best move for me.

2295
01:36:59,150 --> 01:37:02,150
He set me back four spaces earlier,

2296
01:37:02,150 --> 01:37:03,860
and now,
he's sending me three spaces forward.

2297
01:37:04,460 --> 01:37:07,390
What is this? I can't understand him.

2298
01:37:07,390 --> 01:37:10,200
It felt like
Keun Woo was part of the game too.

2299
01:37:10,200 --> 01:37:13,000
I can't understand
how he wins all the bids either.

2300
01:37:13,000 --> 01:37:14,770
Him pulling me back and pushing me forward
makes me think...

2301
01:37:14,770 --> 01:37:17,770
he's maintaining the balance of the game.

2302
01:37:19,170 --> 01:37:21,610
Today, I'll be a bass.

2303
01:37:21,610 --> 01:37:22,680
It was my goal...

2304
01:37:22,940 --> 01:37:25,910
to make the game muddy...

2305
01:37:26,280 --> 01:37:27,650
so I could stay behind.

2306
01:37:28,380 --> 01:37:30,780
Heo Seong Beom, please place your cards.

2307
01:37:33,150 --> 01:37:37,020
(Seong Beom needs to place a card
bigger than 2.)

2308
01:37:37,220 --> 01:37:39,730
Jin Ho, you need to move forward.

2309
01:37:39,890 --> 01:37:41,330
He can't move.

2310
01:37:41,330 --> 01:37:42,700
Ji Hoo took this card.

2311
01:37:42,700 --> 01:37:43,930
- He goes first.
- I...

2312
01:37:43,930 --> 01:37:45,400
- No.
- Ji Hoo goes first.

2313
01:37:45,400 --> 01:37:47,670
Give me one to reset that.

2314
01:37:47,670 --> 01:37:49,200
- Need to get rid of it.
- Reset it.

2315
01:37:49,200 --> 01:37:50,200
Any card.

2316
01:37:50,500 --> 01:37:55,570
(Round 9, Keun Woo, Seong Beom,
Hye Seon, Seung Yong)

2317
01:37:55,770 --> 01:37:57,880
(He places Cards 3 and 1 as planned.)

2318
01:37:59,710 --> 01:38:00,710
What about Hye Seon?

2319
01:38:00,880 --> 01:38:02,350
She needs to move.

2320
01:38:02,350 --> 01:38:04,120
You want to move Hye Seon? Should I?

2321
01:38:04,620 --> 01:38:05,820
- I can go.
- Isn't it better if she goes?

2322
01:38:05,820 --> 01:38:07,620
- Okay.
- I'm unrivaled,

2323
01:38:07,620 --> 01:38:09,790
- I'll give you a left.
- so I doubt anyone can catch me.

2324
01:38:09,890 --> 01:38:12,520
(He places the last 3 he has
in Hye Seon's slot.)

2325
01:38:12,960 --> 01:38:15,530
Choi Hye Seon, please place your cards.

2326
01:38:15,730 --> 01:38:18,300
(Choi Hye Seon's turn)

2327
01:38:21,730 --> 01:38:24,270
(Hye Seon fills up her gear board
to defend from a reverse card.)

2328
01:38:24,540 --> 01:38:27,270
- What happened?
- Stopping that from using the booster.

2329
01:38:27,270 --> 01:38:29,010
- Who?
- You.

2330
01:38:29,010 --> 01:38:30,080
- Me?
- Yes.

2331
01:38:30,580 --> 01:38:32,380
(Seung Yong can activate the booster,
as he is right behind YunB.)

2332
01:38:32,380 --> 01:38:34,010
(Shin Seung Yong)

2333
01:38:34,450 --> 01:38:36,920
I'll flip over YunB.

2334
01:38:36,920 --> 01:38:39,750
(She places 0 and 2 in YunB's slots.)

2335
01:38:39,750 --> 01:38:42,690
(Lastly, it's Shin Seung Yong's turn.)

2336
01:38:43,590 --> 01:38:44,860
- It's not too bad.
- What?

2337
01:38:44,860 --> 01:38:46,330
Shall we aim for the next turn?

2338
01:38:46,930 --> 01:38:50,360
We got really good cards,
a reverse card and a four.

2339
01:38:50,360 --> 01:38:51,600
But we couldn't use them.

2340
01:38:51,600 --> 01:38:54,600
They'd filled up all their slots.

2341
01:38:54,670 --> 01:38:58,800
(Round 9, Keun Woo, Seong Beom,
Hye Seon, Seung Yong)

2342
01:38:58,800 --> 01:39:02,570
(He voids the reverse
and places 1 on his slot.)

2343
01:39:02,570 --> 01:39:05,440
(Round 9, Keun Woo, Seong Beom,
Hye Seon, Seung Yong)

2344
01:39:06,250 --> 01:39:07,850
(He places 4 in Jeong Keun Woo's slot.)

2345
01:39:07,850 --> 01:39:10,550
We were sure Keun Woo's predicted rank
was low,

2346
01:39:10,550 --> 01:39:13,450
so we placed a four in Keun Woo's slot
to send him forward.

2347
01:39:14,220 --> 01:39:16,390
Thank you. I thought I'd be
the only one left out.

2348
01:39:16,760 --> 01:39:17,760
But you gave me one.

2349
01:39:19,290 --> 01:39:21,730
All the movement cards have been placed.

2350
01:39:21,730 --> 01:39:22,900
(Round 9)

2351
01:39:22,900 --> 01:39:25,900
(Everyone except Jeong Keun Woo can move.)

2352
01:39:25,900 --> 01:39:28,230
The race cars will start moving now.

2353
01:39:30,300 --> 01:39:34,270
Kang Ji Hoo,
1 space forward and 1 space right.

2354
01:39:34,270 --> 01:39:37,110
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

2355
01:39:37,210 --> 01:39:40,580
You've collided with Sung Joo's
and Jin Ho's race cars.

2356
01:39:40,610 --> 01:39:41,910
Hamburger.

2357
01:39:41,910 --> 01:39:43,120
- Hamburger.
- Three-storey.

2358
01:39:44,480 --> 01:39:45,980
This is the first three-storey collision.

2359
01:39:45,980 --> 01:39:47,020
Let's sleep here.

2360
01:39:48,050 --> 01:39:50,890
YunB, two spaces right.

2361
01:39:50,890 --> 01:39:54,060
Your race car has flipped over,
and you cannot move until the next round.

2362
01:39:57,200 --> 01:39:59,700
Heo Seong Beom, three spaces forward.

2363
01:40:00,100 --> 01:40:02,000
I'm finally back to my original spot.

2364
01:40:03,970 --> 01:40:07,570
Choi Hye Seon,
2 spaces forward and 1 space left.

2365
01:40:07,570 --> 01:40:09,270
- Let's go, Hye Seon.
- Let's go.

2366
01:40:09,270 --> 01:40:10,380
Here she goes.

2367
01:40:10,380 --> 01:40:12,780
(Hye Seon has widened the gap.)

2368
01:40:14,680 --> 01:40:15,750
So this is how it feels.

2369
01:40:16,480 --> 01:40:17,780
I want to come in first place.

2370
01:40:18,350 --> 01:40:19,390
Same here.

2371
01:40:19,550 --> 01:40:21,790
Hyun Sung Joo. You cannot move.

2372
01:40:21,950 --> 01:40:24,890
(There's a long way for Sung Joo to go.)

2373
01:40:25,820 --> 01:40:26,930
I'd better grab some grub.

2374
01:40:28,290 --> 01:40:31,330
Shin Seung Yong, one space right.

2375
01:40:31,330 --> 01:40:34,100
(Seung Yong is back
to where he could get a booster.)

2376
01:40:34,170 --> 01:40:35,230
What?

2377
01:40:35,230 --> 01:40:37,570
Hold on. I practically helped him
get a booster.

2378
01:40:38,170 --> 01:40:39,740
Smart move, Seung Yong.

2379
01:40:41,170 --> 01:40:42,740
All players have completed their moves.

2380
01:40:42,740 --> 01:40:43,810
(Round 9 Movement Results)

2381
01:40:43,810 --> 01:40:44,840
(Player, predicted rank:
1. Choi Hye Seon, 2. YunB,)

2382
01:40:44,840 --> 01:40:45,840
(3. Shin Seung Yong, 4. Kang Ji Hoo,
5. Hong Jin Ho, 6. Hyun Sung Joo,)

2383
01:40:45,840 --> 01:40:47,050
(7. Jeong Keun Woo, 8. Heo Seong Beom)

2384
01:40:49,550 --> 01:40:51,550
We will begin Round Ten.

2385
01:40:52,720 --> 01:40:55,390
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

2386
01:40:56,220 --> 01:40:58,790
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,)

2387
01:40:58,790 --> 01:41:01,530
(Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

2388
01:41:03,160 --> 01:41:05,530
(Staring)

2389
01:41:05,830 --> 01:41:08,700
It's not moving at all. It's not.

2390
01:41:09,470 --> 01:41:11,340
It's not moving.

2391
01:41:11,340 --> 01:41:12,340
(Sung Joo has been buried since Round 6.)

2392
01:41:12,340 --> 01:41:14,770
I'll get rid of them...

2393
01:41:15,410 --> 01:41:16,540
if I win an area.

2394
01:41:16,640 --> 01:41:17,740
Hi.

2395
01:41:19,980 --> 01:41:22,580
You've placed Card Three in Area D.
Is that right?

2396
01:41:22,580 --> 01:41:23,680
Yes.

2397
01:41:24,320 --> 01:41:25,320
(Sung Joo dreams of winning.)

2398
01:41:25,320 --> 01:41:26,490
Please move to the main hall.

2399
01:41:26,490 --> 01:41:28,790
(Sung Joo dreams of winning.)

2400
01:41:29,920 --> 01:41:31,820
- It's you, right?
- What? Yes.

2401
01:41:32,190 --> 01:41:33,860
We should both check.

2402
01:41:33,860 --> 01:41:35,930
(Ji Hoo and YunB are the first to start.)

2403
01:41:35,930 --> 01:41:38,200
Either of us needs to win.

2404
01:41:40,770 --> 01:41:43,540
From what I see,
Hye Seon in a commanding lead is...

2405
01:41:44,100 --> 01:41:45,500
actually great.

2406
01:41:46,870 --> 01:41:49,480
Either way, you're 2nd place
and I'm 3rd place.

2407
01:41:50,840 --> 01:41:53,480
Aside from Ji Hoo and me,
someone on the other team...

2408
01:41:53,480 --> 01:41:55,280
had to be in first place,

2409
01:41:55,280 --> 01:41:57,120
whether it was Hye Seon or someone else.

2410
01:41:57,120 --> 01:41:58,720
But it ended up being Hye Seon.

2411
01:41:59,120 --> 01:42:00,620
(YunB: Predicted 3rd,
Kang Ji Hoo: Predicted 2nd)

2412
01:42:00,620 --> 01:42:02,150
(YunB and Ji Hoo are leading,
just as predicted.)

2413
01:42:02,150 --> 01:42:04,760
No one was coming in first place.

2414
01:42:04,760 --> 01:42:07,230
But thanks to Hye Seon moving forward,

2415
01:42:07,230 --> 01:42:09,290
I can act as if I wanted to follow her.

2416
01:42:09,290 --> 01:42:11,160
With that,
I can naturally come in second place.

2417
01:42:11,400 --> 01:42:13,700
I'm in a way better place than before.

2418
01:42:16,070 --> 01:42:17,700
How about letting Hye Seon go?

2419
01:42:18,100 --> 01:42:19,270
Why?

2420
01:42:19,640 --> 01:42:21,010
I don't mind.

2421
01:42:21,240 --> 01:42:22,710
But I'm worried she'd go too far.

2422
01:42:22,710 --> 01:42:25,940
The other team is trying to end the game.

2423
01:42:25,940 --> 01:42:26,950
(The game ends
when a player finishes the race.)

2424
01:42:26,950 --> 01:42:29,750
We can adjust our team's pace,

2425
01:42:29,750 --> 01:42:31,150
but not theirs.

2426
01:42:33,850 --> 01:42:35,490
I currently have Three,

2427
01:42:35,490 --> 01:42:37,720
so I think you or YunB...

2428
01:42:37,890 --> 01:42:39,630
should go for 4 or 5.

2429
01:42:40,290 --> 01:42:43,400
I personally think 4 is better of the 2.

2430
01:42:43,400 --> 01:42:45,200
(The goal is Area D,
where the reverse is.)

2431
01:42:46,400 --> 01:42:49,070
(YunB bets a 5 on Area D.)

2432
01:42:50,540 --> 01:42:52,340
(Kang Ji Hoo bets a 4 on Area A.)

2433
01:42:54,310 --> 01:42:57,340
(Shin Seung Yong bets a 3 on Area B.)

2434
01:43:07,750 --> 01:43:12,390
(Seung Yong Alliance
shares the betting information.)

2435
01:43:26,270 --> 01:43:28,040
Just look at them.

2436
01:43:34,650 --> 01:43:36,580
- So...
- Yes?

2437
01:43:38,650 --> 01:43:40,490
You're willing to betray...

2438
01:43:41,650 --> 01:43:44,260
if you ever get in a favorable situation
in the far future, right?

2439
01:43:44,960 --> 01:43:46,060
Of course.

2440
01:43:46,060 --> 01:43:47,460
- Yes?
- Yes.

2441
01:43:47,460 --> 01:43:49,330
If we split up...

2442
01:43:49,330 --> 01:43:51,560
and can't win together,

2443
01:43:51,760 --> 01:43:53,570
I'll secure my win.

2444
01:43:53,970 --> 01:43:55,800
It's risky,
so I'm not going to share anything.

2445
01:43:55,800 --> 01:43:56,800
Right.

2446
01:43:57,270 --> 01:43:59,340
- Sung Joo...
- I'm watching with full attention.

2447
01:43:59,500 --> 01:44:01,540
Are you confident about
not telling anyone?

2448
01:44:01,570 --> 01:44:02,570
Of course.

2449
01:44:03,710 --> 01:44:05,210
I'll tell you in a bit.

2450
01:44:05,380 --> 01:44:06,910
There's no need to tell me now.

2451
01:44:07,780 --> 01:44:09,410
If we need to talk in the later half,

2452
01:44:09,410 --> 01:44:10,750
you have to find me.

2453
01:44:10,750 --> 01:44:13,420
After all, I'm alone.
Me looking for you is weird.

2454
01:44:17,460 --> 01:44:19,120
Here's what's clear. I'm in the lead.

2455
01:44:20,730 --> 01:44:22,160
That's obvious
even without you telling me.

2456
01:44:23,230 --> 01:44:24,300
Okay.

2457
01:44:25,300 --> 01:44:27,100
All players have placed their bets.

2458
01:44:28,630 --> 01:44:30,740
I will announce the betting results.

2459
01:44:31,800 --> 01:44:34,370
Area A has no winners.

2460
01:44:34,740 --> 01:44:35,810
That's bad.

2461
01:44:36,240 --> 01:44:39,140
Area B goes to Shin Seung Yong.

2462
01:44:39,140 --> 01:44:40,980
(Area B goes to Shin Seung Yong.)

2463
01:44:41,150 --> 01:44:44,880
Area C goes to Choi Hye Seon.

2464
01:44:45,920 --> 01:44:49,390
Area D goes to YunB.

2465
01:44:50,560 --> 01:44:51,820
(Round 10 Betting Results)

2466
01:44:51,820 --> 01:44:53,890
(A: Kang Ji Hoo, Heo Seong Beom,
B: Shin Seung Yong,)

2467
01:44:53,890 --> 01:44:56,530
(C: Choi Hye Seon, Hong Jin Ho,
D: YunB, Hyun Sung Joo, Jeong Keun Woo)

2468
01:44:57,330 --> 01:44:59,970
You will now place your movement cards.

2469
01:45:01,100 --> 01:45:03,300
YunB, please place your cards.

2470
01:45:09,810 --> 01:45:12,740
(Placing reverse and 3
without a 2nd thought)

2471
01:45:13,080 --> 01:45:14,480
- What?
- We've been attacked.

2472
01:45:14,480 --> 01:45:15,580
He's dragging us down.

2473
01:45:16,050 --> 01:45:18,220
- Hye Seon?
- Don't do this.

2474
01:45:19,320 --> 01:45:21,720
I couldn't help but wonder
why they're pulling...

2475
01:45:21,720 --> 01:45:22,920
Hye Seon back.

2476
01:45:23,090 --> 01:45:25,790
I doubt there was a first place.

2477
01:45:26,930 --> 01:45:28,760
Did Ji Hoo really write down first place?

2478
01:45:28,760 --> 01:45:32,230
Letting Hye Seon get first place is
favorable to us.

2479
01:45:32,630 --> 01:45:34,030
There was no need to pull her back.

2480
01:45:34,170 --> 01:45:36,670
But I had to keep acting out
the image that...

2481
01:45:36,870 --> 01:45:38,970
I'm striving to come in first place.

2482
01:45:38,970 --> 01:45:40,310
Acting as if
I wanted to come in first place.

2483
01:45:40,310 --> 01:45:42,470
Acting like I'm going to pull
Hye Seon back.

2484
01:45:43,010 --> 01:45:45,410
All the movement cards have been placed.

2485
01:45:45,410 --> 01:45:48,050
(Round 10: Jeong Keun Woo, Kang Ji Hoo,
Heo Seong Beom, Choi Hye Seon)

2486
01:45:48,580 --> 01:45:50,680
The race cars will start moving now.

2487
01:45:53,190 --> 01:45:56,890
Kang Ji Hoo, 2 spaces forward
and 1 space right.

2488
01:45:57,260 --> 01:45:58,790
One, two, three.

2489
01:45:59,830 --> 01:46:02,530
(Ji Hoo pulls far ahead.)

2490
01:46:02,630 --> 01:46:06,230
Heo Seong Beom, 1 space forward
and 1 space right.

2491
01:46:07,070 --> 01:46:08,630
Three cars.

2492
01:46:09,600 --> 01:46:11,970
Choi Hye Seon, three spaces backward.

2493
01:46:12,740 --> 01:46:14,810
- Seriously?
- Look at the gap now.

2494
01:46:16,210 --> 01:46:17,640
You guys are right on my heels.

2495
01:46:18,880 --> 01:46:22,410
Jeong Keun Woo, 2 spaces forward
and 1 space left.

2496
01:46:22,410 --> 01:46:23,480
Crash!

2497
01:46:24,150 --> 01:46:26,080
- No.
- A three-stack burger.

2498
01:46:26,920 --> 01:46:28,990
You've collided with Hyun Sung Joo
and Hong Jin Ho's...

2499
01:46:28,990 --> 01:46:30,260
- race cars.
- A three-stack burger.

2500
01:46:30,460 --> 01:46:32,120
Jin Ho can't escape.

2501
01:46:32,120 --> 01:46:33,530
I'm doomed.

2502
01:46:34,390 --> 01:46:37,100
- A three-stack burger.
- YunB, your car can move now.

2503
01:46:37,560 --> 01:46:39,330
(Round 10 Movement Results)

2504
01:46:39,330 --> 01:46:41,070
(Player, predicted rank:
1. Choi Hye Seon, 2. Kang Ji Hoo,)

2505
01:46:41,070 --> 01:46:42,070
(3. YunB, 4. Shin Seung Yong,
5. Heo Seong Beom, 6. Jeong Keun Woo,)

2506
01:46:42,070 --> 01:46:43,070
(7. Hong Jin Ho, 8. Hyun Sung Joo)

2507
01:46:43,070 --> 01:46:46,640
Sung Joo, hang in there.
You'll be able to move soon.

2508
01:46:47,570 --> 01:46:49,310
That's been on my mind for the past hour.

2509
01:46:49,810 --> 01:46:50,840
(A three-stack burger parking:)

2510
01:46:50,840 --> 01:46:51,880
(Jeong Keun Woo, Hong Jin Ho,
Hyun Sung Joo)

2511
01:46:51,880 --> 01:46:53,010
Sung Joo...

2512
01:46:53,010 --> 01:46:54,480
- Don't you pity him?
- I do.

2513
01:46:54,480 --> 01:46:56,650
Sung Joo is being crushed by everyone.

2514
01:46:56,650 --> 01:46:58,720
- Should I help you out, Sung Joo?
- What?

2515
01:46:58,720 --> 01:47:00,890
Do you need my help?
Are you okay being crushed down?

2516
01:47:00,890 --> 01:47:02,320
It won't go your way either way.

2517
01:47:02,320 --> 01:47:03,390
Why not?

2518
01:47:03,820 --> 01:47:04,920
There's another player on top.

2519
01:47:04,920 --> 01:47:06,660
He needs to move...

2520
01:47:06,660 --> 01:47:08,030
- as well.
- If I make a move out,

2521
01:47:08,030 --> 01:47:09,390
you'll be able to get the car out
on the next turn.

2522
01:47:09,690 --> 01:47:12,700
You kept winning the bets,
so I doubt you will this time.

2523
01:47:13,500 --> 01:47:15,700
Isn't it a new round now?
Isn't it Round 11?

2524
01:47:15,700 --> 01:47:17,040
- Yes.
- You're right.

2525
01:47:17,400 --> 01:47:18,940
He's the king of betting.

2526
01:47:18,940 --> 01:47:20,970
(A new round receiving new betting cards)

2527
01:47:21,140 --> 01:47:23,180
Round 11 will begin now.

2528
01:47:24,740 --> 01:47:26,580
(Round 11)

2529
01:47:26,580 --> 01:47:27,580
(Jeong Keun Woo, Kang Ji Hoo, YunB,
Heo Seong Beom, Hong Jin Ho,)

2530
01:47:27,580 --> 01:47:28,650
(Choi Hye Seon, Hyun Sung Joo,
Shin Seung Yong)

2531
01:47:30,550 --> 01:47:32,450
- Tell me something, Keun Woo.
- What?

2532
01:47:32,450 --> 01:47:33,750
Are you going to go backward or not?

2533
01:47:34,420 --> 01:47:35,490
If possible.

2534
01:47:36,220 --> 01:47:37,390
I am!

2535
01:47:37,960 --> 01:47:40,130
(Keun Woo is after the reverse card.)

2536
01:47:40,130 --> 01:47:42,060
You're in front of everyone, no?

2537
01:47:42,360 --> 01:47:44,860
I want us to advance together.

2538
01:47:44,860 --> 01:47:47,470
From what I see,

2539
01:47:47,470 --> 01:47:48,730
not many were after this just now.

2540
01:47:48,730 --> 01:47:50,540
But I think Keun Woo is going to get
Area A.

2541
01:47:50,670 --> 01:47:53,610
If Keun Woo were to go backward,

2542
01:47:53,610 --> 01:47:55,140
we would need this area for sure.

2543
01:47:55,140 --> 01:47:56,840
This area is going to explode.

2544
01:47:57,140 --> 01:47:59,140
Let's keep this safe...

2545
01:47:59,480 --> 01:48:01,410
and go in here. That's for the best.

2546
01:48:01,410 --> 01:48:02,610
Are you worried he'd outrun you?

2547
01:48:03,110 --> 01:48:04,650
- You are, right?
- Yes.

2548
01:48:04,650 --> 01:48:07,290
But Seung Yong has a booster.
He could use it.

2549
01:48:07,290 --> 01:48:08,850
Seung Yong has a Zero.

2550
01:48:08,850 --> 01:48:10,220
Oh, right. Lucky me.

2551
01:48:10,420 --> 01:48:12,920
Then Ji Hoo will try to outrun me.

2552
01:48:12,960 --> 01:48:14,330
Will YunB let that happen?

2553
01:48:14,760 --> 01:48:16,060
Since he has to advance as well?

2554
01:48:16,360 --> 01:48:18,000
In my opinion,

2555
01:48:18,000 --> 01:48:20,470
- Among them.
- YunB would feel safe in the back.

2556
01:48:20,470 --> 01:48:22,330
YunB is probably in the middle-low rank.

2557
01:48:22,330 --> 01:48:25,140
- Right?
- YunB could join...

2558
01:48:25,140 --> 01:48:26,370
just because there's a gap.

2559
01:48:26,370 --> 01:48:28,870
Seung Yong and Ji Hoo
are in the top ranks,

2560
01:48:28,870 --> 01:48:30,280
and YunB can join only because
he's in the lower ranks.

2561
01:48:30,280 --> 01:48:32,110
- He might overlap with us.
- Exactly.

2562
01:48:32,110 --> 01:48:34,610
- If YunB is helping out the others,
- Interesting.

2563
01:48:34,610 --> 01:48:36,510
we could buy this one.

2564
01:48:37,050 --> 01:48:38,080
True.

2565
01:48:38,350 --> 01:48:43,460
(The strategy is to keep YunB,
the first player, in check.)

2566
01:48:43,520 --> 01:48:45,690
Heo Seong Beom, here's your green card.

2567
01:48:45,690 --> 01:48:46,690
Thank you.

2568
01:48:47,030 --> 01:48:48,060
(Heo Seong Beom bets a 5 on Area C.)

2569
01:48:48,060 --> 01:48:50,330
You've placed Card Five in Area C.

2570
01:48:50,330 --> 01:48:51,400
(Choi Hye Seon bets on Area D.)

2571
01:48:51,400 --> 01:48:53,030
Place your card
in the area of your choice.

2572
01:48:53,030 --> 01:48:54,230
(Hong Jin Ho bets on Area B.)

2573
01:48:54,230 --> 01:48:57,340
I think this is a crucial turning point.

2574
01:48:57,340 --> 01:48:59,700
It's a golden opportunity to tie...

2575
01:48:59,700 --> 01:49:01,140
Jin Ho down.

2576
01:49:01,310 --> 01:49:03,010
Since Keun Woo goes later,

2577
01:49:03,010 --> 01:49:04,540
Jin Ho is guaranteed to get tied down.

2578
01:49:04,540 --> 01:49:05,710
(Jeong Keun Woo, Hong Jin Ho)

2579
01:49:05,710 --> 01:49:07,880
The best option we have is...

2580
01:49:07,880 --> 01:49:10,420
to win the most bets.

2581
01:49:10,650 --> 01:49:12,920
If YunB wins Area C and I win Area A,

2582
01:49:13,150 --> 01:49:15,850
I could drag Hye Seon...

2583
01:49:15,850 --> 01:49:17,120
or Seong Beom down.

2584
01:49:18,490 --> 01:49:21,060
It'd be amazing if you could win either...

2585
01:49:21,060 --> 01:49:22,390
Area B or Area D.

2586
01:49:24,000 --> 01:49:25,060
Okay.

2587
01:49:26,500 --> 01:49:27,970
(The strategy is to keep Jin Ho in check.)

2588
01:49:27,970 --> 01:49:29,430
Hi.

2589
01:49:33,710 --> 01:49:37,210
You've placed Card Four in Area A.

2590
01:49:38,380 --> 01:49:39,910
(YunB bets on Area C.)

2591
01:49:39,910 --> 01:49:41,010
(Ji Hoo bets on Area B.)

2592
01:49:41,010 --> 01:49:42,550
All players have placed their bets.

2593
01:49:42,550 --> 01:49:43,580
(Round 11 Betting Results)

2594
01:49:43,580 --> 01:49:44,620
(A: Shin Seung Yong,
B: Hong Jin Ho, Kang Ji Hoo)

2595
01:49:44,620 --> 01:49:45,720
(C: Heo Seong Beom, YunB,
D: Choi Hye Seon)

2596
01:49:45,720 --> 01:49:48,220
I will announce the betting results.

2597
01:49:48,650 --> 01:49:52,860
Area A goes to Hyun Sung Joo.

2598
01:49:53,290 --> 01:49:54,360
How did he do that?

2599
01:49:54,660 --> 01:49:56,590
Area B goes to Kang Ji Hoo.

2600
01:49:56,800 --> 01:49:58,700
Area C goes to Heo Seong Beom.

2601
01:49:59,660 --> 01:50:03,030
Area D goes to Jeong Keun Woo.

2602
01:50:03,600 --> 01:50:05,700
- Keun Woo didn't get the reverse.
- No, he didn't.

2603
01:50:06,670 --> 01:50:08,710
Keun Woo doesn't have to move.

2604
01:50:09,740 --> 01:50:10,780
Are you sure?

2605
01:50:11,040 --> 01:50:12,680
Isn't there a plan we don't know about?

2606
01:50:14,380 --> 01:50:15,650
Should we let Sunny go?

2607
01:50:16,310 --> 01:50:17,420
<i>Sunny</i>

2608
01:50:18,220 --> 01:50:21,190
- The numbers are 3 and 4, right?
- Yes.

2609
01:50:21,920 --> 01:50:24,590
Hye Seon, do you want to take
the outer course or the inner course?

2610
01:50:24,920 --> 01:50:26,790
The inner course looks risky.
I'll take the outer one.

2611
01:50:31,660 --> 01:50:33,100
Let's go all out.

2612
01:50:34,500 --> 01:50:35,530
Okay.

2613
01:50:37,370 --> 01:50:39,800
Hyun Sung Joo, please place your cards.

2614
01:50:41,010 --> 01:50:42,570
Is our burger finally going to move?

2615
01:50:44,110 --> 01:50:45,540
Let me go backward, Sung Joo.

2616
01:50:46,240 --> 01:50:47,650
Please help Three go backward.

2617
01:50:48,450 --> 01:50:50,180
Help Shin Seung Yong go backward.

2618
01:50:51,120 --> 01:50:52,180
Are you asking your car
to be flipped over?

2619
01:50:52,180 --> 01:50:53,690
I've already made up my mind.

2620
01:50:58,090 --> 01:51:00,790
- Good one.
- Nice. He's helping us out.

2621
01:51:01,260 --> 01:51:02,690
(Sung Joo gets rid of
the two stacked-up cars.)

2622
01:51:02,690 --> 01:51:04,830
Sung Joo must want to get rid of it fast.

2623
01:51:06,130 --> 01:51:08,400
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

2624
01:51:08,400 --> 01:51:10,570
(It's betting ace Keun Woo's turn.)

2625
01:51:10,570 --> 01:51:12,300
I wonder if you have Card One left.

2626
01:51:12,940 --> 01:51:14,740
How about placing Zero on mine?

2627
01:51:15,510 --> 01:51:19,080
(Kang Ji Hoo: 3)

2628
01:51:20,180 --> 01:51:21,610
You're giving Three to me?

2629
01:51:21,980 --> 01:51:23,520
Do you have Card One left?

2630
01:51:23,680 --> 01:51:25,950
Zero to Shin Seung Yong.

2631
01:51:25,950 --> 01:51:28,220
(Heo Seong Beom: 2, 1)

2632
01:51:28,690 --> 01:51:29,890
Thank you, Keun Woo.

2633
01:51:30,760 --> 01:51:32,190
Zero...

2634
01:51:32,560 --> 01:51:33,760
- You want it?
- Please.

2635
01:51:33,760 --> 01:51:35,090
Will you be moving forward with Zero?

2636
01:51:35,360 --> 01:51:36,690
- Zero...
- No, I'd stay still.

2637
01:51:37,430 --> 01:51:40,130
This would disappear,
which would be favorable for Seung Yong.

2638
01:51:40,130 --> 01:51:42,630
I see. Are you desperate, Seung Yong?

2639
01:51:43,230 --> 01:51:45,770
- Please. Help me.
- I'm discarding it.

2640
01:51:47,810 --> 01:51:48,910
I'm discarding it.

2641
01:51:51,280 --> 01:51:53,010
His plea has been discarded.

2642
01:51:53,710 --> 01:51:55,580
Kang Ji Hoo, please place your cards.

2643
01:51:56,410 --> 01:51:58,550
(Kang Ji Hoo)

2644
01:51:58,550 --> 01:51:59,820
(Shin Seung Yong)

2645
01:51:59,820 --> 01:52:01,050
Doesn't this look right?

2646
01:52:03,120 --> 01:52:04,820
- It's not bad.
- What about this one?

2647
01:52:05,420 --> 01:52:07,060
- Discard it.
- Give it to someone.

2648
01:52:07,430 --> 01:52:08,830
I kind of want to help someone.

2649
01:52:09,990 --> 01:52:11,730
- Discard it.
- Should I?

2650
01:52:12,200 --> 01:52:14,100
If I place it here,

2651
01:52:14,600 --> 01:52:16,370
you could move to the left.

2652
01:52:17,300 --> 01:52:18,640
Okay, I'm going with this.

2653
01:52:18,640 --> 01:52:20,770
(Kang Ji Hoo, Shin Seung Yong)

2654
01:52:20,770 --> 01:52:22,470
Ji Hoo is making a move.

2655
01:52:23,310 --> 01:52:25,140
Ji Hoo, girlfriend?

2656
01:52:27,010 --> 01:52:28,580
(Round 11)

2657
01:52:28,580 --> 01:52:32,220
(Everyone can move
besides YunB and Hyun Sung Joo.)

2658
01:52:32,450 --> 01:52:34,820
The race cars will start moving now.

2659
01:52:34,820 --> 01:52:36,960
Heo Seong Beom, booster activated.

2660
01:52:36,960 --> 01:52:38,990
You will start two spaces ahead.

2661
01:52:39,690 --> 01:52:41,330
My plan wasn't to move this fast.

2662
01:52:41,860 --> 01:52:44,730
One space forward and one space left.

2663
01:52:45,430 --> 01:52:47,270
Look at him making a comeback from behind.

2664
01:52:47,270 --> 01:52:49,070
What a weird world.

2665
01:52:49,270 --> 01:52:50,440
- I was here.
- Exactly.

2666
01:52:50,440 --> 01:52:52,500
- It's just like life.
- Unbelievable.

2667
01:52:52,500 --> 01:52:53,740
It won't work out for me.

2668
01:52:53,740 --> 01:52:55,940
Hong Jin Ho, you cannot move.

2669
01:52:55,940 --> 01:52:57,510
What is this, long-term parking?

2670
01:52:57,980 --> 01:53:00,180
- The parking fee is beyond imagination.
- Is this Incheon International Airport?

2671
01:53:00,180 --> 01:53:04,180
Choi Hye Seon,
3 spaces forward and 1 space right.

2672
01:53:04,750 --> 01:53:05,950
Yes!

2673
01:53:07,890 --> 01:53:09,690
How's the view from over there, Hye Seon?

2674
01:53:09,690 --> 01:53:11,690
- You can see the finish line from there.
- It's great.

2675
01:53:11,690 --> 01:53:13,560
- The finish line is visible, right?
- Right?

2676
01:53:13,560 --> 01:53:14,690
How's the view?

2677
01:53:15,530 --> 01:53:17,760
Shin Seung Yong, booster activated.

2678
01:53:17,760 --> 01:53:19,700
You will start two spaces ahead.

2679
01:53:19,700 --> 01:53:21,670
One space right.

2680
01:53:21,870 --> 01:53:24,200
- Gosh.
- You've collided with the wall.

2681
01:53:24,640 --> 01:53:27,840
Your race car has flipped over,
and you cannot move until the next round.

2682
01:53:28,040 --> 01:53:29,540
Come on. Why didn't you save me?

2683
01:53:30,540 --> 01:53:32,780
Jeong Keun Woo, two spaces backward.

2684
01:53:33,010 --> 01:53:35,810
It was hard getting there,
but I'm back to where I was before.

2685
01:53:36,050 --> 01:53:38,750
Kang Ji Hoo, three spaces forward.

2686
01:53:38,750 --> 01:53:40,320
(Kang Ji Hoo: Predicted 2nd)

2687
01:53:40,320 --> 01:53:41,750
He's turning with Hye Seon.

2688
01:53:41,950 --> 01:53:44,520
- Congratulations.
- The youngsters are fast.

2689
01:53:45,560 --> 01:53:47,330
All players have completed their moves.

2690
01:53:47,330 --> 01:53:48,660
(Round 11 Movement Results)

2691
01:53:48,660 --> 01:53:50,530
(Player, predicted rank:)

2692
01:53:50,530 --> 01:53:52,560
(1. Choi Hye Seon, 2. Kang Ji Hoo,
3. Heo Seong Beom, 4. Shin Seung Yong,)

2693
01:53:52,560 --> 01:53:54,900
(5. YunB, 6. Hong Jin Ho,
7. Hyun Sung Joo, 8. Jeong Keun Woo)

2694
01:53:55,870 --> 01:53:57,540
Can you wake me up when you move your car?

2695
01:53:59,700 --> 01:54:00,910
I think...

2696
01:54:01,110 --> 01:54:03,980
Hye Seon is indeed first
in the predicted rank.

2697
01:54:04,610 --> 01:54:05,680
She's in the top ranks.

2698
01:54:05,680 --> 01:54:09,180
Their plan is to make it possible
to end the game...

2699
01:54:09,180 --> 01:54:10,520
whenever possible.

2700
01:54:11,380 --> 01:54:13,650
Round 12 will begin now.

2701
01:54:13,650 --> 01:54:14,990
(Round 12, Seong Beom)

2702
01:54:14,990 --> 01:54:18,120
We're first in the upcoming turn
and the next one.

2703
01:54:18,120 --> 01:54:20,120
I'm in a good position to pull ahead.

2704
01:54:20,120 --> 01:54:22,560
(Team P3 Alliance
goes 1st twice in a row.)

2705
01:54:22,560 --> 01:54:24,600
(Heo Seong Beom,
Hong Jin Ho, Choi Hye Seon)

2706
01:54:24,800 --> 01:54:28,230
I'm thinking of betting with 3 and 3...

2707
01:54:28,230 --> 01:54:30,270
- I see.
- or 4 and 2.

2708
01:54:31,000 --> 01:54:33,140
- If we bet 4 and 2...
- It overlaps with 3 and 3.

2709
01:54:33,140 --> 01:54:35,040
Right? But Three does move first.

2710
01:54:35,540 --> 01:54:37,580
- You're right.
- It does.

2711
01:54:37,580 --> 01:54:40,280
Seung Yong from the other team can't move.

2712
01:54:41,250 --> 01:54:42,510
But Ji Hoo can move.

2713
01:54:42,610 --> 01:54:43,780
Even YunB...

2714
01:54:44,120 --> 01:54:46,550
can't move
because of the One on the right.

2715
01:54:46,550 --> 01:54:48,490
Only Ji Hoo can move.

2716
01:54:48,490 --> 01:54:50,860
But even if he does move,
Ji Hoo can't attack us.

2717
01:54:50,860 --> 01:54:52,460
I doubt everyone will choose both areas.

2718
01:54:53,020 --> 01:54:55,160
I'm going to discard the card this time.

2719
01:54:56,560 --> 01:54:58,330
Where will you discard it to?

2720
01:54:59,830 --> 01:55:01,170
Area B.

2721
01:55:01,700 --> 01:55:02,930
Then I'll discard it...

2722
01:55:04,240 --> 01:55:05,300
in Area A.

2723
01:55:05,870 --> 01:55:06,970
- You?
- Yes.

2724
01:55:07,270 --> 01:55:08,370
Got it.

2725
01:55:08,770 --> 01:55:14,110
(As Jin Ho predicted,
Ji Hoo and Seung Yong bet with low cards.)

2726
01:55:18,280 --> 01:55:19,420
Right now...

2727
01:55:19,880 --> 01:55:21,220
The best case is...

2728
01:55:21,720 --> 01:55:24,390
If I were to win Area D and place Three,

2729
01:55:24,390 --> 01:55:27,130
I'll be in front of you,
and you'll get the booster.

2730
01:55:27,330 --> 01:55:28,360
Right.

2731
01:55:29,590 --> 01:55:33,260
(YunB makes a safe bet on Area D.)

2732
01:55:33,600 --> 01:55:35,400
You just want to stay there, don't you?

2733
01:55:35,700 --> 01:55:37,540
- No.
- No? Do you want to move?

2734
01:55:37,540 --> 01:55:39,140
- Of course.
- Is that so?

2735
01:55:39,700 --> 01:55:41,840
Why wouldn't I move when I've got a car?

2736
01:55:43,110 --> 01:55:45,380
I felt pretty guilty.

2737
01:55:45,840 --> 01:55:46,980
I have to go slow.

2738
01:55:47,380 --> 01:55:49,550
(Keun Woo bets on Area D.)

2739
01:55:49,550 --> 01:55:52,080
(Sung Joo also bets on Area D.)

2740
01:55:52,320 --> 01:55:55,450
What I can't decide on is how much to bet.

2741
01:55:56,190 --> 01:55:58,660
I think it's best to secure good cards...

2742
01:55:58,660 --> 01:56:00,430
when we're the first to play.

2743
01:56:00,430 --> 01:56:02,630
Using Five seems like a good idea.

2744
01:56:03,090 --> 01:56:05,600
We deliberately set up
three consecutive turns...

2745
01:56:05,600 --> 01:56:08,670
because we wanted to make big bets
when we had the first move...

2746
01:56:08,900 --> 01:56:11,570
and win the big cards.

2747
01:56:11,770 --> 01:56:13,770
We could use the cards we wanted...

2748
01:56:13,770 --> 01:56:16,470
and block the other teams
from playing whatever they've planned.

2749
01:56:19,740 --> 01:56:21,010
Ta-da.

2750
01:56:21,010 --> 01:56:24,120
Choi Hye Seon.
You've placed Card Five in Area A.

2751
01:56:26,120 --> 01:56:29,550
Hong Jin Ho.
You've placed Card Four in Area C.

2752
01:56:29,890 --> 01:56:31,420
Why did you only use Card One?

2753
01:56:31,420 --> 01:56:33,260
This is a throwaway round.

2754
01:56:33,520 --> 01:56:34,530
What?

2755
01:56:35,730 --> 01:56:36,990
The later rounds are more important,

2756
01:56:37,230 --> 01:56:39,160
and Team P3 Alliance's turn
is about to start.

2757
01:56:39,300 --> 01:56:41,730
We don't have any aggressive moves to make
at the moment.

2758
01:56:42,370 --> 01:56:43,370
I don't think...

2759
01:56:44,200 --> 01:56:45,800
it's a good idea
to just throw it away whole.

2760
01:56:45,800 --> 01:56:47,740
Only one player should make the sacrifice.

2761
01:56:48,240 --> 01:56:49,970
If the other team wins all three,

2762
01:56:50,680 --> 01:56:52,880
we can't catch up to them anymore.

2763
01:56:53,640 --> 01:56:55,410
All players have placed their bets.

2764
01:56:55,410 --> 01:56:57,010
(Round 12: Betting Ends)

2765
01:56:57,220 --> 01:56:59,220
I will announce the betting results.

2766
01:56:59,220 --> 01:57:00,280
(Round 12 Betting Results)

2767
01:57:00,280 --> 01:57:01,320
(A: Choi Hye Seon, Kang Ji Hoo,
B: Shin Seung Yong, C: Hong Jin Ho,)

2768
01:57:01,320 --> 01:57:02,390
(D: YunB, Jeong Keun Woo, Hyun Sung Joo)

2769
01:57:02,450 --> 01:57:05,320
Area A goes to Choi Hye Seon.

2770
01:57:05,360 --> 01:57:06,360
Good for you.

2771
01:57:06,860 --> 01:57:07,960
Area B...

2772
01:57:09,360 --> 01:57:11,800
goes to Shin Seung Yong.

2773
01:57:12,700 --> 01:57:14,330
What about me?

2774
01:57:15,270 --> 01:57:16,370
What about me?

2775
01:57:17,030 --> 01:57:20,270
(Team P3 Alliance
focused on Areas A and C.)

2776
01:57:20,410 --> 01:57:21,540
How about we...

2777
01:57:22,370 --> 01:57:23,780
We need to go with Plan B.

2778
01:57:23,780 --> 01:57:27,480
(A backup bet in Area A
that was considered more important)

2779
01:57:27,480 --> 01:57:29,680
You've placed Card Two in Area A.

2780
01:57:30,950 --> 01:57:32,120
(Thanks to it,
Seung Yong won Area B with Card 1.)

2781
01:57:32,120 --> 01:57:33,250
Thank you.

2782
01:57:34,120 --> 01:57:36,950
Area C goes to Hong Jin Ho.

2783
01:57:37,860 --> 01:57:38,890
Area D...

2784
01:57:41,860 --> 01:57:44,230
- goes to Jeong Keun Woo.
- What?

2785
01:57:44,400 --> 01:57:45,700
Seriously?

2786
01:57:46,060 --> 01:57:47,370
Isn't this scripted?

2787
01:57:48,130 --> 01:57:49,270
Are you sure this isn't scripted?

2788
01:57:49,270 --> 01:57:51,070
How did things turn out like this?

2789
01:57:51,070 --> 01:57:52,770
He's a genius.

2790
01:57:53,200 --> 01:57:55,840
I'm now tired of hearing
that I won an area.

2791
01:57:55,840 --> 01:57:57,540
And I knew I'd win it.

2792
01:57:57,710 --> 01:58:00,750
I interacted with Keun Woo
a handful of times.

2793
01:58:00,850 --> 01:58:02,280
He should go to Kangwon Land.

2794
01:58:02,550 --> 01:58:04,420
- Goodness, you...
- This is wild.

2795
01:58:04,420 --> 01:58:05,920
- Gosh.
- How is this possible?

2796
01:58:05,920 --> 01:58:07,390
Keun Woo has the highest winning rate.

2797
01:58:07,390 --> 01:58:08,390
(YunB fails every bet he's in
against Keun Woo.)

2798
01:58:08,720 --> 01:58:12,120
Seong Beom should get...

2799
01:58:12,460 --> 01:58:15,190
(Heo Seong Beom: 2)

2800
01:58:15,760 --> 01:58:17,030
One first.

2801
01:58:17,530 --> 01:58:19,200
- I'm going to crush him.
- From over there...

2802
01:58:19,700 --> 01:58:22,330
- Get on top of mine.
- Ji Hoo can't move.

2803
01:58:23,800 --> 01:58:25,470
This feels right for Ji Hoo.

2804
01:58:25,770 --> 01:58:26,840
Like so.

2805
01:58:26,900 --> 01:58:28,240
Is it better to go right or left?

2806
01:58:28,240 --> 01:58:29,770
- Right.
- Weren't you taking the inside line?

2807
01:58:29,810 --> 01:58:32,410
Why left when he's already Two?

2808
01:58:32,410 --> 01:58:33,950
- Do you want to flip over?
- Right.

2809
01:58:33,950 --> 01:58:36,180
Flipping over seems riskier.

2810
01:58:36,750 --> 01:58:39,380
(Hong Jin Ho: 4)

2811
01:58:39,980 --> 01:58:42,020
Choi Hye Seon, please place your cards.

2812
01:58:43,020 --> 01:58:44,160
Give me Three.

2813
01:58:44,160 --> 01:58:45,790
(Hong Jin Ho: 3, 4)

2814
01:58:45,790 --> 01:58:47,790
(Heo Seong Beom: 2, 1)

2815
01:58:48,330 --> 01:58:50,360
- Who needs Three?
- Sung Joo.

2816
01:58:51,460 --> 01:58:52,530
Would you like it?

2817
01:58:53,330 --> 01:58:54,370
Sung Joo wants it.

2818
01:58:54,700 --> 01:58:57,070
He won't say it with confidence.
All he's doing is nodding.

2819
01:58:58,200 --> 01:58:59,500
Or should I move farther?

2820
01:58:59,500 --> 01:59:01,070
No. They'll probably use reverse.

2821
01:59:01,540 --> 01:59:03,470
- Right.
- No, that's bad.

2822
01:59:04,710 --> 01:59:06,040
Do you need it, Sung Joo?

2823
01:59:06,040 --> 01:59:07,110
Do as you'd like.

2824
01:59:08,610 --> 01:59:10,880
- He doesn't need it.
- Choi Hye Seon has discarded a card.

2825
01:59:11,180 --> 01:59:12,780
Should I save your Zero?

2826
01:59:12,780 --> 01:59:13,850
That'd be great.

2827
01:59:14,550 --> 01:59:16,350
You should give YunB 2 and me 1.

2828
01:59:17,150 --> 01:59:19,820
It's the same for me either way
because Seong Beom will crush me.

2829
01:59:19,820 --> 01:59:20,860
(His car will be crushed by Seong Beom's.)

2830
01:59:21,090 --> 01:59:22,860
(Choi Hye Seon: Reverse)

2831
01:59:22,860 --> 01:59:24,230
- Two. Like this?
- Yes.

2832
01:59:24,230 --> 01:59:26,330
(Kang Ji Hoo: 1)

2833
01:59:26,630 --> 01:59:28,530
Hye Seon's car is going to go backward.

2834
01:59:29,430 --> 01:59:31,070
I expected it. It's not even a surprise.

2835
01:59:32,070 --> 01:59:33,700
- They're really coming after her.
- Jeong Keun Woo,

2836
01:59:33,700 --> 01:59:35,170
please place your cards.

2837
01:59:35,470 --> 01:59:37,140
- Where...
- Let's see.

2838
01:59:39,310 --> 01:59:40,980
(Jeong Keun Woo: 1, 2)

2839
01:59:43,510 --> 01:59:45,720
- Jeong Keun Woo has discarded a card.
- He's a tough man.

2840
01:59:47,320 --> 01:59:48,620
He's a real tough man.

2841
01:59:48,620 --> 01:59:50,190
(Round 12)

2842
01:59:50,190 --> 01:59:54,860
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,
and Jin Ho can move.)

2843
01:59:56,160 --> 01:59:59,330
I think Keun Woo is in last place.
That's my guess.

2844
01:59:59,330 --> 02:00:02,100
Right? There's no reason
why he wouldn't use three.

2845
02:00:02,570 --> 02:00:03,900
Seeing how he didn't use just three...

2846
02:00:05,640 --> 02:00:07,910
The race cars will start moving now.

2847
02:00:08,310 --> 02:00:10,240
Seong Beom, one space forward...

2848
02:00:10,240 --> 02:00:12,180
and one space left.

2849
02:00:12,180 --> 02:00:13,280
(Heo Seong Beom)

2850
02:00:13,540 --> 02:00:15,610
You've collided with Ji Hoo's race car.

2851
02:00:15,610 --> 02:00:16,680
Crash.

2852
02:00:17,150 --> 02:00:18,880
Sorry, Ji Hoo.

2853
02:00:18,880 --> 02:00:22,420
(Round 12)

2854
02:00:22,420 --> 02:00:24,290
Jin Ho, three spaces forward...

2855
02:00:24,290 --> 02:00:26,120
and one space right.

2856
02:00:26,290 --> 02:00:27,660
Gosh, he's going far.

2857
02:00:27,790 --> 02:00:29,060
Get ready to collide.

2858
02:00:29,630 --> 02:00:30,800
Three layers for three people.

2859
02:00:31,460 --> 02:00:32,600
I'm the head.

2860
02:00:32,600 --> 02:00:34,570
Keun Woo, one space forward...

2861
02:00:34,570 --> 02:00:36,400
and one space right.

2862
02:00:37,400 --> 02:00:40,400
Ji Hoo, you cannot move.

2863
02:00:40,810 --> 02:00:42,970
YunB, booster activated.

2864
02:00:42,970 --> 02:00:44,910
You will start two spaces ahead.

2865
02:00:45,040 --> 02:00:47,980
One space forward and one space left.

2866
02:00:48,650 --> 02:00:49,810
They're going together.

2867
02:00:49,810 --> 02:00:51,220
- There you go.
- He's right behind me.

2868
02:00:51,650 --> 02:00:54,450
Seung Yong, your car can move now.

2869
02:00:54,450 --> 02:00:55,490
Yes!

2870
02:00:56,220 --> 02:00:57,590
(Round 12 Movement Results)

2871
02:00:57,590 --> 02:01:00,360
(Player, predicted rank:
1. Choi Hye Seon, 2. Heo Seong Beom,)

2872
02:01:00,360 --> 02:01:03,190
(3. Kang Ji Hoo, 4. YunB,
5. Hong Jin Ho, 6. Shin Seung Yong,)

2873
02:01:03,190 --> 02:01:05,430
(7. Hyun Sung Joo, 8. Jeong Keun Woo)

2874
02:01:05,660 --> 02:01:08,000
Round 13 will begin now.

2875
02:01:08,600 --> 02:01:11,140
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

2876
02:01:12,240 --> 02:01:13,770
(Round 13, Jin Ho)

2877
02:01:13,770 --> 02:01:15,110
(Keun Woo, Ji Hoo, YunB, Seong Beom,)

2878
02:01:15,110 --> 02:01:16,610
(Jin Ho, Hye Seon, Sung Joo, Seung Yong)

2879
02:01:17,340 --> 02:01:18,910
Others will reverse other than me
in this round.

2880
02:01:18,910 --> 02:01:20,010
Two will reverse.

2881
02:01:20,010 --> 02:01:21,350
(Choi Hye Seon, Reverse)

2882
02:01:28,120 --> 02:01:33,020
(Heading straight to the Voting Room)

2883
02:01:40,800 --> 02:01:41,930
Keun Woo.

2884
02:01:42,230 --> 02:01:44,400
Place your card
in the area of your choice.

2885
02:01:44,940 --> 02:01:47,610
You've placed Card Three in Area D.

2886
02:01:54,050 --> 02:01:55,250
- You're done already?
- Yes.

2887
02:01:55,950 --> 02:01:58,520
We're all being dragged by him.

2888
02:01:59,180 --> 02:02:00,720
He's taking everything.

2889
02:02:02,250 --> 02:02:03,850
All players have placed their bets.

2890
02:02:04,320 --> 02:02:06,460
I will announce the betting results.

2891
02:02:07,560 --> 02:02:09,260
Area A goes to Hong Jin Ho.

2892
02:02:09,260 --> 02:02:10,630
(Area A goes to Hong Jin Ho.)

2893
02:02:10,630 --> 02:02:12,360
Area B goes to Kang Ji Hoo.

2894
02:02:12,360 --> 02:02:13,830
(Area B goes to Kang Ji Hoo.)

2895
02:02:14,400 --> 02:02:16,270
Area C goes to Shin Seung Yong.

2896
02:02:16,270 --> 02:02:17,640
(Area C goes to Shin Seung Yong.)

2897
02:02:18,140 --> 02:02:21,310
Area D goes to Jeong Keun Woo.

2898
02:02:22,770 --> 02:02:24,940
Stop letting me take the areas.

2899
02:02:24,940 --> 02:02:28,180
You guys... Aren't you going to keep up?

2900
02:02:29,310 --> 02:02:30,410
- Hey.
- Gosh, I placed my bet too.

2901
02:02:30,450 --> 02:02:32,750
You guys are funny.

2902
02:02:33,350 --> 02:02:36,350
(YunB lost the area to Keun Woo
five times already.)

2903
02:02:36,350 --> 02:02:37,990
(Round 12 Betting Results)

2904
02:02:37,990 --> 02:02:39,460
(A: Hong Jin Ho, Hyun Sung Joo,
B: Kang Ji Hoo, Heo Seong Beom)

2905
02:02:39,460 --> 02:02:40,860
(C: Shin Seung Yong, D: Jeong Keun Woo,
YunB, Choi Hye Seon)

2906
02:02:41,330 --> 02:02:43,730
You will now place your movement cards.

2907
02:02:43,730 --> 02:02:44,960
(Placing movement cards)

2908
02:02:44,960 --> 02:02:47,100
Hong Jin Ho, please place your cards.

2909
02:02:48,200 --> 02:02:50,970
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2910
02:02:51,400 --> 02:02:54,370
(Hong Jin Ho)

2911
02:02:54,370 --> 02:02:56,340
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2912
02:02:56,340 --> 02:02:57,510
Seung Yong, I helped you.

2913
02:02:57,780 --> 02:02:59,280
You want my car to flip over again?

2914
02:02:59,280 --> 02:03:01,950
No, I helped you to go far.

2915
02:03:02,950 --> 02:03:03,950
You're so mean.

2916
02:03:03,950 --> 02:03:04,950
- Darn.
- Shin Seung Yong,

2917
02:03:04,950 --> 02:03:06,350
please place your cards.

2918
02:03:06,350 --> 02:03:08,320
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2919
02:03:08,320 --> 02:03:09,490
(Sighing)

2920
02:03:09,490 --> 02:03:10,890
How will you use the reverse card?

2921
02:03:10,890 --> 02:03:12,590
I think you can use it on Seong Beom.

2922
02:03:12,590 --> 02:03:13,620
Right.

2923
02:03:13,690 --> 02:03:15,190
Stop sending me back!

2924
02:03:15,530 --> 02:03:17,390
That team got the reverse card well,

2925
02:03:17,530 --> 02:03:19,430
but they couldn't get the hang of it.

2926
02:03:19,660 --> 02:03:21,770
Why do they keep using
the reverse card on us?

2927
02:03:21,930 --> 02:03:23,270
After everything I went through
to get here.

2928
02:03:23,270 --> 02:03:24,970
I made it to second place
after going through a lot.

2929
02:03:26,340 --> 02:03:28,310
You have ten seconds left.

2930
02:03:29,670 --> 02:03:32,480
If I use it...
I'll use the reverse card on him.

2931
02:03:32,880 --> 02:03:35,280
I'll use either 3 or 4 on him.

2932
02:03:35,280 --> 02:03:36,410
Hurry, you're running out of time.

2933
02:03:36,650 --> 02:03:37,680
No, there.

2934
02:03:37,680 --> 02:03:38,780
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2935
02:03:38,780 --> 02:03:40,520
(Seong Beom, reverse)

2936
02:03:40,520 --> 02:03:41,650
Where should I use zero?

2937
02:03:42,750 --> 02:03:44,620
Your time is up.

2938
02:03:44,890 --> 02:03:46,520
The card will be discarded.

2939
02:03:48,690 --> 02:03:50,260
- Gosh, darn it.
- Let's see.

2940
02:03:51,400 --> 02:03:53,400
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2941
02:03:53,400 --> 02:03:55,400
Jeong Keun Woo, please place your cards.

2942
02:03:55,400 --> 02:03:56,770
(Round 13, Jin Ho, Seung Yong,
Keun Woo, Ji Hoo)

2943
02:03:56,770 --> 02:03:58,600
(Keun Woo, 2, 3)

2944
02:03:58,600 --> 02:04:00,970
(Hye Seon, 1)

2945
02:04:00,970 --> 02:04:04,180
(He's done placing his cards.)

2946
02:04:04,680 --> 02:04:07,910
(Keun Woo gave the lowest card, 1,
to Hye Seon.)

2947
02:04:08,510 --> 02:04:09,680
Thank you, Keun Woo.

2948
02:04:09,680 --> 02:04:11,650
- Why does he keep helping?
- Thank you.

2949
02:04:11,920 --> 02:04:13,180
I'm the most curious...

2950
02:04:13,520 --> 02:04:15,290
about the rank Keun Woo
predicted himself to win.

2951
02:04:15,290 --> 02:04:16,290
I know.

2952
02:04:16,290 --> 02:04:17,720
(Predicted 7th, currently 7th)

2953
02:04:17,990 --> 02:04:20,360
All the movement cards have been placed.

2954
02:04:20,690 --> 02:04:22,990
The race cars will start moving now.

2955
02:04:23,490 --> 02:04:25,360
Hong Jin Ho, one space forward...

2956
02:04:25,360 --> 02:04:27,230
and one space left.

2957
02:04:28,000 --> 02:04:29,000
Choi Hye Seon,

2958
02:04:29,000 --> 02:04:30,700
one space backward.

2959
02:04:30,700 --> 02:04:32,570
Shin Seung Yong, two spaces forward...

2960
02:04:32,570 --> 02:04:34,410
and two spaces left.

2961
02:04:34,540 --> 02:04:36,570
You've collided with YunB's race car.

2962
02:04:36,710 --> 02:04:37,810
They collided.

2963
02:04:37,810 --> 02:04:39,810
(Seung Yong and YunB's cars collided.)

2964
02:04:40,080 --> 02:04:42,010
Jeong Keun Woo, two spaces forward...

2965
02:04:42,010 --> 02:04:43,750
and one space right.

2966
02:04:43,750 --> 02:04:47,080
(Jeong Keun Woo is maintaining 7th place
that he predicted.)

2967
02:04:48,390 --> 02:04:50,690
Heo Seong Beom, three spaces backward.

2968
02:04:51,920 --> 02:04:53,520
(Heo Seong Beom, currently 6th place)

2969
02:04:53,520 --> 02:04:55,290
(Heo Seong Beom places 6th,
the rank he predicted.)

2970
02:04:55,290 --> 02:04:56,790
Do something about that.

2971
02:04:56,790 --> 02:04:58,460
(Heo Seong Beom places 6th,
the rank he predicted.)

2972
02:04:58,460 --> 02:05:00,230
All players have completed their moves.

2973
02:05:01,070 --> 02:05:02,300
(Round 13 Movement Results)

2974
02:05:02,300 --> 02:05:03,800
(Hye Seon, Jin Ho, Ji Hoo, Seung Yong,
YunB, Seong Beom, Keun Woo, Sung Joo)

2975
02:05:03,800 --> 02:05:05,870
Round 14 will begin now.

2976
02:05:07,500 --> 02:05:10,010
The movement cards
for each area are revealed.

2977
02:05:10,880 --> 02:05:12,340
(A: Shin Seung Yong, Hyun Sung Joo,
Jeong Keun Woo)

2978
02:05:12,340 --> 02:05:13,780
