and they each place 2nd and 3rd.)

3961
02:48:38,180 --> 02:48:41,320
"YunB and I will survive
if things end like this."

3962
02:48:41,620 --> 02:48:43,180
Fourth place, Shin Seung Yong.

3963
02:48:43,180 --> 02:48:44,290
(4th place:
Shin Seung Yong, Predicted 6th)

3964
02:48:44,320 --> 02:48:46,890
Fifth place, Hong Jin Ho.

3965
02:48:46,890 --> 02:48:48,390
(5th place: Hong Jin Ho, Predicted 1st)

3966
02:48:49,820 --> 02:48:51,090
Is there a place for the cards?

3967
02:48:53,900 --> 02:48:56,200
(The Seung Yong Alliance
didn't know Seong Beom's predicted rank.)

3968
02:48:56,200 --> 02:48:59,970
There was nothing I could do
in the final round.

3969
02:49:02,140 --> 02:49:05,240
(YunB ended up discarding
all three cards.)

3970
02:49:05,270 --> 02:49:07,910
He discarded all three of his cards.

3971
02:49:07,910 --> 02:49:09,410
(Seong Beom kept his predicted rank
after a tough game.)

3972
02:49:09,480 --> 02:49:11,850
"I did it."

3973
02:49:12,350 --> 02:49:14,120
If they figured it out...

3974
02:49:14,150 --> 02:49:16,680
and went against him,
Seong Beom would've placed fifth.

3975
02:49:16,920 --> 02:49:18,290
Fortunately, they didn't figure it out
until the end.

3976
02:49:18,820 --> 02:49:21,490
It was a big relief
to be able to keep Seong Beom.

3977
02:49:21,620 --> 02:49:22,890
It was the same with Hye Seon.

3978
02:49:23,590 --> 02:49:25,090
Sixth place, Heo Seong Beom.

3979
02:49:25,860 --> 02:49:27,260
Seventh place, Hyun Sung Joo.

3980
02:49:27,660 --> 02:49:29,500
Eighth place, Jeong Keun Woo.

3981
02:49:30,130 --> 02:49:33,300
You overrated yourself.

3982
02:49:33,300 --> 02:49:35,240
Soon, the prediction result
will be checked...

3983
02:49:35,240 --> 02:49:36,940
to announce the final result.

3984
02:49:39,670 --> 02:49:40,710
Gosh.

3985
02:49:41,940 --> 02:49:44,380
I will announce the semi-final results.

3986
02:49:45,180 --> 02:49:46,810
The players who will advance
to the finals...

3987
02:49:46,810 --> 02:49:48,880
after winning the semi-finals are...

3988
02:49:51,020 --> 02:49:52,050
Kang Ji Hoo,

3989
02:49:53,120 --> 02:49:54,190
YunB,

3990
02:49:55,390 --> 02:49:56,490
Heo Seong Beom,

3991
02:50:06,600 --> 02:50:07,970
and Hyun Sung Joo.

3992
02:50:07,970 --> 02:50:10,810
(Hyun Sung Joo)

3993
02:50:10,810 --> 02:50:11,840
Gosh.

3994
02:50:15,140 --> 02:50:17,050
- Nice one.
- Gosh.

3995
02:50:19,150 --> 02:50:22,150
Sung Joo, choose your predicted rank.

3996
02:50:22,980 --> 02:50:25,150
(Hyun Sung Joo: Predicted 7th)

3997
02:50:25,290 --> 02:50:27,620
Members of an alliance...

3998
02:50:27,620 --> 02:50:29,890
can pull or push each other.

3999
02:50:29,990 --> 02:50:32,290
I thought that each team would put
at least one person in the leading group.

4000
02:50:32,390 --> 02:50:35,360
Instead of going for 1st, 2nd, or 3rd,
I thought that 4th, 5th, 6th, or 7th...

4001
02:50:35,360 --> 02:50:37,530
was a better way to fish
in troubled waters.

4002
02:50:37,530 --> 02:50:40,540
I had to be a joker in the pack today.

4003
02:50:40,540 --> 02:50:43,100
That was why I went with seventh place
at the end of the race.

4004
02:50:43,840 --> 02:50:45,810
(Sung Joo's turn to place
the movement cards early in the race)

4005
02:50:45,810 --> 02:50:47,540
Even though my predicted rank was seventh,

4006
02:50:47,540 --> 02:50:50,110
I thought that it was important...

4007
02:50:50,110 --> 02:50:52,650
to make myself feel like
my predicted rank...

4008
02:50:52,650 --> 02:50:54,120
was in the leading group or the middle.

4009
02:50:55,050 --> 02:50:58,120
I kept showing the others that I wanted to
to move forward with my cards.

4010
02:50:58,320 --> 02:50:59,720
(Impressed)

4011
02:50:59,720 --> 02:51:00,960
Are you finally moving?

4012
02:51:01,090 --> 02:51:03,690
I wanted to show my eagerness
of wanting to move forward.

4013
02:51:03,790 --> 02:51:06,130
I discarded the cards
to show the others...

4014
02:51:06,130 --> 02:51:07,500
that I wanted to move forward on my own.

4015
02:51:07,630 --> 02:51:09,630
Keun Woo and I were the only ones
with no other teammates.

4016
02:51:09,630 --> 02:51:12,000
The one who kept quiet...

4017
02:51:12,000 --> 02:51:14,070
suddenly started talking to
Seong Beom and Jin Ho.

4018
02:51:16,770 --> 02:51:18,140
It felt like he predicted 6th or 7th.

4019
02:51:18,140 --> 02:51:20,780
I knew that it was a competition
between us.

4020
02:51:20,880 --> 02:51:22,510
The one who played the game on his own...

4021
02:51:22,510 --> 02:51:23,910
started to work with another team.

4022
02:51:23,910 --> 02:51:26,380
Instead of solving things on my own
with my cards,

4023
02:51:26,380 --> 02:51:28,320
I also started to look for help
due to anxiety.

4024
02:51:28,780 --> 02:51:30,050
Did you decide where to place your bet?

4025
02:51:30,850 --> 02:51:31,890
(He strategically approached YunB...)

4026
02:51:31,890 --> 02:51:33,920
(and Seung Yong.)

4027
02:51:33,920 --> 02:51:35,860
To place 7th and 6th,
we needed someone to be in 8th place.

4028
02:51:35,860 --> 02:51:38,560
To put Keun Woo in 8th place,

4029
02:51:38,560 --> 02:51:39,730
we decided to place
the reverse card on his gear board.

4030
02:51:39,960 --> 02:51:41,660
Then, I'll use this on Keun Woo.

4031
02:51:43,060 --> 02:51:48,440
(They placed the reverse card and 4
on Keun Woo's gear board.)

4032
02:51:48,440 --> 02:51:51,170
After placing the reverse card,
Seung Yong placed four.

4033
02:51:51,170 --> 02:51:52,840
That moved Keun Woo further back.

4034
02:51:52,970 --> 02:51:55,340
Keun Woo, four spaces backward.

4035
02:51:55,340 --> 02:51:56,480
Gosh, I'm last.

4036
02:51:58,150 --> 02:52:00,520
(Keun Woo ended up placing 8th.)

4037
02:52:01,020 --> 02:52:03,750
"Gosh, this worked. This actually worked."

4038
02:52:04,090 --> 02:52:05,920
(Prediction Race Results)

4039
02:52:05,920 --> 02:52:07,260
(Ji Hoo: Predicted 2nd, 2nd Place,
YunB: Predicted 3rd, 3rd place)

4040
02:52:07,260 --> 02:52:08,520
(Seong Beom: Predicted 6th, 6th place,
Sung Joo: Predicted 7th, 7th place)

4041
02:52:08,520 --> 02:52:09,760
(Hye Seon, Seung Yong, Jin Ho, Keun Woo
failed with their predictions.)

4042
02:52:11,890 --> 02:52:13,030
Choi Hye Seon,

4043
02:52:13,330 --> 02:52:14,360
Shin Seung Yong,

4044
02:52:14,760 --> 02:52:15,800
Hong Jin Ho,

4045
02:52:16,200 --> 02:52:17,230
and Jeong Keun Woo...

4046
02:52:17,500 --> 02:52:20,740
have been eliminated from Bloody Game X.

4047
02:52:21,170 --> 02:52:23,470
Please leave the main hall immediately.

4048
02:52:24,240 --> 02:52:26,640
- I'll get going! Good luck!
- Good luck!

4049
02:52:26,640 --> 02:52:27,680
Good luck, Seong Beom!

4050
02:52:27,680 --> 02:52:30,180
I am totally satisfied.

4051
02:52:30,340 --> 02:52:32,210
Jeong Keun Woo was able to
reach the semi-finals...

4052
02:52:32,210 --> 02:52:34,820
and make a beautiful departure.

4053
02:52:35,080 --> 02:52:36,550
I'm very grateful for that.

4054
02:52:36,620 --> 02:52:39,520
Hong Jin Ho, Xitsuh, and Lee Tae Gyun.

4055
02:52:39,690 --> 02:52:42,160
The plays we made as a four...

4056
02:52:42,160 --> 02:52:45,060
will become memories I will never forget.

4057
02:52:45,560 --> 02:52:49,630
I was invited again
after being in Season One.

4058
02:52:49,960 --> 02:52:51,600
Thank you so much...

4059
02:52:51,600 --> 02:52:53,940
for giving me the chance to redeem myself.

4060
02:52:54,070 --> 02:52:55,400
And as for myself,

4061
02:52:59,140 --> 02:53:01,140
I was able to reach...

4062
02:53:01,640 --> 02:53:04,610
the semi-finals.

4063
02:53:04,980 --> 02:53:08,080
Thank you so much
for making me feel confident...

4064
02:53:08,650 --> 02:53:11,620
about being able to reach
even further in the future.

4065
02:53:12,050 --> 02:53:14,090
- Become the champion.
- "Seventh place?"

4066
02:53:14,790 --> 02:53:15,990
Great job today.

4067
02:53:16,960 --> 02:53:18,030
Things didn't work out.

4068
02:53:18,230 --> 02:53:21,600
Getting eliminated
was quite disappointing.

4069
02:53:21,800 --> 02:53:25,270
I played many different games
before reaching the semi-finals.

4070
02:53:25,670 --> 02:53:28,800
I did my best to stay focused
for each game.

4071
02:53:28,940 --> 02:53:31,070
I can confidently say...

4072
02:53:31,140 --> 02:53:34,680
that I gave it my all for those games.

4073
02:53:34,940 --> 02:53:38,880
After going through three Deathmatches,

4074
02:53:38,880 --> 02:53:41,320
I learned about what type of person I was.

4075
02:53:41,450 --> 02:53:44,620
It was a great time to learn about myself.

4076
02:53:44,820 --> 02:53:46,590
Through Bloody Game,

4077
02:53:47,360 --> 02:53:49,760
I've learned a lot of things.

4078
02:53:50,090 --> 02:53:52,890
I've achieved my goal...

4079
02:53:52,890 --> 02:53:55,200
of wanting to reach the semi-finals,

4080
02:53:55,560 --> 02:53:56,630
so I feel happy about that.

4081
02:53:56,900 --> 02:54:00,200
I think I'll feel very proud
if Ji Hoo becomes the champion.

4082
02:54:00,500 --> 02:54:02,100
- Good luck!
- Good luck, Seong Beom!

4083
02:54:03,770 --> 02:54:05,510
- Good luck!
- Gosh.

4084
02:54:06,770 --> 02:54:10,280
It's disappointing,
but I don't feel any regret.

4085
02:54:10,580 --> 02:54:12,610
During the previous season,

4086
02:54:12,610 --> 02:54:16,250
I think I was very intimidated.

4087
02:54:16,250 --> 02:54:19,050
I lacked confidence and was intimidated.

4088
02:54:19,490 --> 02:54:20,760
For this season,

4089
02:54:20,760 --> 02:54:24,390
I had a lot more life experience.

4090
02:54:24,560 --> 02:54:27,090
I was a lot more active...

4091
02:54:27,400 --> 02:54:30,670
and showed a lot more development
than before.

4092
02:54:30,900 --> 02:54:33,730
I also enjoyed it a lot more.

4093
02:54:36,040 --> 02:54:38,140
Gosh, this is so sad!
I don't want to go home!

4094
02:54:41,140 --> 02:54:44,510
I'm able to go home
after an incredible experience.

4095
02:54:44,510 --> 02:54:46,050
Thank you so much.

4096
02:54:46,710 --> 02:54:48,080
We'll go home together.

4097
02:54:48,080 --> 02:54:50,380
- We've survived for a long time.
- Right.

4098
02:54:50,920 --> 02:54:54,220
Bloody Game X felt a lot more exciting.

4099
02:54:54,320 --> 02:54:55,920
There were many plays that I made...

4100
02:54:55,920 --> 02:54:57,590
for a team battle.

4101
02:54:57,730 --> 02:54:58,960
I felt a sense of comradeship
very quickly.

4102
02:54:59,130 --> 02:55:02,630
I've definitely felt the charms
of a team battle...

4103
02:55:03,000 --> 02:55:05,830
through my time here.

4104
02:55:06,100 --> 02:55:09,770
After going through
the Bloody Game series,

4105
02:55:10,000 --> 02:55:11,270
I've become a lot stronger.

4106
02:55:11,710 --> 02:55:13,210
It was tough every time...

4107
02:55:13,210 --> 02:55:14,840
and I hated being in the wild.

4108
02:55:15,980 --> 02:55:17,650
There were things that could
only be experienced in Bloody Game...

4109
02:55:17,650 --> 02:55:21,480
and there were things
I couldn't feel anywhere else.

4110
02:55:22,980 --> 02:55:24,020
I loved those moments.

4111
02:55:24,020 --> 02:55:26,990
Not being able to reach the final
is quite disappointing,

4112
02:55:27,590 --> 02:55:30,830
but as someone who has experienced
Bloody Games 2, 3, and X,

4113
02:55:31,260 --> 02:55:35,330
I've truly had a blast.

4114
02:55:35,630 --> 02:55:38,630
As I must think positively,
I'm glad that...

4115
02:55:38,630 --> 02:55:41,170
Seong Beom has advanced
as our representative.

4116
02:55:41,570 --> 02:55:44,140
I'm sure Seong Beom will go
and destroy them all.

4117
02:55:44,710 --> 02:55:45,840
- Great job.
- Gosh!

4118
02:55:46,240 --> 02:55:47,280
Gosh!

4119
02:55:47,280 --> 02:55:48,440
- Become the champion.
- Wasn't that the plan?

4120
02:55:48,710 --> 02:55:50,010
- Great work.
- Great work.

4121
02:55:52,280 --> 02:55:53,610
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

4122
02:55:53,610 --> 02:55:54,780
You've made it this far.

4123
02:55:54,780 --> 02:55:56,380
- Let's go!
- Thank you.

4124
02:55:57,250 --> 02:55:59,650
Ji Hoo! Good luck, Ji Hoo.

4125
02:56:00,320 --> 02:56:01,660
- Good luck!
- Thank you.

4126
02:56:01,660 --> 02:56:02,860
- Good luck!
- Smack their faces...

4127
02:56:02,860 --> 02:56:04,190
with your talent.

4128
02:56:05,560 --> 02:56:06,590
Good luck!

4129
02:56:09,460 --> 02:56:10,800
Seong Beom, give me a call
if the others harass you.

4130
02:56:10,800 --> 02:56:12,200
Thank you!

4131
02:56:13,630 --> 02:56:14,940
Thank you!

4132
02:56:15,440 --> 02:56:16,700
You'll still represent us.

4133
02:56:17,170 --> 02:56:19,040
It's the 1-on-1 match you love. Go for it.

4134
02:56:19,270 --> 02:56:20,410
- Bye!
- Finish them off!

4135
02:56:20,410 --> 02:56:21,680
- I'll get going now.
- Good luck!

4136
02:56:21,680 --> 02:56:23,110
- Bye!
- Good luck!

4137
02:56:23,110 --> 02:56:24,380
- Good luck!
- Bye!

4138
02:56:26,150 --> 02:56:27,780
(Bloody Game X eliminated players)

4139
02:56:27,780 --> 02:56:29,420
(Hong Jin Ho, Jeong Keun Woo,
Shin Seung Yong, Choi Hye Seon)

4140
02:56:29,420 --> 02:56:30,750
We've made it this far.

4141
02:56:31,490 --> 02:56:34,160
- Great work, everyone!
- Great work, everyone.

4142
02:56:34,160 --> 02:56:36,290
- Bye!
- Bye!

4143
02:56:48,840 --> 02:56:49,870
Will you be able to handle it?

4144
02:56:49,870 --> 02:56:51,470
Team C is full of jerks.

4145
02:56:51,470 --> 02:56:52,840
That's betraying Team C.

4146
02:56:52,840 --> 02:56:54,080
One must die.

4147
02:56:54,080 --> 02:56:55,110
Those wimps.

4148
02:56:58,350 --> 02:56:59,580
I will be cheap and dirty.

4149
02:56:59,580 --> 02:57:00,580
Gosh!

4150
02:57:01,750 --> 02:57:02,820
I did it.

4151
02:57:02,880 --> 02:57:03,880
Sang Min!

4152
02:57:03,880 --> 02:57:05,690
- Don't do that!
- Gosh, that hurts.

4153
02:57:06,050 --> 02:57:07,050
Quiet!

4154
02:57:07,890 --> 02:57:09,090
You did well. Don't blank out.

4155
02:57:09,690 --> 02:57:10,690
I hope I won't have to cry.

4156
02:57:10,690 --> 02:57:12,030
I want to kill them all.

4157
02:57:12,030 --> 02:57:13,130
I'm a petty criminal.

4158
02:57:14,260 --> 02:57:15,600
We should cut Seung Yong's throat.

4159
02:57:15,600 --> 02:57:17,060
What story are you on about?

4160
02:57:17,060 --> 02:57:18,200
It was coming.

4161
02:57:20,370 --> 02:57:21,470
I don't want any more piggyback rides.

4162
02:57:21,470 --> 02:57:23,600
Stop with that!

4163
02:57:23,600 --> 02:57:24,770
One space forward.

4164
02:57:29,480 --> 02:57:31,050
Reaching the final?

4165
02:57:31,380 --> 02:57:32,550
It feels quite all right.

4166
02:57:32,980 --> 02:57:34,220
Two of the unorthodox sect
from Bloody Game Two...

4167
02:57:34,220 --> 02:57:36,350
and two of the orthodox sect.

4168
02:57:36,980 --> 02:57:39,450
Flipping the tables
against everyone's expectations.

4169
02:57:39,820 --> 02:57:41,190
That is my strength.

4170
02:57:41,260 --> 02:57:43,590
I will take the bull by the horns.

4171
02:57:44,790 --> 02:57:46,190
I do believe I'm the underdog,

4172
02:57:46,460 --> 02:57:47,900
but I have a good chance of winning.

4173
02:57:48,930 --> 02:57:51,870
The ones who were known to be prodigies...

4174
02:57:52,300 --> 02:57:54,740
can get their pride hurt
by losing to someone like YunB or me.

4175
02:57:54,940 --> 02:57:56,300
We can compete with 120 percent
of what we have,

4176
02:57:56,300 --> 02:57:57,670
but they will feel this pressure.

4177
02:57:57,670 --> 02:57:59,910
As we have nothing to lose,

4178
02:57:59,970 --> 02:58:01,380
I think we will feel very comfortable
in the game.

4179
02:58:02,140 --> 02:58:04,280
I will do my best to become the champion.

4180
02:58:05,850 --> 02:58:08,580
I thought that I would reach the final
with my talent.

4181
02:58:08,650 --> 02:58:10,820
But many of the things I lacked...

4182
02:58:11,290 --> 02:58:12,690
were filled by the older ones.

4183
02:58:12,920 --> 02:58:15,860
I was able to reach the final
because of their sacrifice.

4184
02:58:15,960 --> 02:58:19,360
I will fight until the end
and become the champion.

4185
02:58:20,090 --> 02:58:22,600
It was the moment I've always dreamed of.

4186
02:58:22,600 --> 02:58:26,000
I've made it this far
with the sacrifice of the others.

4187
02:58:26,270 --> 02:58:29,270
I will put my life and beliefs
on the line...

4188
02:58:29,570 --> 02:58:31,170
and do my best in the final.

4189
02:58:34,310 --> 02:58:35,910
(Kang Ji Hoo)

4190
02:58:35,910 --> 02:58:37,450
(Hyun Sung Joo)

4191
02:58:37,450 --> 02:58:39,110
(Heo Seong Beom)

4192
02:58:39,110 --> 02:58:40,750
(YunB)

4193
02:58:40,950 --> 02:58:44,590
(Who will become the final winner
of Bloody Game X?)

4194
02:59:45,410 --> 02:59:47,410
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
